 responsive tab text size\n- assessments: flex-wrap safety banner on mobile","tree":{"sha":"1a35e8e8d023f6bf23f97b96e3880a22420e789e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/1a35e8e8d023f6bf23f97b96e3880a22420e789e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/3144572ccadd9cf74378cc23b6c8ddb15db539fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/3144572ccadd9cf74378cc23b6c8ddb15db539fd","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKDMxNDQ1NzJjY2FkZDljZjc0Mzc4Y2MyM2I2YzhkZGIxNWRiNTM5ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/23519d463823ce8741ea8d65e7ee10fa0639b300","sha":"23519d463823ce8741ea8d65e7ee10fa0639b300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/23519d463823ce8741ea8d65e7ee10fa0639b300"}],"sha":"3144572ccadd9cf74378cc23b6c8ddb15db539fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/3144572ccadd9cf74378cc23b6c8ddb15db539fd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/ebc0fda8529f5bbdf9825593742c5f5df2498310/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T21:21:18Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T21:21:18Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"message":"docs: guide for creating new 3D avatar personas\n\nStep-by-step runbook covering the full flow: Avaturn dev project setup,\nthe T1-vs-T2 trap, using the avaturn-exporter helper, verifying the GLB,\nwiring PERSONAS + i18n + new voices, plus a troubleshooting catalogue\nfor the common failure modes (blend-shapes-not-found, empty thumbnails,\nhunched shoulders, voice/gender mismatch).","tree":{"sha":"2404fcfc9001ce11354eacdd484ae55e648a8d35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/2404fcfc9001ce11354eacdd484ae55e648a8d35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/ebc0fda8529f5bbdf9825593742c5f5df2498310","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/ebc0fda8529f5bbdf9825593742c5f5df2498310","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKGViYzBmZGE4NTI5ZjViYmRmOTgyNTU5Mzc0MmM1ZjVkZjI0OTgzMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/eb7f0124b8b168819b49b6327641c93c207b1f68","sha":"eb7f0124b8b168819b49b6327641c93c207b1f68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/eb7f0124b8b168819b49b6327641c93c207b1f68"}],"sha":"ebc0fda8529f5bbdf9825593742c5f5df2498310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/ebc0fda8529f5bbdf9825593742c5f5df2498310"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135621823?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anatoli-derese","id":135621823,"login":"anatoli-derese","node_id":"U_kgDOCBVsvw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anatoli-derese","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/23519d463823ce8741ea8d65e7ee10fa0639b300/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T21:17:15Z","email":"135621823+anatoli-derese@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anatoli Derese"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T21:17:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #47 from Teklez/feat/add-multiple-avatars-and-thumbnails\n\nTurns the single-RPM placeholder picker into a multi-persona experience                                                                                                                                                                         \n  and gets the Gemini API key off the client.                                                                                                                                                                                                     \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  Personas                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n  - Wire four Avaturn T2 GLBs (Dawit, Bereket, Ashenafi, Bedru) into the\n    picker. Plumb a per-rig retarget through showAvatar so the Avaturn                                                                                                                                                                            \n    skeleton sits naturally (shoulders, spine, head, slight eye baseline).                                                                                                                                                                        \n  - Rename Henok → Bereket in en/am; add Ashenafi and Bedru localisations.                                                                                                                                                                        \n  - Sora and Kai become Coming Soon (url: null disables click + play) and                                                                                                                                                                         \n    sort to the bottom so real personas surface first.                                                                                                                                                                                            \n                                                                  \n  Picker previews                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \n  - New AvatarThumbnail: briefly mounts a live three.js render to capture\n    each persona''s head as a PNG, caches it in localStorage, and serves                                                                                                                                                                           \n    instantly thereafter. Renders are serialized through a module-level\n    queue so cards don''t fight for GPU contexts on slower devices. Works                                                                                                                                                                          \n    around three.js''s default preserveDrawingBuffer=false by forcing a\n    fresh render right before toDataURL in the same sync tick.                                                                                                                                                                                    \n  - New MiniHead: mounts on play, fades in over the resting thumbnail,\n    lipsyncs the persona''s intro with TalkingHead''s English engine, and                                                                                                                                                                           \n    unmounts on stop / playback end / picker unmount. Resumes the audio                                                                                                                                                                           \n    context inside the user-gesture-initiated effect to satisfy Chrome''s                                                                                                                                                                          \n    autoplay policy.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n  - TTS audio cached per (avatar, locale) so a locale switch doesn''t\n    replay an English intro under the Amharic UI; hover/focus warms the                                                                                                                                                                           \n    fetch so click → audio is instant.                                                                                                                                                                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  Backend-proxied TTS                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n  - New POST /api/v1/voice/tts authenticated endpoint that calls Gemini                                                                                                                                                                           \n    server-side and returns base64 PCM + sample rate. Voice whitelist,\n    bounded text length, 400/502/503 on bad input / upstream / missing                                                                                                                                                                            \n    key. Frontend fetchTTS now goes through apiRequest, inheriting auth,                                                                                                                                                                          \n    401 redirect, and timeout behavior.                                                                                                                                                                                                           \n  - NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY is no longer required by the frontend.                                                                                                                                                                             \n  - New Gemini voices added to the voice list: Orus (Ashenafi), Zephyr,                                                                                                                                                                           \n    Algenib (Bedru — Zephyr reads feminine).                                                                                                                                                                                                      \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  Tooling / docs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  - avaturn-exporter.html helper for generating more T2 GLBs from the\n    Avaturn developer SDK.                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n  - Research note in thoughts/shared documenting the RPM-shutdown →\n    Avaturn migration and the rig calibration process.","tree":{"sha":"f999ba5aa048f54064caea3be4c32507ab2515b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/f999ba5aa048f54064caea3be4c32507ab2515b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/23519d463823ce8741ea8d65e7ee10fa0639b300","verification":{"payload":"tree f999ba5aa048f54064caea3be4c32507ab2515b5\nparent 4345851b5d4727432e16b7aa269fc36f415246c5\nparent eb7f0124b8b168819b49b6327641c93c207b1f68\nauthor Anatoli Derese <135621823+anatoli-derese@users.noreply.github.com> 1779830235 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779830235 +0300\n\nMerge pull request #47 from Teklez/feat/add-multiple-avatars-and-thumbnails\n\nTurns the single-RPM placeholder picker into a multi-persona experience                                                                                                                                                                         \n  and gets the Gemini API key off the client.                                                                                                                                                                                                     \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  Personas                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n  - Wire four Avaturn T2 GLBs (Dawit, Bereket, Ashenafi, Bedru) into the\n    picker. Plumb a per-rig retarget through showAvatar so the Avaturn                                                                                                                                                                            \n    skeleton sits naturally (shoulders, spine, head, slight eye baseline).                                                                                                                                                                        \n  - Rename Henok → Bereket in en/am; add Ashenafi and Bedru localisations.                                                                                                                                                                        \n  - Sora and Kai become Coming Soon (url: null disables click + play) and                                                                                                                                                                         \n    sort to the bottom so real personas surface first.                                                                                                                                                                                            \n                                                                  \n  Picker previews                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \n  - New AvatarThumbnail: briefly mounts a live three.js render to capture\n    each persona''s head as a PNG, caches it in localStorage, and serves                                                                                                                                                                           \n    instantly thereafter. Renders are serialized through a module-level\n    queue so cards don''t fight for GPU contexts on slower devices. Works                                                                                                                                                                          \n    around three.js''s default preserveDrawingBuffer=false by forcing a\n    fresh render right before toDataURL in the same sync tick.                                                                                                                                                                                    \n  - New MiniHead: mounts on play, fades in over the resting thumbnail,\n    lipsyncs the persona''s intro with TalkingHead''s English engine, and                                                                                                                                                                           \n    unmounts on stop / playback end / picker unmount. Resumes the audio                                                                                                                                                                           \n    context inside the user-gesture-initiated effect to satisfy Chrome''s                                                                                                                                                                          \n    autoplay policy.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n  - TTS audio cached per (avatar, locale) so a locale switch doesn''t\n    replay an English intro under the Amharic UI; hover/focus warms the                                                                                                                                                                           \n    fetch so click → audio is instant.                                                                                                                                                                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  Backend-proxied TTS                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n  - New POST /api/v1/voice/tts authenticated endpoint that calls Gemini                                                                                                                                                                           \n    server-side and returns base64 PCM + sample rate. Voice whitelist,\n    bounded text length, 400/502/503 on bad input / upstream / missing                                                                                                                                                                            \n    key. Frontend fetchTTS now goes through apiRequest, inheriting auth,                                                                                                                                                                          \n    401 redirect, and timeout behavior.                                                                                                                                                                                                           \n  - NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY is no longer required by the frontend.                                                                                                                                                                             \n  - New Gemini voices added to the voice list: Orus (Ashenafi), Zephyr,                                                                                                                                                                           \n    Algenib (Bedru — Zephyr reads feminine).                                                                                                                                                                                                      \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  Tooling / docs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n  - avaturn-exporter.html helper for generating more T2 GLBs from the\n    Avaturn developer SDK.                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n  - Research note in thoughts/shared documenting the RPM-shutdown →\n    Avaturn migration and the rig calibration process.                                                                                                                                                                                            \n                                                                                                                             