:false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/0ceacb1ce42a4023d4b051807192aab61ac253c1","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKDBjZWFjYjFjZTQyYTQwMjNkNGIwNTE4MDcxOTJhYWI2MWFjMjUzYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/7ef55d18d02919c4998c08e036d5d2db501343db","sha":"7ef55d18d02919c4998c08e036d5d2db501343db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/7ef55d18d02919c4998c08e036d5d2db501343db"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/b50423cc1b67e3c790c6a0199175283dfd5a9a06","sha":"b50423cc1b67e3c790c6a0199175283dfd5a9a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/b50423cc1b67e3c790c6a0199175283dfd5a9a06"}],"sha":"0ceacb1ce42a4023d4b051807192aab61ac253c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/0ceacb1ce42a4023d4b051807192aab61ac253c1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/b50423cc1b67e3c790c6a0199175283dfd5a9a06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T12:50:56Z","email":"shadow@Zemenus-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Zemenu Mekuria"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T12:50:56Z","email":"shadow@Zemenus-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Zemenu Mekuria"},"message":"feat(assessments): redesign listing, take flow, result, and crisis interstitial\n\nListing now opens with an editorial header (stats row + safety banner)\nand three-up cards tinted per instrument family (sage/PHQ-9, honey/GAD-7,\ndawn/PSS), each surfacing the last-taken score with a severity pill in\nthe unified 5-point gentle scale (moss → sage-honey → sand → warm clay\n→ clay). The history grid pairs a 12-row recent list with stacked trend\ncards that compute direction (↘/→/↗) from linear regression and render\nhand-rolled SVG mini-charts colored by the latest severity.\n\nTake flow gains a sticky top progress bar with a \"Saved\" indicator that\nappears once any response is logged, plus a sticky footer with keyboard\nhints. Question body uses a serif headline + per-instrument preamble +\nnumbered option pills (`1..N` selects, `Enter` advances, `Escape` saves\nand exits).\n\nResult page is now a two-column layout: score ring + severity scale\ngradient + range pill on the left; recharts trend chart with 90D/6M/1Y/\nAll toggle + suggested-next-steps list + safety card (only at level ≥ 3\nor crisis_detected) on the right. Bottom strip exposes PDF / Share\n(stubbed) and a \"Retake in 2 weeks\" action that writes a localStorage\nreminder.\n\nCrisis interstitial moves to clay tone (not red — \"we''re paying\nattention,\" not \"you''re broken\"), pulls locale-aware resources via\ngetCrisisResources, and offers both \"Continue check-in\" and \"I''ll come\nback later\" as equally valid paths. The Q9 response is logged before\nthe screen renders so the safety-team feedback loop has data either\nway.\n\nAdds lib/assessment-level.ts (level → unified scale index, instrument\ncodes, tones) and lib/crisis-resources.ts (locale-aware crisis list).","tree":{"sha":"b72488b3c9c91cfd06f59972d8afd2155da591ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/b72488b3c9c91cfd06f59972d8afd2155da591ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/b50423cc1b67e3c790c6a0199175283dfd5a9a06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/b50423cc1b67e3c790c6a0199175283dfd5a9a06","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKGI1MDQyM2NjMWI2N2UzYzc5MGM2YTAxOTkxNzUyODNkZmQ1YTlhMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/5775e5dddbd6c1385388f7ac55050d14d5c93f82","sha":"5775e5dddbd6c1385388f7ac55050d14d5c93f82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/5775e5dddbd6c1385388f7ac55050d14d5c93f82"}],"sha":"b50423cc1b67e3c790c6a0199175283dfd5a9a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/b50423cc1b67e3c790c6a0199175283dfd5a9a06"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/5775e5dddbd6c1385388f7ac55050d14d5c93f82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T12:50:21Z","email":"shadow@Zemenus-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Zemenu Mekuria"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T12:50:21Z","email":"shadow@Zemenus-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Zemenu Mekuria"},"message":"feat(groups): unify list + room into a shared chat-style layout\n\nThe previous /groups (discovery grid) and /groups/[id] (chat) were two\ndisjoint pages; switching circles meant a full route transition. This\ncollapses both routes under a single layout that owns a persistent left\nsidebar with search, my/discover tabs, category chips, the group list,\nand a create-group entry point. Picking a group swaps only the right\npane (Next.js layout persistence) so the sidebar never unmounts and the\nuser perceives no page transition.\n\nAlso introduces the supporting palette tokens (honey/dawn/clay/online/\nidle/primary-soft/primary-deep + lvl-1..5 for the upcoming severity\nscale) in globals.css and registers them in tailwind.config.ts. The\nroom view is rebuilt around a RoomHeader + restyled feed + MembersRail\n(right column on xl+, sheet on smaller screens).\n\nAdds groups.room.* i18n keys.","tree":{"sha":"f206b58391c2383cf2293bc58c0e39ffbd4b6701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/f206b58391c2383cf2293bc58c0e39ffbd4b6701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/5775e5dddbd6c1385388f7ac55050d14d5c93f82","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.