NTAxMzQzZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/7886ba0130c85babd7cbb2c5187a597b05f71992","sha":"7886ba0130c85babd7cbb2c5187a597b05f71992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/7886ba0130c85babd7cbb2c5187a597b05f71992"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/d0223a086213d8503030a40eba472dd1fbcb87b8","sha":"d0223a086213d8503030a40eba472dd1fbcb87b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/d0223a086213d8503030a40eba472dd1fbcb87b8"}],"sha":"7ef55d18d02919c4998c08e036d5d2db501343db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/7ef55d18d02919c4998c08e036d5d2db501343db"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/d0223a086213d8503030a40eba472dd1fbcb87b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T09:39:25Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T09:39:25Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"message":"fix(avatar): make lipsync work for Amharic and survive strict-mode remount\n\n- Transliterate Ethiopic syllables to Latin so LipsyncEn produces visemes\n  for Amharic transcripts (engine only understands Latin letters)\n- Replace head.stop() with dispose() + canvas removal on unmount so React\n  strict-mode''s double-mount doesn''t leave a frozen first canvas stacked\n  over the live second one\n- Drop the post-load updateMorphTargets() call that reassigned each mesh''s\n  morphTargetInfluences array, orphaning the references TalkingHead had\n  already cached in mtAvatar — viseme writes were silently no-oping\n- Resume head.audioCtx from the user gesture so Chrome''s autoplay policy\n  doesn''t leave speakAudio''s animQueue empty\n- Remove TEMP diagnostic buttons and console.log probes","tree":{"sha":"982ceef0b97703195c1f4debcb617c22d37ba63e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/982ceef0b97703195c1f4debcb617c22d37ba63e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/d0223a086213d8503030a40eba472dd1fbcb87b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/d0223a086213d8503030a40eba472dd1fbcb87b8","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKGQwMjIzYTA4NjIxM2Q4NTAzMDMwYTQwZWJhNDcyZGQxZmJjYjg3Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/d640d6cf7a08ff1bcc96fef40bc95ccbbb076a16","sha":"d640d6cf7a08ff1bcc96fef40bc95ccbbb076a16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/d640d6cf7a08ff1bcc96fef40bc95ccbbb076a16"}],"sha":"d0223a086213d8503030a40eba472dd1fbcb87b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/d0223a086213d8503030a40eba472dd1fbcb87b8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/d640d6cf7a08ff1bcc96fef40bc95ccbbb076a16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T09:10:11Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T09:10:11Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"message":"docs(chat): add hard-delete implementation plan","tree":{"sha":"d7380d3d21b95e49b073a80150fda8e05d9c0a58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/d7380d3d21b95e49b073a80150fda8e05d9c0a58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/d640d6cf7a08ff1bcc96fef40bc95ccbbb076a16","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/d640d6cf7a08ff1bcc96fef40bc95ccbbb076a16","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKGQ2NDBkNmNmN2EwOGZmMWJjYzk2ZmVmNDBiYzk1Y2NiYmIwNzZhMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/fda439206aae0f4fde7cfff63685faae1dc60c3d","sha":"fda439206aae0f4fde7cfff63685faae1dc60c3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/fda439206aae0f4fde7cfff63685faae1dc60c3d"}],"sha":"d640d6cf7a08ff1bcc96fef40bc95ccbbb076a16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/d640d6cf7a08ff1bcc96fef40bc95ccbbb076a16"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/fda439206aae0f4fde7cfff63685faae1dc60c3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T09:07:48Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T09:07:48Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"message":"feat(rag): extract user facts and expose memory management UI\n\nPhase 7 of the RAG personalization plan\n(docs/plans/2026-05-15-rag-phase-7-facts-and-memory-ui.md).\n\nPhase 0/1 set up retrieval over memory_chunks with `kinds=[\"...\", \"profile_fact\"]`\nin both chat_service and voice_service, but nothing wrote profile_fact rows.\nThis change makes them real and gives users a way to view and delete what\nMindEase remembers about them.\n\nBackend:\n- FactExtractor (app/services/fact_extractor.py) runs after each user\n  text-chat turn via fire-and-forget asyncio.create_task. It calls the\n  existing Ollama-backed `generate_response` with a strict JSON-only prompt\n  for short, third-person facts, parses defensively (fenced blocks,\n  preambles), de-dupes against the user''s existing profile_facts by exact\n  text match, and indexes the survivors as memory_chunks with\n  source_kind=\"profile_fact\". Failures are logged, never raised — the chat\n  turn is never affected.\n- ProfileService.build_profile_block now appends a \"Known facts about this\n  user:\" block of the most-recent 15 facts to the system prompt, so the\n  text chat sees them on every turn (in addition to the existing semantic\n  retrieval).\n- VoiceContextService gains a `_profile_facts` section method wired into\n  the dossier so the voice avatar gets the same baseline.\n- MemoryService grows `list_for_user`, `delete`, `delete_all_for_user`.\n- New /api/v1/me/memory router:\n    GET    /memory?kind=&limit=&offset=  → paginated list (no embedding)\n    DELETE /memory/{chunk_id}            → 204, scoped to current user\n    DELETE /memory                       → {deleted: N}\n  Routes registered under /me in api/v1/router.py.\n\nFrontend:\n- /settings/memory page grouped by source_kind with per-row trash and a\n  confirmation dialog for \"Delete all memory\". Follows the mood page''s\n  container/header/skeleton/empty-state conventions, uses the existing\n  shadcn Dialog + Radix toast hook, no new dependencies.\n- lib/api.ts grows MemorySourceKind, MemoryChunkResponse, MemoryListResponse\n  and the three helpers (listMyMemory, deleteMyMemoryChunk, deleteAllMyMemory).\n- UserMenu''s \"Settings (coming soon)\" item is now a real Link to\n  /settings/memory.\n- settings.memory i18n namespace added to en.json + am.json.\n\nSmoke-verified end to end against the running stack: facts extracted from\na fact-rich chat message within ~10s, dedupe on repeat, DELETE one + DELETE\nall behave as expected, 401/404 paths return the right codes.","tree":{"sha":"6534ac7d9adca6f6b4f3d91b015d76731045f0dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/6534ac7d9adca6f6b4f3d91b015d76731045f0dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/fda439206aae0f4fde7cfff63685faae1dc60c3d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/fda439206aae0f4fde7cfff63685faae1dc60c3d","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKGZkYTQzOTIwNmFhZTBmNGZkZTdjZmZmNjM2ODVmYWFlMWRjNjBjM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/b7587e535fafb869540a9ad86170bfbe87183560","sha":"b7587e535fafb869540a9ad86170bfbe87183560","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/b7587e535fafb869540a9ad86170bfbe87183560"}],"sha":"fda439206aae0f4fde7cfff63685faae1dc60c3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/fda439206aae0f4fde7cfff63685faae1dc60c3d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/b7587e535fafb869540a9ad86170bfbe87183560/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T09:06:32Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T09:06:32Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"message":"feat(rag): route voice avatar through backend with persisted transcripts\n\nPhase 3 of the RAG personalization plan\n(docs/plans/2026-05-14-rag-phase-3-voice-backend.md).\n\nThe voice avatar previously opened a Gemini Live WebSocket directly from\nthe browser to Google with only a static persona prompt — no user\nidentity, no history, no backend involvement, nothing persisted. This\nmoves Live behind a backend WebSocket proxy so every call opens with a\nfull per-user dossier and every turn is persisted and indexed alongside\ntext-chat messages.\n\nBackend:\n- POST /api/v1/voice/conversations creates/reuses a Conversation marked\n  conversation_type=\"voice\" with persona attrs.\n- /ws/voice/{conversation_id} proxies audio in both directions to Gemini\n  Live via google-genai''s client.aio.live.connect, requests input + output\n  transcription, persists each turn as user + AI Message rows, and indexes\n  them into memory_chunks with source_kind=\"voice_transcript\".\n- VoiceContextService assembles a dossier (identity, engagement, mood,\n  screenings, resource prefs, peer groups, crisis signal) for the Live\n  system_instruction; semantic retrieval over prior voice_transcript +\n  text-chat memory feeds the same instruction.\n- Adds conversation_type + attrs columns on conversations\n  (b2c3d4e5f6a7_add_conversation_type_attrs).\n- Changes conversation soft-delete to a hard delete with explicit\n  memory_chunks scrub; messages cascade via FK\n  (c3d4e5f6a7b8_messages_cascade_on_conversation_delete) and the chat\n  service''s delete_conversation replaces archive_conversation.\n\nFrontend:\n- BackendVoiceSession replaces the direct-to-Gemini VoiceSession.\n- /avatar opens a conversation up front, attaches it to the WS, and the\n  conversation appears in the chat sidebar with a phone icon. Clicking\n  surfaces the transcript in /chat/[id]; \"Continue this call\" reopens\n  /avatar bound to the same conversation.\n- gemini-avatar.ts keeps fetchTTS for persona previews; VoiceSession is\n  gone. NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY survives only for previews; the Live\n  key now lives only on the backend.","tree":{"sha":"7cfe1cffdeee2da02915ae1ca0baa426207e7164","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/7cfe1cffdeee2da02915ae1ca0baa426207e7164"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/b7587e535fafb869540a9ad86170bfbe87183560","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/b7587e535fafb869540a9ad86170bfbe87183560","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKGI3NTg3ZTUzNWZhZmI4Njk1NDBhOWFkODYxNzBiZmJlODcxODM1NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/6c4e90727a5ada9e5b392f54b26a89f41f490562","sha":"6c4e90727a5ada9e5b392f54b26a89f41f490562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/6c4e90727a5ada9e5b392f54b26a89f41f490562"}],"sha":"b7587e535fafb869540a9ad86170bfbe87183560","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/b7587e535fafb869540a9ad86170bfbe87183560"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/6c4e90727a5ada9e5b392f54b26a89f41f490562/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T22:05:14Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T22:05:14Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"message":"feat(rag): wire chat prompt + indexing hooks to memory_chunks\n\n- Rewrite ChatService.process_message_stream prompt builder: embed user content\n  once in parallel with crisis check; reuse the vector for retrieval and the\n  inline user-chunk insert; assemble layered system prompt\n  (## About this user / ## Relevant past moments) over the last 10 messages\n- Fire-and-forget index AI messages after stream completes (own session)\n- MoodService.create_entry indexes non-empty notes; AssessmentService.submit\n  indexes feedback_text — both background tasks with their own sessions\n- Add ProfileService.build_profile_block (display_name + recent mood + latest\n  screenings) plus MoodService.recent_summary and\n  AssessmentService.{latest_per_type, format_latest_block}\n- Add manual backfill script: python -m app.seeds.backfill_memory\n  (idempotent via the unique partial index on (source_kind, source_id))","tree":{"sha":"4b597dfae59b6e467c1a9ec25834f1f1dbde2ae2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/4b597dfae59b6e467c1a9ec25834f1f1dbde2ae2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/6c4e90727a5ada9e5b392f54b26a89f41f490562","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/6c4e90727a5ada9e5b392f54b26a89f41f490562","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKDZjNGU5MDcyN2E1YWRhOWU1YjM5MmY1NGIyNmE4OWY0MWY0OTA1NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/2c08a5830b9e38b90c4ea60147f988ddf1f534a8","sha":"2c08a5830b9e38b90c4ea60147f988ddf1f534a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/2c08a5830b9e38b90c4ea60147f988ddf1f534a8"}],"sha":"6c4e90727a5ada9e5b392f54b26a89f41f490562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/6c4e90727a5ada9e5b392f54b26a89f41f490562"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/commits/2c08a5830b9e38b90c4ea60147f988ddf1f534a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T22:05:06Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T22:05:06Z","email":"anatoli@Anatolis-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Anatoli"},"message":"feat(rag): add pgvector foundation, memory_chunks table, /embed, MemoryService\n\n- Swap Postgres image to pgvector/pgvector:pg16; enable vector + pgcrypto extensions\n- Add memory_chunks table (vector(768), JSONB attrs) with ivfflat cosine, filter,\n  and partial-unique (source_kind, source_id) indexes; register MemoryChunk model\n- Add /embed endpoint on ai-service backed by Gemini gemini-embedding-001 (768-d,\n  RETRIEVAL_DOCUMENT task type, batches up to 100)\n- Introduce backend AIClient.embed() and MemoryService with index/index_many/retrieve\n  (precomputed-vector escape hatch, cosine_distance ordering)\n\nPhase 0 is non-behavioral on its own — no existing code path changes. Phase 1\nwires it into the chat prompt and indexing hooks.","tree":{"sha":"6b15be4cff7c4dece79dd8b4b106c9d7e626e2f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/trees/6b15be4cff7c4dece79dd8b4b106c9d7e626e2f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Amantsehay/MindEase/git/commits/2c08a5830b9e38b90c4ea60147f988ddf1f534a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/2c08a5830b9e38b90c4ea60147f988ddf1f534a8","node_id":"C_kwDOSpuiPdoAKDJjMDhhNTgzMGI5ZTM4YjkwYzRlYTYwMTQ3Zjk4OGRkZjFmNTM0YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Amantsehay/MindEase/commit/50d262ca3a7f9eec30bee58304f7c44cf5af1364","sha":"50d262ca3a7f9eec30bee58304f7c44cf5af1364","url":"https://api.github.com