0e9c9db026b8f9aaf567ea9db3ce","node_id":"C_kwDOSp3UndoAKDdlOWFhMzFkNjhlMTBlOWM5ZGIwMjZiOGY5YWFmNTY3ZWE5ZGIzY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/j0yen/wintermute-audio/commit/1af678df6334993cd72f8f3e63e4d2829cff5b61","sha":"1af678df6334993cd72f8f3e63e4d2829cff5b61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/j0yen/wintermute-audio/commits/1af678df6334993cd72f8f3e63e4d2829cff5b61"}],"sha":"7e9aa31d68e10e9c9db026b8f9aaf567ea9db3ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/j0yen/wintermute-audio/commits/7e9aa31d68e10e9c9db026b8f9aaf567ea9db3ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178452872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/j0yen","id":178452872,"login":"j0yen","node_id":"U_kgDOCqL5iA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/j0yen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/j0yen/wintermute-audio/commits/1af678df6334993cd72f8f3e63e4d2829cff5b61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T01:59:21Z","email":"jyen.tech@gmail.com","name":"Joe Yen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T01:59:21Z","email":"jyen.tech@gmail.com","name":"Joe Yen"},"message":"wintermute-audio: v0.2.0 — pw-record subprocess source (PRD-pipewire-input)\n\nCloses the input-side gap: the daemon now spawns pw-record and streams\n16 kHz mono i16 frames through the existing UDS fanout. Mirror of the\nwm-tts pw-cat output ship from earlier today.\n\nWhat''s new:\n- SupervisedPwRecord source spawns pw-record (or $WM_PW_RECORD_BIN),\n  reads 320-sample frames off stdout, and respawns on exit with\n  1s/2s/4s/.../30s capped backoff so capture is a persistent service.\n- wm.audio.capture.start / wm.audio.capture.end / wm.audio.error\n  envelopes wrap each spawn cycle; the self-emitted-topic filter\n  (mirror of wm-tts/bus.rs) silences any echoed publishes that come\n  back through wm.audio.* subscribers.\n- AC9: missing-node fallback. When WM_MIC_NODE is set but absent from\n  the live pactl source list, fall back to PipeWire''s default and emit\n  wm.audio.error{kind:\"mic_node_fallback\"} rather than refusing to start.\n- AC10: missing-binary soft-fail. When pw-record isn''t on $PATH, emit\n  wm.audio.error{kind:\"pw_record_missing\"} and retry with backoff\n  instead of crashing.\n- captured_bytes metric (PRD §2.4 / AC7) bumps on each frame seen\n  through the fanout broadcast.\n\nOther fixes rolled in for the build to be green:\n- Bump MSRV / rust-toolchain.toml to 1.88 — agorabus v0.3 uses let-chains\n  which are stable in 1.88+; the previous 1.85 pin no longer compiles\n  the workspace.\n- Add allow-wildcard-paths = true to deny.toml for the in-tree\n  agorabus path dep (cargo deny check bans now clean).\n- 60 lib tests pass (was 42; +18 new tests cover the supervisor,\n  argv builder, mic-node resolver, backoff schedule, and the\n  capture/error event shapes).\n\nCloses PRD-wintermute-audio-pipewire-input.","tree":{"sha":"dfea237b8c28686ee1a068cf64d9f0c372526dd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/j0yen/wintermute-audio/git/trees/dfea237b8c28686ee1a068cf64d9f0c372526dd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/j0yen/wintermute-audio/git/commits/1af678df6334993cd72f8f3e63e4d2829cff5b61","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconte