gDOCV0gkg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/commits/4ecaa7918caaf9ae5e8992255d0687f932f5f941/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:59:11Z","email":"typhosj@gmx.de","name":"typhosj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:59:11Z","email":"typhosj@gmx.de","name":"typhosj"},"message":"docs: condense the changelog, and correct the value and table pages\n\nThe WIP changelog had grown to 35 flat entries and became the 1.0.0 release\nnotes nobody would read. 22 now, ordered by what a user cares about, with the\nentries merged that a user does not tell apart: the eight clipping defects share\none cause and read as one line, as do the five single layout fixes and the three\nlanguage entries. Nothing actionable was dropped -- the twenty retired Material\nDesign Icons names are still listed, because that one is a to-do for anyone\nusing them.\n\nTwo documented statements were wrong. value.md gave \"x/1000\" as the calculation\nexample in both languages; the placeholder is #value, and an expression without\nit is never evaluated, so the field silently did nothing for anyone following the\ndocumentation. table.md described the old per-row column behaviour, which the\nfix in the previous commit replaced -- and it told the reader to keep the same\nproperty order in every row, advice that is now unnecessary.\n\nThe Table''s alternating row color (upstream wish #127) was not documented at all.\n\nChecked while there, all clean: 60 files, DE/EN parity 1:1, every internal link\nand all 112 images resolve, no orphaned image, and the terminology matches the\neditor labels in admin/i18n.","tree":{"sha":"38344c9d64cac3778432c518d62656eca0c6dcef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/git/trees/38344c9d64cac3778432c518d62656eca0c6dcef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/git/commits/4ecaa7918caaf9ae5e8992255d0687f932f5f941","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157098130?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/typhosj","id":157098130,"login":"typhosj","node_id":"U_kgDOCV0gkg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/commit/4ecaa7918caaf9ae5e8992255d0687f932f5f941","node_id":"C_kwDOSqNii9oAKDRlY2FhNzkxOGNhYWY5YWU1ZTg5OTIyNTVkMDY4N2Y5MzJmNWY5NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/commit/4b9fb9407eae73be8a9d060f23db0b3b3ef4c3d1","sha":"4b9fb9407eae73be8a9d060f23db0b3b3ef4c3d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/commits/4b9fb9407eae73be8a9d060f23db0b3b3ef4c3d1"}],"sha":"4ecaa7918caaf9ae5e8992255d0687f932f5f941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/commits/4ecaa7918caaf9ae5e8992255d0687f932f5f941"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157098130?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/typhosj","id":157098130,"login":"typhosj","node_id":"U_kgDOCV0gkg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/commits/4b9fb9407eae73be8a9d060f23db0b3b3ef4c3d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:58:59Z","email":"typhosj@gmx.de","name":"typhosj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:58:59Z","email":"typhosj@gmx.de","name":"typhosj"},"message":"fix(widgets): bind #value instead of compiling it, and six more from a review\n\nThe Value widget pasted the state''s own text into the expression it then handed\nto Function(): a state holding \"(fetch(evil),1)\" ran that code in every browser\nshowing the view, and whatever writes the datapoint -- an MQTT topic, an HTTP\nresponse, a cloud adapter -- decided what ran. mathjs is not a dependency and\nvis-2 does not load it, so the Function() fallback was the only path, never the\nfallback it was written as. #value is bound as an argument now. That also ends\ntwo crashes it caused: a string value compiled to a bare identifier and threw a\nReferenceError out of render, and a mistyped expression did the same -- each\nblanked the whole view, since vis-2 renders a view''s widgets in one tree without\nan error boundary. Both are caught now and leave the plain value standing.\n\nThe iframe dialog was the one navigation sink still taking its address\nunchecked, while Buttons, Card and IconList all go through safeWidgetUrl. Its\ndefault sandbox carries allow-scripts together with allow-same-origin, which the\nspec treats as no sandbox at all, so a javascript: address there ran in the page.\n\nThree copies of the number coercion had drifted from the shared numberValue --\nthe same drift the Calendar was fixed for in 0.3.5, in the copies that were left\nbehind. Number('''') is a finite 0, so a cleared field beat its declared default:\na Progress whose maximum had been emptied sat at 0 % whatever the datapoint said.\nThe decimals path needed more than the alias, because it asked === undefined and\n'''' is not undefined; optionalNumber joins numberValue in widgetUtils and replaces\nthe private copy the chart canvas kept.\n\nThe Table read every row against its own key order, so one missing property slid\nthe rest of that row a column to the left. The columns are the first row''s keys\nnow, read once, and the header, aria-sort and sort arrow use the same list --\nthey were reading content[0] after the sort, which is a different row.\n\nRead-only and working-locked sliders, switches, checkboxes and buttons ran their\nhaptics and click sound before the check that refused the write, and the sliders\ntook the pointer capture as well. A cancelled drag -- an incoming call, a palm on\nthe screen -- released the capture but left the throttled write queued, so the\nvalue the finger rested on still landed a moment later.\n\nThe duration and timestamp formats read every d, h, m and s in the template as a\ntoken, so \"hh:mm [Std]\" printed \"08:30 St0\" and a label''s letters even decided\nwhich units the duration was split into. Text in [brackets] is literal now, the\nmoment convention both formatters replaced and which MDW 1.x configs carry.\n\nSeven runnable checks come with it: the injection payload is not executed, a\nstring condition does not throw, a broken expression leaves the value standing,\ncleared min/max/maxDecimals fall back to their defaults, a row missing a field\nkeeps its column, and both formatters keep bracketed text.","tree":{"sha":"4101d2fddb41b843ca02765b0328fbf6639ebf5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/git/trees/4101d2fddb41b843ca02765b0328fbf6639ebf5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/git/commits/4b9fb9407eae73be8a9d060f23db0b3b3ef4c3d1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157098130?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/typhosj","id":157098130,"login":"typhosj","node_id":"U_kgDOCV0gkg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/commit/4b9fb9407eae73be8a9d060f23db0b3b3ef4c3d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSqNii9oAKDRiOWZiOTQwN2VhZTczYmU4YTl