,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/commits/edfe822f6cb2041f0da9acacf794548bcd241b80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T06:15:25Z","email":"typhosj@gmx.de","name":"typhosj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T06:15:25Z","email":"typhosj@gmx.de","name":"typhosj"},"message":"fix(list): let the header padding take part on every side\n\nThe header row carried a fixed height and no `border-box`, so that height was its content box: the bottom padding hung below it and the header container clipped it away with `overflow: hidden`. \"Padding bottom\" therefore did nothing in any setting, in the List and in the Icon List alike. The height is a minimum now, the row measures itself with `border-box`, and the clipping container plus its -5px pull are gone. The fallback for the bottom padding drops from 20 to 0 - those 20px were never drawn, and keeping them would grow every existing header on update.","tree":{"sha":"3e02fcbcdfeed6a9372212d0ebb4b3952ff15a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/git/trees/3e02fcbcdfeed6a9372212d0ebb4b3952ff15a85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typhosj/ioBroker.vis2-materialdesign/git/commits/edfe822f6cb2041f0da9acacf794548bcd241b80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157098130?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/typhosj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_