026-05-28T07:20:33Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"bejono17","providerType":"User"},"email":"bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:13:02.631Z","repositoryId":1252248682,"sha":"7afbd0674fe2296abfadba28af108d6a199bdc30"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"bejono17","providerType":"User"},"email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"authoredDate":"2026-05-28T07:16:50Z","committedDate":"2026-05-28T07:16:50Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"bejono17","providerType":"User"},"email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:13:02.631Z","repositoryId":1252248682,"sha":"9a2f4b63b81955e5c99ea2e12296044a62aefa90"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"bejono17","providerType":"User"},"email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"authoredDate":"2026-05-27T10:32:06Z","committedDate":"2026-05-27T10:32:06Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"bejono17","providerType":"User"},"email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:13:02.631Z","repositoryId":1252248682,"sha":"e1de0b6add9d2c6ae924ffe678f9bc617969d3fa"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:13:02.631Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/f92a7e6555e91d4618a177822b541969c6695c15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:09:32Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:09:32Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"fix(init): platform picker selected the wrong thing, and `layer` did nothing\n\nThree bugs reported from actually using the wizard, all confirmed.\n\n1. Choosing codex or kiro produced claude-code files.\n\n   `checked: p === \"claude-code\"` pre-selected claude-code in the platform\n   checkbox. Arrow keys move the cursor there but only SPACE toggles, so\n   arrowing to \"codex\" and pressing enter submitted the pre-checked claude-code\n   and left codex unselected. Nothing is pre-selected now, the prompt says\n   \"press SPACE to select, ENTER to confirm\", and `required: true` rejects an\n   empty answer instead of relying on a later error.\n\n2. The profile list ignored the chosen layer.\n\n   Picking `backend` still offered react-vite and react-rsbuild-microfrontend,\n   and filtering was not even possible: no profile declared a layer. Each\n   profile now carries `layers:` frontmatter, loadProfile strips it so it never\n   reaches a generated context file, and the wizard offers only the profiles\n   that match — falling back to the full list for layers no profile claims yet\n   (worker, mobile) rather than showing an empty prompt.\n\n3. `layer` was decorative, and the consequence was a security hole.\n\n   It appeared in four places, all display strings, and filtered nothing: every\n   repo got all 12 agents. A frontend-only repo shipped a `migration-author` for\n   a database it did not have — and because the manifest declared no\n   `paths.migrations`, that agent had no allow-list, so the guard fell through\n   to the forbidden list alone. Confirmed on the demo frontend repo: a\n   `backend-builder` write to `src/components/Evil.tsx` returned exit 0. The\n   agent nobody wanted was the least constrained one in the repo.\n\n   An editing agent is now generated only when the manifest declares the paths\n   it owns; read-only agents are always generated. Re-install deletes agents a\n   previous manifest left behind — without that the fix would only have applied\n   to new repos, and a stale unscoped writer would have stayed on disk.\n\n   The result is an invariant rather than a rule: every generated editing agent\n   has an entry in factory-scope.json, because one manifest key produces both.\n   Verified on demo/frontend — backend-builder, devops-builder and\n   migration-author are gone, and no editing agent is left unscoped.\n\n   The Codex orchestrator no longer treats a missing agent file as fatal; it\n   skips the step, since a repo legitimately may not have that agent.\n\nD6''s distinction survives: an absent key means the agent does not exist here, a\nkey present but empty means it exists and may edit nothing.\n\nNot addressed here, by request: a `fullstack` repo still declares a single\n`profile:`, so it cannot say \"backend is bun-hono, frontend is react-vite\".\nThat changes the manifest schema and is its own decision.\n\nTests: 199 (was 190) — a new agent-relevance suite plus profile-metadata checks;\nthe adapter tests now derive the expected agent set from the manifest instead of\nassuming all twelve.","tree":{"sha":"c8ddb57d55c8d85b426793205b1c471550479dea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/c8ddb57d55c8d85b426793205b1c471550479dea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/f92a7e6555e91d4618a177822b541969c6695c15","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/f92a7e6555e91d4618a177822b541969c6695c15","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKGY5MmE3ZTY1NTVlOTFkNDYxOGExNzc4MjJiNTQxOTY5YzY2OTVjMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/b544feda9838ec52b1a08b16c154794ab3570ef9","sha":"b544feda9838ec52b1a08b16c154794ab3570ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/b544feda9838ec52b1a08b16c154794ab3570ef9"}],"sha":"f92a7e6555e91d4618a177822b541969c6695c15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/f92a7e6555e91d4618a177822b541969c6695c15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/b544feda9838ec52b1a08b16c154794ab3570ef9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:24:08Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:24:08Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"fix(guard): name the platform''s own context file in the block message\n\nConfirming Kiro CLI enforcement turned up a smaller bug in the shared guard. An\nout-of-scope fs_write was correctly blocked, but the reason ended with\n\n  (CLAUDE.md -> \"Path scoping for agents\")\n\nin a repo whose context file is `.kiro/steering/project.md`. The guard is shared\nby Claude Code and Kiro and hardcoded one platform''s filename, so it pointed\nKiro users at a file they do not have — the same class of leak as the prompt\ntool names, just quieter.\n\n- ScopeConfig gains `contextFile`; each adapter passes its own (CLAUDE.md,\n  .kiro/steering/project.md, AGENTS.md) into factory-scope.json.\n- Both assets read it, with a neutral fallback for an older config file.\n- tests: the message quotes the configured file, and falls back when absent.\n\nAlso records what the Kiro run established. Kiro''s per-agent hook lives in the\nagent''s JSON config and **does** fire:\n\n  ✗ preToolUse \"node .kiro/factory-guard.mjs migration-author\" failed with exit\n    code: 2 … PreToolHook blocked the tool execution\n\nfile untouched. Claude Code''s equivalent in agent frontmatter does not (D5). The\ntwo read like one feature in the docs; only running them apart shows they are\nnot. New D13 in the book covers that, plus the testing problem behind it: every\nagent refused the out-of-scope write on prompt grounds before reaching any tool\ncall, so both confirmations needed the prompt-level rules temporarily removed —\na compliant agent can never exercise its own guard.\n\nkiro.ts''s \"verified against Kiro CLI\" comment now cites the observed output\nrather than asserting it.\n\nTests: 190 (was 188).","tree":{"sha":"735d7fe2f86ae2eb64c7000d4bab1eb5a7e101b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/735d7fe2f86ae2eb64c7000d4bab1eb5a7e101b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/b544feda9838ec52b1a08b16c154794ab3570ef9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/b544feda9838ec52b1a08b16c154794ab3570ef9","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKGI1NDRmZWRhOTgzOGVjNTJiMWEwOGIxNmMxNTQ3OTRhYjM1NzBlZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/4f436e083f3ab18289888a23b4fa66b182db5d6a","sha":"4f436e083f3ab18289888a23b4fa66b182db5d6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/4f436e083f3ab18289888a23b4fa66b182db5d6a"}],"sha":"b544feda9838ec52b1a08b16c154794ab3570ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/b544feda9838ec52b1a08b16c154794ab3570ef9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/4f436e083f3ab18289888a23b4fa66b182db5d6a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:17:39Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:17:39Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"fix(prompts): researcher was blind on Codex — remove platform tool names\n\nRunning `.codex/orchestrator/spike.sh` against the demo repo returned \"unable\nto determine\" for every section of the researcher''s report, ending with:\n\n  Cannot determine how tenant scoping is enforced ... because the available\n  inspection path requires shell commands, which the role instructions prohibit.\n\nThe cause is in prompts/agents/researcher.md, which told the agent to \"use Grep\nand Glob aggressively\" and, two lines later, \"do not run shell commands\". Those\nare Claude Code''s tool names. Codex has no such tools and inspects a repo\n*through* the shell, so the prompt named capabilities it lacked and banned the\nonly one it had. Tier 1 was useless on Codex and nobody had noticed, because\nnobody had run it.\n\nThis is the leak the book''s chapter 01 exists to prevent: prompts carry the\nprocess, adapters carry the platform. Tool naming already lives in the adapters\n(TOOLS_BY_AGENT in claude-code.ts, the tools array in kiro.ts) and had no\nbusiness in a prompt.\n\n- researcher.md: search/read described by capability, not by tool name; the\n  shell ban becomes the intent it was reaching for — change nothing, inspection\n  is read-only, reading and searching by any available means is fine.\n- spec-writer.md: same leak in its hard-rules list, same fix.\n- test/prompt-neutrality.test.ts: four checks over every prompt — no\n  platform-specific tool name, no platform product name, no blanket shell ban.\n  The failure mode was silent and platform-specific, so it needs a guard that\n  is neither.\n\nVerified by re-running the same spike on Codex. The researcher now returns real\ncitations — `src/routes/orders.ts:11-14`, `src/services/order.service.ts:3-4` —\nand independently flagged the IDOR planted in the demo fixture under both\n\"Tenant isolation\" and \"Auth and authorization gaps\".\n\nTests: 188 (was 184).","tree":{"sha":"850d6dcfbd5a3a878058fa2c3273e932faccac1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/850d6dcfbd5a3a878058fa2c3273e932faccac1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/4f436e083f3ab18289888a23b4fa66b182db5d6a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/4f436e083f3ab18289888a23b4fa66b182db5d6a","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKDRmNDM2ZTA4M2YzYWIxODI4OTg4OGEyM2I0ZmE2NmIxODJkYjVkNmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/b7e96eb15db6fef2279450671c16d3adc5fefb2d","sha":"b7e96eb15db6fef2279450671c16d3adc5fefb2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/b7e96eb15db6fef2279450671c16d3adc5fefb2d"}],"sha":"4f436e083f3ab18289888a23b4fa66b182db5d6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/4f436e083f3ab18289888a23b4fa66b182db5d6a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/b7e96eb15db6fef2279450671c16d3adc5fefb2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:08:57Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:08:57Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"fix(claude-code): per-agent scoping was never enforced — move it to the session hook\n\nPer-agent path scoping has been documented as enforced since the feature\nlanded. It wasn''t. Claude Code ignores the `hooks:` block in agent frontmatter,\nso every generated per-agent hook was dead config, and only the `forbidden`\nlist — carried by the session-level hook in settings.json — was ever applied.\n\nFound by running the real thing. Unit tests had always passed because they\ninvoke the guard directly; nobody had watched an actual subagent try to break\nscope. Instrumenting the guard to log every invocation and driving Claude Code\n2.1.278 through a subagent edit showed one invocation with no argv, and an\nout-of-scope write by `migration-author` into `src/services/**` landing on\ndisk.\n\nThe same log line carried the fix: the PreToolUse payload now includes\n`agent_type` — the acting subagent''s name, or null for the main session. That\nis the information the original design (D5) said wasn''t available, which is why\nit went into frontmatter in the first place.\n\n- assets/factory-guard.mjs: resolve the agent from `argv[2]` first, else\n  `agent_type` from the payload. Kiro CLI still passes argv, so it is\n  unaffected and argv keeps winning.\n- claude-code.ts: stop emitting frontmatter `hooks:` blocks entirely, with a\n  comment recording why. Emit the session hook whenever *any* scope is declared,\n  not just a forbidden list — it now carries per-agent enforcement too.\n- tests: the three that asserted frontmatter hooks now assert their absence;\n  four new cases cover scoping by `agent_type`, a null agent falling back to\n  forbidden-only, an unknown agent, and argv still taking precedence.\n\nVerified end-to-end, not just in unit tests. With the prompt-level rules\ntemporarily stripped from the demo''s CLAUDE.md — so a compliant agent would\nactually attempt the write — Claude Code returned:\n\n  PreToolUse:Edit hook error: Blocked by ai-factory path guard:\n  \"src/services/order.service.ts\" is outside migration-author allowed paths\n  [src/db/**, drizzle/**]\n\nand the file was untouched. The same prompt before this change modified it.\n\nDocs: README''s enforcement section, book ch04''s layer diagram, and D5 — which\nis now a reversal entry, including the lesson. A hook nobody has watched fire\nis a hypothesis, not enforcement.\n\nKnown residual risk: enforcement now depends on `agent_type` being present. A\nversion that stops sending it degrades silently to forbidden-only rather than\nfailing loudly — the same failure shape this commit just fixed, and a candidate\nfor the eval harness.\n\nTests: 184 (was 180).","tree":{"sha":"6e7f312e4a50b8e2d8e4e9c7fd9b652039630485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/6e7f312e4a50b8e2d8e4e9c7fd9b652039630485"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/b7e96eb15db6fef2279450671c16d3adc5fefb2d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/b7e96eb15db6fef2279450671c16d3adc5fefb2d","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKGI3ZTk2ZWIxNWRiNmZlZjIyNzk0NTA2NzFjMTZkM2FkYzVmZWZiMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/291ed494b0712f33dfda182c04d297a4200c2f1d","sha":"291ed494b0712f33dfda182c04d297a4200c2f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/291ed494b0712f33dfda182c04d297a4200c2f1d"}],"sha":"b7e96eb15db6fef2279450671c16d3adc5fefb2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/b7e96eb15db6fef2279450671c16d3adc5fefb2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/291ed494b0712f33dfda182c04d297a4200c2f1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:34:26Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:34:26Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"feat(claude-code): emit .claude/FACTORY.md, and fix the stale Kiro one\n\nKiro and Codex each generate a FACTORY.md; Claude Code never did. That gap got\nworse with every phase: `.claude/` now holds a path guard, two optional\nlifecycle hooks, `permissions.deny` rules and possibly a sandbox block, and\nnothing in an installed repo explained where any of it came from. Someone\nopening such a repo could find `sandbox.filesystem.denyWrite` in their\nsettings.json with no way to trace it.\n\nThe generated doc is manifest-aware rather than boilerplate:\n\n- A provenance table with one row per thing the factory actually added to\n  settings.json — what it is, why it''s there, and the exact `.factory.yaml`\n  edit that turns it off. Rows appear only for features this manifest enables;\n  a manifest with no scope and no hooks says so instead.\n- The path-scoping section lists the agents actually scoped, and its heading\n  reads \"enforced\" or \"prompt-only\" to match. Claiming enforcement over an\n  empty allow-list is the kind of quiet lie this project exists to avoid.\n- The boundary is stated plainly: only the per-agent hook is per-agent, so a\n  shell write is checked against the forbidden list and never against an\n  allow-list. Guardrail, not containment.\n\nAlso fixes a bug this work uncovered. The Phase 3 switch to native Kiro Agent\nSkills patched `kiro.ts` with a script that used plain backticks, but the\nFACTORY.md template literal escapes them (\\\\`), so most replacements silently\ndid nothing — and the verifying grep only covered README.md and docs/, not\nsrc/. The result shipped to every Kiro repo told users to type\n`#skill-feature-factory`, which install had just deleted, while one line in the\nsame file already said `/feature-factory`. Now consistent.\n\nTwo lessons worth keeping: a string replace with no match assertion is a silent\nno-op, and a grep that doesn''t cover the generator source doesn''t verify\ngenerated output. The golden snapshot didn''t catch this one because the stale\ntext was on both sides of the diff — a snapshot pins what is, not what should be.\n\nTests: 180 (counts and golden snapshots updated for the new file).","tree":{"sha":"6fa1f41689909c84cac3670ab504bf7d7bf33122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/6fa1f41689909c84cac3670ab504bf7d7bf33122"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/291ed494b0712f33dfda182c04d297a4200c2f1d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/291ed494b0712f33dfda182c04d297a4200c2f1d","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKDI5MWVkNDk0YjA3MTJmMzNkZmRhMTgyYzA0ZDI5N2E0MjAwYzJmMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/1be323fca515421d430dc0e5d787bfdbde392953","sha":"1be323fca515421d430dc0e5d787bfdbde392953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/1be323fca515421d430dc0e5d787bfdbde392953"}],"sha":"291ed494b0712f33dfda182c04d297a4200c2f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/291ed494b0712f33dfda182c04d297a4200c2f1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/1be323fca515421d430dc0e5d787bfdbde392953/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:14:59Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:14:59Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"docs(book): catch the book up with five phases of changes\n\nThe book''s own rule is \"if the code and the book disagree, the code wins — fix\nthe book\", and it had drifted on every chapter that touches enforcement.\n\n- ch04: \"the two-layer design\" becomes four layers. Layers 1–2 are the\n  per-agent hooks as before; layer 3 is `permissions.deny`, which also covers\n  the file commands Claude Code recognises inside Bash; layer 4 is the opt-in\n  OS-level sandbox, which reaches child processes. Records the two syntax traps\n  that fail silently (`Edit(...)` not `Write(...)`; sandbox paths use the\n  opposite absolute/relative convention to permission rules), the symlink hole\n  and its realpath fix, and why Codex keeps a post-run check.\n- ch04 lifecycle: ownership is now by script name (`applyHook`/`ownsMarker`),\n  and deny/denyWrite rules are pruned against the previous factory-scope.json.\n- ch02: the adapter writes six kinds of output, not four; settings.json merges\n  three contributions, not one; `extractDescription` is now the shared\n  `skillDescription` in src/util/skill-meta.ts.\n- ch01: documents `models:`, `hooks:` and `sandbox:` and the rule they follow —\n  anything that changes session behaviour is opt-in.\n- ch05: Kiro emits native Agent Skills; Claude Code is the only adapter that\n  can express layers 3–4 and the lifecycle hooks.\n- ch09: D7 rewritten (Bash is no longer simply out of scope, and the honest\n  residue is that only layers 1–2 are per-agent), D5''s trade-off corrected, and\n  three new entries — D10 opt-in-by-default, D11 why Codex PreToolUse was\n  rejected, D12 golden snapshots. Known-limitations and future-work tables\n  re-pointed: \"run it for real\" is now the top item, because everything from\n  the lifecycle hooks onward is verified as generated correctly, not as\n  honoured by the platform.\n\nNo code changes; 180 tests still pass.","tree":{"sha":"31b0c4a841b13f69113fc6ffb9182401de9d89ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/31b0c4a841b13f69113fc6ffb9182401de9d89ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/1be323fca515421d430dc0e5d787bfdbde392953","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/1be323fca515421d430dc0e5d787bfdbde392953","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKDFiZTMyM2ZjYTUxNTQyMWQ0MzBkYzBlNWQ3ODdiZmRiZGUzOTI5NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/603a2e730799b4a91770b7695ae29bf14223df18","sha":"603a2e730799b4a91770b7695ae29bf14223df18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/603a2e730799b4a91770b7695ae29bf14223df18"}],"sha":"1be323fca515421d430dc0e5d787bfdbde392953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/1be323fca515421d430dc0e5d787bfdbde392953"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/603a2e730799b4a91770b7695ae29bf14223df18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:09:49Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:09:49Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"feat(claude-code): opt-in OS-level sandbox, with forbidden as denyWrite\n\nThree layers guarded `forbidden:` and none of them saw a subprocess. The\nPreToolUse hook fires on the edit tools; permissions.deny adds the file\ncommands Claude Code recognises inside Bash; but a Node or Python script the\nagent runs opens files itself, and nothing caught that. `sandbox: true` closes\nit — enforcement is OS-level (Seatbelt on macOS, bubblewrap on Linux/WSL2), so\nit covers a command''s child processes.\n\nEach forbidden glob becomes a `sandbox.filesystem.denyWrite` rule alongside\n`sandbox.enabled`. What makes this work at all: a denyWrite holds *inside* the\nwider allow that makes the repo writable, so denying `./.env*` bites even\nthough the whole project root is writable. Without that the sandbox would only\nhave stopped writes outside the repo, which is not where the manifest''s\nforbidden files live.\n\nTwo rules per glob, `./x` and `./**/x`, because the syntaxes disagree about\ndepth: `forbidden:` is gitignore-flavoured, where a bare filename matches\nanywhere, while sandbox paths resolve `./x` against the project root and it is\nnot documented whether a leading double-star also matches zero segments. For a\ndeny list, over-emitting is the safe direction — a redundant rule, not a hole.\n\nNote the two syntaxes in play: sandbox paths use `/` for absolute and `./` for\nproject-relative, the opposite of the `//` and `/` convention that Read/Edit\npermission rules use. Getting these backwards is silent, so they are derived in\nseparate functions rather than shared.\n\nOff by default, like the lifecycle hooks: the sandbox constrains every command\nin a session. Turning it back off removes our denyWrite rules and removes\n`enabled` only when that is all we wrote — a sandbox the user configured\nthemselves is left alone.\n\nCodex is not wired up. It has an OS-level sandbox (`sandbox_mode`,\n`sandbox_workspace_write.writable_roots`) and per-path permission profiles, but\nits docs say the two must not be combined, and generating `.codex/config.toml`\nwould mean owning a file that also carries the user''s own Codex configuration.\n\nTests: 180 (was 175).","tree":{"sha":"f8eeebe563664b9ef968c8b211db8483da6a0262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/f8eeebe563664b9ef968c8b211db8483da6a0262"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/603a2e730799b4a91770b7695ae29bf14223df18","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/603a2e730799b4a91770b7695ae29bf14223df18","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKDYwM2EyZTczMDc5OWI0YTkxNzcwYjc2OTVhZTI5YmYxNDIyM2RmMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/6dfdfc814fd4bbea0b4817f391da37624be250aa","sha":"6dfdfc814fd4bbea0b4817f391da37624be250aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/6dfdfc814fd4bbea0b4817f391da37624be250aa"}],"sha":"603a2e730799b4a91770b7695ae29bf14223df18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/603a2e730799b4a91770b7695ae29bf14223df18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/6dfdfc814fd4bbea0b4817f391da37624be250aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:03:11Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:03:11Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"feat(kiro): emit native Agent Skills instead of steering files\n\nKiro grew a first-class Agent Skills mechanism, which is what the three\norchestrators have wanted to be all along. They now generate to\n.kiro/skills/<name>/SKILL.md with `name` + `description` frontmatter, so Kiro\ncan match a request against the description and invoke one on its own; `/spike`\ninvokes by hand. The old manual-inclusion steering files only ever supported\n`#skill-<name>`, and are removed on install so the two mechanisms can''t sit\nside by side describing the same chain.\n\nskillDescription() moves to src/util/skill-meta.ts, shared with the Claude Code\nadapter (caps differ: 500 vs Kiro''s 1024). Both platforms match a request\nagainst this text to decide whether to invoke, so it has to be the real trigger\nprose rather than the `# Title` — keeping one implementation stops the two\ndrifting, same reasoning as agent-meta.ts.\n\nDocs: README status line, preserved/overwritten table, and the walkthrough''s\nplatform table all move from `#skill-<name>` to `/<name>`.\n\nNot done in this phase, and neither is merely deferred bookkeeping:\n\n- Codex PreToolUse (replacing the post-run git-diff check). Codex does have\n  lifecycle hooks with the same event schema now, but it edits through\n  `apply_patch` and its PreToolUse payload carries `tool_input.command` — the\n  patch text — not a file path, and the docs state there is no documented way\n  for a hook to learn which paths a call will write. The shared guard reads\n  `tool_input.file_path`, which Codex never sends, so wiring it would be a\n  silent no-op: docs claiming enforced over nothing enforced. Observing the git\n  tree after the fact is the mechanism that fits this platform. Recorded in the\n  README so nobody re-proposes it.\n- Kiro .kiro/hooks/*.json and the agent `permissions` block. The hook config\n  shape is documented, but the exact trigger spelling, the STDIN payload and\n  the exit-code contract are not, and the permissions page 404s. Same silent\n  no-op risk, so not generated on a guess.\n\nTests: 175 (was 172).","tree":{"sha":"0fb17f410355d638acd0b857660137661d05fcfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/0fb17f410355d638acd0b857660137661d05fcfb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/6dfdfc814fd4bbea0b4817f391da37624be250aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/6dfdfc814fd4bbea0b4817f391da37624be250aa","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKDZkZmRmYzgxNGZkNGJiZWEwYjQ4MTdmMzkxZGEzNzYyNGJlMjUwYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/733c005b624506c848ad60a856d914c388592af9","sha":"733c005b624506c848ad60a856d914c388592af9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/733c005b624506c848ad60a856d914c388592af9"}],"sha":"6dfdfc814fd4bbea0b4817f391da37624be250aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/6dfdfc814fd4bbea0b4817f391da37624be250aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/733c005b624506c848ad60a856d914c388592af9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T03:48:39Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T03:48:39Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"feat(claude-code): opt-in Stop validation gate and SubagentStop recorder\n\nPath scoping was enforced mechanically; everything else was still prose. Every\nbuilder prompt says \"run the validation commands, do not return with failing\nchecks\", and nothing ever verified that — the Codex FACTORY.md admits as much.\nTwo lifecycle hooks close that, both off unless .factory.yaml asks: each\nchanges how a session behaves, which is not a change to make on a repo''s\nbehalf. Generated output is byte-identical until opted in, which the untouched\ngolden snapshot proves.\n\nstop-on-failing-validation (assets/factory-stop.mjs, Stop):\n\nRe-runs commands.typecheck / commands.test and exits 2 to refuse the stop when\nthey fail, so a builder cannot report green over a red suite. Stop fires at the\nend of *every* turn, so three guards keep it from trapping the session:\n\n- `stop_hook_active` short-circuits — a blocked stop can never loop.\n- A clean working tree exits before running anything.\n- The working-tree fingerprint is remembered, so a given state blocks once.\n  Asking a question in a repo with already-failing tests does not re-block.\n\nState lives in the OS temp dir keyed by repo path, so nothing is written to the\nrepo; a non-git checkout opts out on its own. The hook reads its commands from\na generated factory-stop.json — it cannot read .factory.yaml, which is the\nfactory''s format, not Claude''s.\n\ncapture-agent-output (assets/factory-capture.mjs, SubagentStop):\n\nWrites each agent''s last_assistant_message to .factory/runs/<session>/NN-<agent>.md.\nChain artifacts currently live only in the orchestrator''s context, so a run\ncannot be audited and every prior output has to be carried forward as inlined\ntext; this is the precondition for passing paths instead, and brings Claude\nCode to parity with Codex, which already tees each step into .codex/runs/.\nObserves only — every path exits 0, and ids are sanitised so a crafted\nsession_id cannot escape the runs directory.\n\nWiring: the three hook entries now go through one applyHook() that owns an\nentry by its script name, so a user''s own hook on the same event survives and\nours never duplicates. hookEntry() emits `matcher` before `hooks` to preserve\nthe key order every installed repo already has — reordering it would churn\nsettings.json everywhere for nothing (caught by the golden snapshot).\n\nDropped from this phase: a PostToolUse format/lint hook. The manifest has no\n`format` command, running `lint` after every edit is slow, and most repos\nalready have format-on-save or a pre-commit hook — it would add a slow,\nduplicative step.\n\nNot wired for Kiro or Codex yet, though both now have an equivalent seam\n(.kiro/hooks/*.json, lifecycle hooks in config.toml). Noted in the README for\nthe platform-parity pass.\n\nTests: 172 (was 158).","tree":{"sha":"307dee6d5060ea69a1cb56292f6902cc1339fb99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/307dee6d5060ea69a1cb56292f6902cc1339fb99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/733c005b624506c848ad60a856d914c388592af9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/733c005b624506c848ad60a856d914c388592af9","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKDczM2MwMDViNjI0NTA2Yzg0OGFkNjBhODU2ZDkxNGMzODg1OTJhZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/967f5d6220bd541ba91ad7d70bf03b0f0d1ad6bc","sha":"967f5d6220bd541ba91ad7d70bf03b0f0d1ad6bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/967f5d6220bd541ba91ad7d70bf03b0f0d1ad6bc"}],"sha":"733c005b624506c848ad60a856d914c388592af9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/733c005b624506c848ad60a856d914c388592af9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/967f5d6220bd541ba91ad7d70bf03b0f0d1ad6bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T03:40:28Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T03:40:28Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"feat: permissions.deny from forbidden, and optional per-agent models\n\nTwo of the three layers the platforms converged on were under-used: the\nmanifest''s `forbidden:` list only ever became a PreToolUse hook, and every\nagent ran on one model tier.\n\npermissions.deny (layer 2, Claude Code):\n\nThe hook fires on the edit tools only, so a file written through Bash never\nreached it. Each forbidden glob is now also emitted as a `permissions.deny`\nrule, merged into .claude/settings.json beside the hook. The two layers catch\ndifferent things — the hook enforces per-agent allow-lists (permission rules\nare session-wide and cannot express those), while the deny rule also covers the\nfile commands Claude Code recognises inside Bash: tee, sed, `> file` redirects.\n\nMapping decisions, all load-bearing:\n\n- `Edit(...)`, never `Write(...)`. Claude Code consults file-path rules for\n  Read and Edit only; a path rule on Write/NotebookEdit/MultiEdit is accepted,\n  never checked, and warns at startup.\n- No matching `Read(...)` rule. `forbidden:` declares \"no agent may edit\", not\n  \"may not read\", and denying reads of `.env*` would also hide `.env.example`.\n- No glob translation: both use gitignore semantics, where a bare filename\n  matches at any depth.\n\nOn re-install the previous `forbidden:` list is read back from\nfactory-scope.json before it is overwritten, and only rules derived from it are\npruned — a shrunk or renamed list cleans up after itself, and the user''s own\nallow / ask / deny rules are never touched. mergeGuardIntoSettings and\nremoveGuardFromSettings collapse into one updateSettings.\n\nStill not a sandbox: a Node or Python script the agent runs opens files itself,\nwhich neither layer sees. README points at Claude Code''s OS-level sandbox.\n\nmodels (optional, Claude Code + Kiro CLI):\n\nNew optional `models:` map (agent name -> model), emitted as `model:` in agent\nfrontmatter and `model` in Kiro CLI agent configs. No defaults ship: which\nagent deserves which model is a quality judgement belonging to the repo owner,\nand a wrong default would quietly degrade every repo on the next sync. An agent\nthe manifest doesn''t name gets no `model` key and follows the session default —\nthe golden snapshot is untouched by this, which is the proof. The README\nsuggests a starting point rather than imposing one.\n\nCodex is deliberately not wired up for models: it selects per invocation\n(`codex exec --model`) rather than declaratively, so it needs the orchestrator\nscripts to carry the map. Noted in the README as not done.\n\nDropped from this phase after a closer look: `disallowedTools` is redundant\nagainst the explicit `tools:` allowlist each agent already gets, and `maxTurns`\nfails by returning partial output — a builder truncated mid-edit leaves a\nhalf-written feature, which is worse than a long run.\n\nTests: 158 (was 145).","tree":{"sha":"bbccd32cba0b41d6873fde36a3bf7b3d559a6229","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/bbccd32cba0b41d6873fde36a3bf7b3d559a6229"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/967f5d6220bd541ba91ad7d70bf03b0f0d1ad6bc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/967f5d6220bd541ba91ad7d70bf03b0f0d1ad6bc","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKDk2N2Y1ZDYyMjBiZDU0MWJhOTFhZDdkNzBiZjAzYjBmMGQxYWQ2YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/2c6e5fe4b68e7107c4764630ab1c5792e7c1a38c","sha":"2c6e5fe4b68e7107c4764630ab1c5792e7c1a38c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/2c6e5fe4b68e7107c4764630ab1c5792e7c1a38c"}],"sha":"967f5d6220bd541ba91ad7d70bf03b0f0d1ad6bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/967f5d6220bd541ba91ad7d70bf03b0f0d1ad6bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/2c6e5fe4b68e7107c4764630ab1c5792e7c1a38c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T03:31:25Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T03:31:25Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"ci: add CI and golden snapshots for generated output\n\nNothing guarded this repo''s output. The suite asserted behaviour (\"a hook block\nis present\", \"the count is N\") but never the bytes, and there was no CI at all\n— a poor fit for a tool whose files are copied verbatim into every consuming\nrepo, where an adapter regression would ship on the next `factory install` with\nnothing to catch it. Ironic too, since the factory scopes devops-builder to\n.github/workflows/** and had none of its own.\n\nCI (.github/workflows/ci.yml):\n\n- corepack -> setup-node 20 -> pnpm install --frozen-lockfile -> typecheck -> test.\n- corepack runs before setup-node so the pinned pnpm is on PATH for its cache.\n- --frozen-lockfile so a drifted package.json fails the build instead of being\n  silently resolved around.\n\nGolden snapshots (test/golden.test.ts), deliberately split in two:\n\n- file tree — real prompts, paths only. Catches a generated file appearing,\n  disappearing or being renamed. Editing a prompt does not churn it.\n- composed output — synthetic minimal agents/skills/profile, full contents.\n  Shows what each adapter wraps around a body (frontmatter, headings, ordering)\n  without dragging 1,900 lines of real prompt across three platforms. 934 lines,\n  readable in a diff.\n\nCopied assets (factory-guard.mjs x2, factory-check.mjs) are elided from the\ncontent snapshot — including them would show every guard fix three times — and\npinned instead by a byte-identity assertion against assets/, so a stale copy in\nan adapter cannot drift unnoticed.\n\nVerified the snapshots actually bite: adding a single trailing space to the\n`tools:` frontmatter line in claude-code.ts fails the content snapshot. Output\nconfirmed deterministic across repeated runs (no temp paths, no timestamps).\n\nTests: 145 (was 142).","tree":{"sha":"251943222122fe8b8a4bd9049f86c361e92b3deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/251943222122fe8b8a4bd9049f86c361e92b3deb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/2c6e5fe4b68e7107c4764630ab1c5792e7c1a38c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/2c6e5fe4b68e7107c4764630ab1c5792e7c1a38c","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKDJjNmU1ZmU0YjY4ZTcxMDdjNDc2NDYzMGFiMWM1NzkyZTdjMWEzOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/de4c3db69fe60a7e12fb55123ae63ad79cb1406c","sha":"de4c3db69fe60a7e12fb55123ae63ad79cb1406c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/de4c3db69fe60a7e12fb55123ae63ad79cb1406c"}],"sha":"2c6e5fe4b68e7107c4764630ab1c5792e7c1a38c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/2c6e5fe4b68e7107c4764630ab1c5792e7c1a38c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/de4c3db69fe60a7e12fb55123ae63ad79cb1406c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T03:27:14Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T03:27:14Z","email":"234321795+bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"fix(guard): resolve symlinks before matching path globs\n\nresolve() is purely lexical, so a symlink sitting inside an allowed directory\nwas matched by its link path and sailed past the forbidden list. Verified hole:\nwith backend-builder scoped to src/**, a write to src/services/leak.ts where\nthat file is a symlink to ../../.env returned exit 0 — the guard allowed an\nedit to a forbidden file. \"Enforced\" path scoping has to mean the real target.\n\n- assets/factory-guard.mjs: add realPath(), which realpathSync()es the target\n  and, when it doesn''t exist yet (the normal case for a Write), falls back to\n  the deepest existing ancestor and re-appends the remaining segments.\n- Both sides of relative() now go through realPath: on macOS /tmp and /var are\n  themselves symlinks, so resolving only one side yields a bogus ''../..'' path.\n- The block message now names the resolved target (\".env\", not \"leak.ts\").\n- tests: 3 regression cases — symlinked file to a forbidden target, symlinked\n  directory widening an allow-list (target not yet created), and a plain path\n  that must still pass.\n\nDocs corrected in the same pass (the README lagged the code, the book didn''t):\n\n- README: \"Kiro and Codex have no hook mechanism, so they remain prompt-only\"\n  was contradicted by the last two feature commits. Replaced with an \"Enforced\n  path scoping (Kiro CLI and Codex)\" section — per-platform mechanism table\n  (block-before-the-edit on Claude Code and Kiro CLI, revert-after on Codex),\n  the Kiro IDE caveat, and a pointer to book ch. 04. Phase B status lines now\n  name .kiro/agents/*.json and .codex/factory-check.mjs.\n- README: \"Default paths/commands are reference documentation only — not\n  parsed\" was half wrong. factory init does parse them\n  (src/util/profile-defaults.ts); only install ignores them. Spelled out, with\n  the two consequences: editing a profile''s defaults changes nothing in repos\n  that already have a manifest, and a path key the profile suggests but the\n  manifest omits is not enforced.\n- walkthrough: split the Kiro bullet — enforced on the CLI, prompt-only in the IDE.\n- package.json: pin pnpm via packageManager (added by pnpm install). vitest was\n  listed in devDependencies but missing from the checkout, so all 11 suites\n  were dormant; they run again.\n\nNote: assets/factory-check.mjs (Codex) has an analogous blind spot of a\ndifferent shape — it reads git-reported paths, so a write through a symlink to\na gitignored file is never reported. Left alone deliberately: that is inherent\nto the git-diff approach, and moving Codex to a PreToolUse hook on the shared\nguard removes it structurally.\n\nTests: 142 (was 139).","tree":{"sha":"cd168ea46a2d71623caf476c0843e99fd359dc9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/cd168ea46a2d71623caf476c0843e99fd359dc9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/de4c3db69fe60a7e12fb55123ae63ad79cb1406c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/de4c3db69fe60a7e12fb55123ae63ad79cb1406c","node_id":"C_kwDOSqPMatoAKGRlNGMzZGI2OWZlNjBhN2UxMmZiNTUxMjNhZTYzYWQ3OWNiMTQwNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commit/cf33d3a1ecd18b4a07985b9d5dc7a1b170338b10","sha":"cf33d3a1ecd18b4a07985b9d5dc7a1b170338b10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/cf33d3a1ecd18b4a07985b9d5dc7a1b170338b10"}],"sha":"de4c3db69fe60a7e12fb55123ae63ad79cb1406c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/de4c3db69fe60a7e12fb55123ae63ad79cb1406c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234321795?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bejono17","id":234321795,"login":"bejono17","node_id":"U_kgDODfd3gw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bejono17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/commits/cf33d3a1ecd18b4a07985b9d5dc7a1b170338b10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T07:36:33Z","email":"bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T07:36:33Z","email":"bejono17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bejono17"},"message":"refactor: remove unimplemented Cursor/Windsurf adapters\n\nThey were throwing stubs, and unlike the live platforms they can''t be verified\nhere (tools not installed) and have no enforcement seam — Cursor (.cursor/rules/*.mdc)\nand Windsurf (.windsurf/rules + workflows) are context-injection formats, so any\nadapter would be prompt-only. Keeping throwing stubs made the \"5 platforms\" claim\nan over-claim. Removed for an honest 3-platform tool (Claude Code, Kiro, Codex —\nall with enforced path scoping).\n\n- delete src/platforms/cursor.ts + windsurf.ts; drop from the registry, the\n  Platform union, and validPlatforms; simplify the init wizard (no stub handling).\n- tests: drop the stub-throws block; add a \"registry exposes exactly the three\n  platforms\" assertion.\n- README + book (00/01/05/08/09) + example manifest + walkthrough: correct the\n  platform list, and rewrite extension Recipe B as \"add a new platform adapter\"\n  (with the honest note on why Cursor/Windsurf aren''t shipped + how to add one).\n\nTests: 139 (cursor now rejected up front with a clear validation error).","tree":{"sha":"c5b8dec2a8724a7e073a904d83c0541354ae6c5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/trees/c5b8dec2a8724a7e073a904d83c0541354ae6c5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dewantrie/ai-software-factory/git/commits/cf33d3a1ecd18b4a07985b9d5dc7a1b170338b10","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned