d.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"chore: MIT license, package metadata, pnpm build approvals\n\n- Add LICENSE (MIT, 2026 Sergio Carrero) and license/repository fields\n- Pin packageManager to pnpm@11.24.0 so CI matches the lockfile\n- Move build-script approvals to pnpm-workspace.yaml (esbuild needs its\n  postinstall; spawn-sync does not) so a clean install exits 0\n- Add vitest / @vitest/coverage-v8 / jsdom dev dependencies and\n  test scripts; ignore coverage/\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3142003586610b4f36a63d67cfa87d3799700a68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/3142003586610b4f36a63d67cfa87d3799700a68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/bb19a0fc1340c1ff05eb9c4a073eda968a703329","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/bb19a0fc1340c1ff05eb9c4a073eda968a703329","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGJiMTlhMGZjMTM0MGMxZmYwNWViOWM0YTA3M2VkYTk2OGE3MDMzMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/ea535fe7295046a2f08adc600060775a3fdff314","sha":"ea535fe7295046a2f08adc600060775a3fdff314","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/ea535fe7295046a2f08adc600060775a3fdff314"}],"sha":"bb19a0fc1340c1ff05eb9c4a073eda968a703329","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/bb19a0fc1340c1ff05eb9c4a073eda968a703329"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/ea535fe7295046a2f08adc600060775a3fdff314/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T17:18:53Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T17:18:53Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"docs: comprehensive documentation suite for v0.3.21\n\nAdds full project documentation to the private repo:\n\n- README.md — rewritten for v0.3.21: 7-tab feature matrix, correct\n  tech stack (prism-react-renderer, @jridgewell/sourcemap-codec),\n  docs index, quick start.\n\n- CHANGELOG.md — version history from v0.1.0 through v0.3.21 with\n  per-release Added/Changed/Fixed entries.\n\n- docs/architecture.md — execution context map, entrypoint\n  responsibilities, full message protocol, capture flow, LLM proxy\n  design, sourcemap pipeline, session memory, CSP constraints, and\n  design decision rationale.\n\n- docs/modules-reference.md — every lib/ module documented: exports,\n  types, key functions, and notes on why they exist.\n\n- docs/runbooks/dev-setup.md — prereqs, install, build, load, hot\n  reload, project layout, common tasks, debugging tips.\n\n- docs/runbooks/ai-setup.md — LM Studio, Ollama, and llama.cpp setup\n  with model recommendations per task type.\n\n- docs/runbooks/mf-demo.md — MF demo host/remote startup, three\n  sourcemap modes (normal / NOSOURCES=1 / SOURCEMAPS=0), GitHub\n  mapping config, Modules tab walkthrough.\n\n- docs/runbooks/github-mappings.md — how mappings work, field\n  reference, {version} templating, common configs, troubleshooting.\n\n- docs/runbooks/troubleshooting.md — 15 failure modes: missing\n  DevTools tab, main-world script absent, empty Components tree,\n  sourcemap errors, AI connectivity, Mermaid parse errors, HTML\n  artifact blank, session memory not propagating, and more.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8b8f29035826955d08e9727f806a67464d074380","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/8b8f29035826955d08e9727f806a67464d074380"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/ea535fe7295046a2f08adc600060775a3fdff314","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/ea535fe7295046a2f08adc600060775a3fdff314","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGVhNTM1ZmU3Mjk1MDQ2YTJmMDhhZGM2MDAwNjA3NzVhM2ZkZmYzMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/bd286f2fa212ecde70cdca8be46f0091b1b07438","sha":"bd286f2fa212ecde70cdca8be46f0091b1b07438","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/bd286f2fa212ecde70cdca8be46f0091b1b07438"}],"sha":"ea535fe7295046a2f08adc600060775a3fdff314","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/ea535fe7295046a2f08adc600060775a3fdff314"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/bd286f2fa212ecde70cdca8be46f0091b1b07438/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T23:04:07Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T23:04:07Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.21: per-page session memory for UX-vision analyses\n\nNew cumulative-context layer: each analysis can be saved to memory,\nand subsequent analyses on the same page can fold the saved insights\nback into the prompt. Unlocks the workflow the user described:\n\n  1. Run Aesthetics & Branding on the whole page root.\n  2. 💾 Save to memory.\n  3. Pick a smaller region (a card, a hero, a CTA).\n  4. Run Layout & Composition with memory included.\n  5. The model now grounds the smaller analysis in the page-level\n     principles already established.\n  6. Ask \"suggest 3 alternative layouts that align with this page''s\n     principles\" — memory makes the constraint explicit.\n\nMemory model (lib/memory/sessionMemory.ts):\n\n  - Per-page keyed by pageKey(url) = origin + pathname. Different\n    routes on the same SPA only share memory when they''re on the\n    same pathname.\n  - In-memory only — no chrome.storage write. Survives multiple\n    captures of the same page within the DevTools session; cleared\n    explicitly via the toolbar.\n  - Per-entry hard ceiling 6 KB, total budget 24 KB. New entries\n    that would push over the budget evict oldest first (FIFO).\n  - addMemoryEntry / removeMemoryEntry / clearMemory live on the\n    Zustand store keyed by pageKey for easy lookup.\n\nPrompt integration (lib/components/uxVisionPrompts.ts):\n\n  - buildUxVisionPayload accepts memoryEntries[].\n  - When non-empty, the user message gains a `## Memory from prior\n    analyses on this page` section at the very top with one `###`\n    heading per entry (labelled with the original action + the\n    component it was scoped to).\n  - System prompt instruction: \"Reference them by their headings\n    when relevant; do not just re-state them.\" Avoids the model\n    parroting memory back verbatim.\n  - describeInputs surfaces \"📚 Memory: N entries (X KB) included\"\n    so the analysis tab''s Context-sent panel shows it explicitly.\n\nComponentsTab UI:\n\n  - New memory toolbar above the preset buttons:\n      📚 Memory: N entries · X.X KB    [✓ Include] [view] [clear]\n      [progress bar showing % of total budget]\n  - Include toggle defaults to on; disabled when memory is empty.\n  - \"view\" expands a list showing each entry''s label, icon,\n    component scope, and KB. Per-entry × removes.\n  - \"clear\" wipes memory for this page.\n  - In every analysis tab header (right side):\n      [💾 Save to memory]  → becomes [📚 In memory] once saved.\n    Disabled while the analysis is still streaming.\n\nWhen an analysis runs with memory included, the tab''s \"Context sent\nto model\" panel lists \"📚 Memory: N entries (X KB) included\" so the\nuser can verify exactly what the model received.\n\nBundle stayed at 4.10 MB. Version bumped to 0.3.21.","tree":{"sha":"3fbc8cc727e4898f3882624e867dbb7d216a3a3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/3fbc8cc727e4898f3882624e867dbb7d216a3a3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/bd286f2fa212ecde70cdca8be46f0091b1b07438","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/bd286f2fa212ecde70cdca8be46f0091b1b07438","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGJkMjg2ZjJmYTIxMmVjZGU3MGNkY2E4YmU0NmYwMDkxYjFiMDc0Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/062d283752ec0458feec561f48355ece65902a23","sha":"062d283752ec0458feec561f48355ece65902a23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/062d283752ec0458feec561f48355ece65902a23"}],"sha":"bd286f2fa212ecde70cdca8be46f0091b1b07438","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/bd286f2fa212ecde70cdca8be46f0091b1b07438"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/062d283752ec0458feec561f48355ece65902a23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T22:41:53Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T22:41:53Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.20: Components tab — Tree rename, keep-mounted fix, DOM context\n\nFixes\n   - Sub-tab \"Components\" renamed to \"Tree\". The double-Components\n     label was redundant — the outer tab already says Components.\n   - Tree no longer shrinks after switching back from an analysis\n     tab. Switching away used to unmount the tree body, which killed\n     the react-arborist ResizeObserver''s measurement; when the body\n     remounted, the tree rendered at the placeholder 600×600 inside\n     a small inner div until the next resize event fired. Now the\n     tree body stays mounted at all times (hidden via display:none\n     when an analysis tab is active) so the observer keeps a live\n     measurement.\n\nFeature: DOM context in every UX-vision request\n\n   Each preset now ships the actual DOM context alongside the cropped\n   image — what the page is ACTUALLY built from, not just what it\n   looks like. The model can cite class names, font stacks, palette\n   tokens, etc. directly.\n\n   New MAIN-world inspectAtBounds(x, y, w, h):\n     - elementFromPoint at the bounds centre, walked up to the\n       smallest ancestor whose rect covers ≥60% of the requested\n       area (elementFromPoint often lands on a leaf span; we want\n       the surrounding card).\n     - outerHTML (truncated to 4 KB, marker comment on truncation)\n     - attributes (excluding style/class/id; truncated values)\n     - 25 key computed style properties (display/position/\n       background/font/spacing/border/shadow/transform/etc),\n       filtered to non-default values.\n     - CSS rules whose selector matches via el.matches(). Walks\n       document.styleSheets, wrapping cssRules access in try/catch\n       to survive cross-origin sheets. Caps at 30 rules / 8 000\n       rules scanned.\n     - Returns counters: rulesScanned, sheetsAccessible,\n       sheetsBlocked — used by the panel UI to tell the user when\n       CORS blocked context.\n\n   Panel-side callInspectAtBounds + threading:\n     - ComponentsTab calls it after scroll-into-view, before crop.\n     - buildUxVisionPayload accepts an optional `domContext` and\n       emits a `## DOM context` block in the user message: element\n       identity + outerHTML + computed styles + matching CSS rules.\n     - When the context is null (cross-origin, off-screen, no\n       match) the prompt falls through cleanly — the image still\n       lands.\n\n   New \"Context sent to model\" panel in every analysis tab:\n     - Crop preview (max 240×160, clickable to open full size in\n       a new tab)\n     - Bulleted summary: selected component name + kind, visible\n       region size, image bytes + dims, DOM element identity,\n       outerHTML char count, computed-style count, matching-rule\n       count, CORS-blocked sheet count (when any).\n     - Collapsible details (open by default).\n\nBundle now 4.10 MB (was 4.09). Version bumped to 0.3.20.","tree":{"sha":"570a4fe96b6a0cb20b16f0a469359e7d25827356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/570a4fe96b6a0cb20b16f0a469359e7d25827356"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/062d283752ec0458feec561f48355ece65902a23","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/062d283752ec0458feec561f48355ece65902a23","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDA2MmQyODM3NTJlYzA0NThmZWVjNTYxZjQ4MzU1ZWNlNjU5MDJhMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/2e87fc8649ce499c85e7a7a62431624b185edcb0","sha":"2e87fc8649ce499c85e7a7a62431624b185edcb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/2e87fc8649ce499c85e7a7a62431624b185edcb0"}],"sha":"062d283752ec0458feec561f48355ece65902a23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/062d283752ec0458feec561f48355ece65902a23"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/2e87fc8649ce499c85e7a7a62431624b185edcb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T22:20:04Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T22:20:04Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.19: Components tab — scroll-on-select + UX-vision analyses (tabs)\n\nComponents tab gets two big upgrades.\n\n1) Auto-scroll on tree select\n   The highlight overlay was already painted at the selected fiber''s\n   document-coord bounds. But if those bounds were below the fold the\n   user just saw a blank scroll position. New MAIN-world\n   `scrollToBounds(x, y, w, h)` centers the rect in the viewport.\n   ComponentsTab calls it inside onSelect whenever a row with bounds\n   is picked — same path that updates `focused` and paints the\n   overlay. Falls back through the v0.3.4 reliableScrollTo so\n   scroll-locked / inner-scroll pages don''t no-op silently.\n\n2) UX-vision analyses — 9 presets + custom\n   Picking a component → \"Analyze region with AI\" pane appears in\n   the selection sidebar. Each button crops the selected region from\n   the snapshot screenshot (cropRegion uses document-coord bounds +\n   DPR to map to image pixels, 16px pad), wraps it in a\n   senior-UX-pro system prompt, and streams the result into a new\n   tab via the existing streamingOneshot proxy.\n\n   Tab container pattern matches the v0.3.17 ModuleAnalysis +\n   FileDetail layout: a permanent \"Components\" tab + one tab per\n   analysis, badge dot on the label (streaming = sky pulsing,\n   done = emerald, error = red), close to fall back.\n\n   Presets (lib/components/uxVisionPrompts.ts):\n     - 🔍 UX audit          comprehensive Nielsen-style review\n     - 🎨 Aesthetics & branding  palette / type / brand voice / 3 references\n     - 📐 Layout & composition   grid, rhythm, balance, alignment\n     - 🎯 Usability          affordances, friction, primary task\n     - ♿ Accessibility      visible WCAG concerns + needs-code-check list\n     - 💖 Engagement         attention anchors, persuasion, dark-pattern risk\n     - ✨ Wow factor         the one distinguishing detail (or its absence)\n     - 🔭 Design trends      where it sits in 2026; Mermaid trend graph\n     - 📊 Market & tech      comparable products, likely stack, market position\n\n   Same preset = same id = replaces tab (no duplicates).\n   Custom prompt → id derived from the prompt text (slugified first\n   60 chars). Different wording → new tab, naturally providing\n   \"history\" for variations of the same question.\n\n   All results render through MarkdownRenderer so any ```mermaid or\n   ```html the model emits auto-renders (and gets the v0.3.18 Heal/\n   Refine affordance for free).\n\nSupporting work:\n   - injected.content.ts gains scrollToBounds + matching\n     callScrollToBounds wrapper in useInspectedEval.\n   - lib/snapshot/cropRegion.ts — clips bounds to the screenshot\n     extent, maps doc-coords to pixels via DPR, paints to a hidden\n     canvas, returns dataURL.\n   - The action pane is gated: hidden when there''s no LLM\n     configured, no screenshot in the snapshot, or no bounds on the\n     selected fiber. Clear copy explains each missing prerequisite.\n\nBundle now 4.09 MB (was 4.07). Version bumped to 0.3.19.","tree":{"sha":"cc3a11347e5f8a4f6d4120d4b02ddb5baa60736d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/cc3a11347e5f8a4f6d4120d4b02ddb5baa60736d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/2e87fc8649ce499c85e7a7a62431624b185edcb0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/2e87fc8649ce499c85e7a7a62431624b185edcb0","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDJlODdmYzg2NDljZTQ5OWM4NWU3YTdhNjI0MzE2MjRiMTg1ZWRjYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/6a9c745000d9f56a03d8800c5edbdc8cf0c64f38","sha":"6a9c745000d9f56a03d8800c5edbdc8cf0c64f38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/6a9c745000d9f56a03d8800c5edbdc8cf0c64f38"}],"sha":"2e87fc8649ce499c85e7a7a62431624b185edcb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/2e87fc8649ce499c85e7a7a62431624b185edcb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/6a9c745000d9f56a03d8800c5edbdc8cf0c64f38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T22:07:51Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T22:07:51Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.18: Heal-with-AI on Mermaid + Refine-with-AI on Artifacts\n\nBlock-level retry affordances so a single bad diagram or artifact\ndoesn''t waste a full analysis run.\n\nMermaidBlock — Heal-with-AI on parse error\n   When the diagram fails to render (lexer error, expecting NL got\n   NODE_STRING, etc.), the error box gains a \"✨ Heal with AI\"\n   button. Clicking it sends:\n     - the broken Mermaid source,\n     - the parser''s error message,\n     - the full MERMAID_RULES block,\n   to the local LLM. The streamed reply is parsed for a ```mermaid\n   fence, which becomes the block''s new source (kept as a local\n   override so the parent reply never sees the change). Live\n   streaming progress is shown inside the error panel — the user\n   sees the model thinking instead of staring at a \"Healing…\"\n   spinner.\n\n   The override resets when the parent passes a new source, so\n   regenerating from upstream replaces it cleanly.\n\nArtifactBlock — Refine-with-AI (always-available)\n   HTML artifacts don''t have a clean \"this is broken\" signal — the\n   iframe always renders something. So the heal pattern there is\n   different: a \"✨ Refine\" toolbar button that''s always available\n   (when an LLM is configured and streaming is done). Clicking it\n   opens an inline textarea where the user can describe the\n   refinement (or leave it blank to \"fix obvious issues\"). Submit\n   sends:\n     - the current artifact source,\n     - the user''s hint (or a generic \"improve readability + fix\n       any obvious issues\" prompt),\n     - the full ARTIFACT_RULES block.\n\n   Result extracted from the ```html fence becomes the new source.\n   Streaming progress shown inline.\n\nSupporting infrastructure:\n\n   - lib/lm-studio/LlmContext.tsx\n       React Context exposing the streamingOneshot proxy to any\n       descendant. App.tsx wraps the panel root in LlmProvider so\n       blocks rendered deep inside MarkdownRenderer can call the LLM\n       without prop drilling.\n\n   - lib/ui/healPrompts.ts\n       buildMermaidHealPayload + buildArtifactRefinePayload + a\n       small extractFenced helper that pulls the relevant block out\n       of the response (tolerates preamble even though we say \"no\n       preamble\" in the system message).\n\n   System messages keep the temperature low (0 for heal, 0.1 for\n   blank-hint refine, 0.3 when user provides intent) and instruct\n   the model to preserve the INTENT — only fix what''s wrong, don''t\n   redesign.\n\nBoth surfaces are non-destructive: the prop source is the source of\ntruth, the local override is just a layer on top. Closing the chat\ntab, re-running an analysis, etc. all reset correctly.\n\nBundle stayed at 4.07 MB — context + prompts add ~3 KB. Version\nbumped to 0.3.18.","tree":{"sha":"9ecaac31e1677339bdc49764fbc1526f24105f1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/9ecaac31e1677339bdc49764fbc1526f24105f1e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/6a9c745000d9f56a03d8800c5edbdc8cf0c64f38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/6a9c745000d9f56a03d8800c5edbdc8cf0c64f38","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDZhOWM3NDUwMDBkOWY1NmEwM2Q4ODAwYzVlZGJkYzhjZjBjNjRmMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/dae25e618e816f8ebe47ff01c491016faf77f4dc","sha":"dae25e618e816f8ebe47ff01c491016faf77f4dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/dae25e618e816f8ebe47ff01c491016faf77f4dc"}],"sha":"6a9c745000d9f56a03d8800c5edbdc8cf0c64f38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/6a9c745000d9f56a03d8800c5edbdc8cf0c64f38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/dae25e618e816f8ebe47ff01c491016faf77f4dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:43:46Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:43:46Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.17: tabs in FileDetail + ModuleAnalysis + Propose-changes flow\n\nThree fixes + one new feature, all in the Modules tab''s right pane.\n\nFix 1) Flicker during streaming analyses\n   The MarkdownRenderer''s `streaming` prop was already implemented\n   in v0.3.1 for the Analyze tab — it suppresses MermaidBlock and\n   ArtifactBlock lexer errors mid-stream so partial fences don''t\n   re-render as broken output every delta. FileDetail and\n   ModuleAnalysis weren''t passing it. Now they do, with the same\n   pattern: `streaming={result.state === ''streaming''}` plus a\n   ▍ caret next to the running text.\n\nFix 2) Tabbed FileDetail layout\n   The result panel was a strip below the source code and felt\n   cramped. Source code + each analysis now live in dedicated tabs,\n   each getting the full vertical pane.\n\n     - Source tab is permanent (📄 Source).\n     - Audit / Improve / Explain runs add a tab. Running the SAME\n       action again replaces the existing tab — no duplicates.\n     - Each tab has a × close affordance; closing falls back to\n       Source.\n     - Each tab gets a small badge dot to the right of the label\n       (streaming = sky pulsing, done = emerald, error = red) so\n       in-flight or failed analyses are visible without switching.\n\nFix 3) Tabbed ModuleAnalysis layout\n   Same pattern as FileDetail. The Summary tab (📊 Summary) is\n   permanent and keeps the stats grid + \"Files that will be sent\"\n   + \"Full file list\" collapsibles. Architecture / Dashboard /\n   Risk / Optimize / Diagram / Ideas each add a tab; same action\n   replaces.\n\nFeature) \"🔧 Propose changes\" flow\n\n   New action on both the file and module surfaces that drafts a\n   structured change plan and hands it off to an AI coding agent\n   or to GitHub. Why a plan and not a direct push:\n\n     - Pushing from the browser would need a stored PAT — a real\n       security surface inside a Chrome extension. Plans are\n       inert markdown.\n     - The agents we hand the plan to (Cursor, Claude Desktop,\n       Claude Code, Claude.ai web) are already the right tool for\n       the actual edits. The browser''s job is to gather context\n       (deployed module URL + sourcemap + GitHub mapping) and\n       structure a brief.\n     - Plans grow naturally — review by a human, paste into an\n       agent, open as a GitHub issue, attach to a discussion.\n       Pushing locks you into one workflow.\n\n   lib/modules/proposePr.ts — buildProposePrPayload for both\n   `file` and `module` scopes. The system prompt asks for a strict\n   markdown structure (Title / Rationale / Files to change /\n   Changes per file with optional diff blocks / Acceptance\n   criteria / Open questions / Implement-this prompt) so the\n   output is directly handoffable.\n\n   The Propose tab has a textarea for the user''s intent + a\n   \"Generate plan\" button. When intent is blank, the latest\n   matching analysis (Improve/Audit/Explain for files, Risk/\n   Optimization/Ideas/Architecture for modules) is folded in as\n   grounding context.\n\n   Hand-off targets (each opens in a new tab via window.open):\n     - 📋 Copy plan — clipboard\n     - ⬇ Download .md — local file\n     - 🤖 Open in Cursor — cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/prompt?text=…\n     - 🟣 Claude Desktop — claude://claude.ai/new?q=…\n     - 🌐 Claude.ai — https://claude.ai/new?q=…\n     - 🐙 GitHub issue — github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/new?title=&body=\n                          (only shown when a mapping resolves)\n\n   Payload is capped at 8 KB per deeplink target (Claude truncates\n   at ~14 KB, Chrome URL dispatch chokes around 30 KB). Full plan\n   is always available via Copy / Download.\n\n   AnalysisPane tabs that support proposing (Improve/Audit for\n   files; Risk/Optimization/Ideas for modules) get an inline\n   \"🔧 Propose changes from this <action>\" button at the bottom\n   that seeds the propose intent with the analysis''s result and\n   auto-runs the proposal.\n\nSupporting infrastructure:\n\n   - lib/ui/Tabs.tsx — generic horizontal tab strip + body slot.\n     Stateless (parent owns activeId). Tabs accept icon, label,\n     badge, closable.\n   - lib/modules/proposePr.ts — prompt + export-target registry.\n     Each target builds a URL or runs an action; the panel renders\n     buttons + dispatches.\n\nVerified end-to-end against the MF demo (host + remote on\nlocalhost:3001 / 3002 with ingscarrero/dom-lens-mf-host and\ndom-lens-mf-remote mapped). All four Cursor / Claude / GitHub\ndeeplinks open correctly with the plan pre-filled.\n\nBundle now 4.07 MB (was 4.05 MB). Version bumped to 0.3.17.","tree":{"sha":"ac7dd8f48a10667e724a9e9d46a124f3056bab32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/ac7dd8f48a10667e724a9e9d46a124f3056bab32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/dae25e618e816f8ebe47ff01c491016faf77f4dc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/dae25e618e816f8ebe47ff01c491016faf77f4dc","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGRhZTI1ZTYxOGU4MTZmOGViZTQ3ZmYwMWM0OTEwMTZmYWY3N2Y0ZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/d71a7f66623664c24c865d91db578b78808c591b","sha":"d71a7f66623664c24c865d91db578b78808c591b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d71a7f66623664c24c865d91db578b78808c591b"}],"sha":"dae25e618e816f8ebe47ff01c491016faf77f4dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/dae25e618e816f8ebe47ff01c491016faf77f4dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d71a7f66623664c24c865d91db578b78808c591b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:08:31Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:08:31Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"mf-demo: NOSOURCES=1 toggle for nosources-source-map mode\n\nAdds a third configuration mode to the demo so the v0.3.16 GitHub\nsource-fetch path can be tested end-to-end:\n\n  pnpm dev               → ''source-map''           (with sourcesContent)\n  NOSOURCES=1 pnpm dev   → ''nosources-source-map'' (without sourcesContent)\n  SOURCEMAPS=0 pnpm dev  → false                  (no .map at all)\n\nThe NOSOURCES=1 mode is the production scenario the GitHub mapping\nfeature was built for: the sourcemap resolves files but doesn''t\nembed source content, so the panel has to pull from GitHub to\nshow anything useful. With v0.3.16''s auto-default, FileDetail\nopens in 🐙 GitHub mode automatically in this case.\n\nREADME updated with a three-row table explaining each mode''s\nbehaviour in the Modules tab.","tree":{"sha":"ef470c5de26d4862f5f447e0ce674f430366eb1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/ef470c5de26d4862f5f447e0ce674f430366eb1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/d71a7f66623664c24c865d91db578b78808c591b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/d71a7f66623664c24c865d91db578b78808c591b","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGQ3MWE3ZjY2NjIzNjY0YzI0Yzg2NWQ5MWRiNTc4Yjc4ODA4YzU5MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/f3b299547c094cb128124b76c69f12cbd67882b3","sha":"f3b299547c094cb128124b76c69f12cbd67882b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/f3b299547c094cb128124b76c69f12cbd67882b3"}],"sha":"d71a7f66623664c24c865d91db578b78808c591b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d71a7f66623664c24c865d91db578b78808c591b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/f3b299547c094cb128124b76c69f12cbd67882b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:07:11Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:07:11Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.16: source mode toggle — fetch from GitHub instead of sourcemap\n\nCloses the loop on the GitHub mapping feature: the panel can now\nactually FETCH source content from GitHub''s raw endpoint, not just\nlink to it. Critical for the production case where the deployed\nbundle ships `nosources-source-map` (sourcemap for stack-trace\nsymbolication, no embedded source content).\n\nFileDetail gains:\n\n  - A \"Source: 📦 Sourcemap | 🐙 GitHub\" segmented control in the\n    action row. Visible whenever a GitHub mapping resolves AND the\n    parent passed `fetchText`.\n  - Status line next to the toggle:\n      \"fetching from raw.githubusercontent.com…\" (loading)\n      \"✓ live from <label>\"                       (success)\n      \"✗ <error message>\"                          (error)\n\n  - Automatic fallback: when the sourcemap''s sourcesContent is null\n    for this file AND a mapping resolves, the mode defaults to\n    GitHub. The user lands on real source instead of a \"no content\n    embedded\" placeholder.\n\n  - The fetch round-trip uses the existing `fetchText` proxy (so\n    background SW''s <all_urls> permission bypasses any CORS edge\n    cases — though raw.githubusercontent.com sends permissive CORS\n    anyway).\n\n  - Content is cached by request URL — selecting the same file\n    twice doesn''t re-fetch.\n\n  - When the fetch fails (404 / wrong branch / wrong path), a clear\n    error panel appears in the code area with the probed URL and a\n    \"Fall back to sourcemap content →\" escape hatch when local\n    content is available.\n\n  - File-level AI actions (Audit / Improve / Explain) operate on\n    whichever source is currently active, so analyses against the\n    GitHub copy work too.\n\n  - CodeViewer''s filename label switches between the sourcemap\n    path and the github.com/blob/... URL based on mode, so the\n    user always knows what they''re looking at.\n\nModulesTab now passes its existing `fetchText` proxy through to\nFileDetail. No new port message types needed.\n\nVerified against the live MF demo repos:\n  - github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens-mf-host (App.jsx, bootstrap.jsx)\n  - github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens-mf-remote (Widget.jsx, Counter.jsx)\nAll four raw.githubusercontent.com URLs return 200.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.16.","tree":{"sha":"df8fceee52f9c56885bb4000ee61cb15941e1a50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/df8fceee52f9c56885bb4000ee61cb15941e1a50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/f3b299547c094cb128124b76c69f12cbd67882b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/f3b299547c094cb128124b76c69f12cbd67882b3","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGYzYjI5OTU0N2MwOTRjYjEyODEyNGI3NmM2OWYxMmNiZDY3ODgyYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/b4b073a760a752c2dcc43749e9af9b2d5b578c55","sha":"b4b073a760a752c2dcc43749e9af9b2d5b578c55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/b4b073a760a752c2dcc43749e9af9b2d5b578c55"}],"sha":"f3b299547c094cb128124b76c69f12cbd67882b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/f3b299547c094cb128124b76c69f12cbd67882b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/b4b073a760a752c2dcc43749e9af9b2d5b578c55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:00:07Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:00:07Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.15: fix webpack://<namespace>/ + version-aware branches\n\nTwo real-world issues reported testing the v0.3.14 GitHub mappings on\nthe MF demo:\n\n  1. Clicking webpack:///src/App.jsx produced a broken GitHub URL\n     containing literal \"webpack:/mf-host/\" in the path.\n  2. No way to track per-version deployments (CDN URLs like\n     /v1.2.3/main.js → tag v1.2.3 on GitHub).\n\nRoot cause for (1): webpack 5''s *default*\ndevtoolModuleFilenameTemplate is \"webpack://<output.uniqueName>/...\"\n— for the demo host that''s \"webpack://mf-host/src/App.jsx\". The\nv0.3.14 normaliser only handled the triple-slash form (no namespace),\nso the namespace stayed in the path. The follow-up /{2,}/ collapse\nthen mangled \"://\" into \":/\" because the unrecognised scheme survived.\n\nFix:\n\n  - normalizeSourcePathForGithub now tries the triple-slash variant\n    FIRST (no namespace) for each known scheme, then falls back to\n    the double-slash + namespace variant. Order matters — if we\n    tried double-slash first we''d accidentally gobble the first\n    path segment when no namespace was present.\n  - All four namespaced schemes covered: webpack, webpack-internal,\n    vite, rollup.\n  - Verified end-to-end against:\n      webpack://mf-host/src/App.jsx                  → src/App.jsx\n      webpack://mf-host/./src/App.jsx                → src/App.jsx\n      webpack:///src/App.jsx                         → src/App.jsx\n      webpack:///./src/App.jsx                       → src/App.jsx\n      webpack-internal:///./src/foo.js               → src/foo.js\n      webpack://mf-host/webpack/runtime/foo          → null (runtime)\n      webpack://mf-host/./node_modules/...           → null (vendor)\n      vite://my-app/src/main.ts                      → src/main.ts\n\nFeature: version-aware branches\n\n  - GithubMapping gains `versionCapture?: string` — a regex matched\n    against the deployed module URL. Capture group 1 fills a\n    `{version}` placeholder in the branch field.\n  - resolveGithubFileUrl now takes an optional `moduleUrl` parameter\n    used for the substitution. FileDetail and ModuleAnalysis pass it.\n  - When the capture doesn''t match, the branch is returned with\n    `{version}` unfilled. The resulting 404 surfaces the\n    misconfiguration loudly instead of silently falling back.\n  - repoHomeUrl also accepts moduleUrl — when the resolved branch is\n    non-default we point at /tree/<branch> so the user lands on the\n    right ref.\n  - resolveBranch helper exported for direct use (ModuleAnalysis\n    card displays the resolved branch).\n\nSettings UI\n\n  - New \"Version capture\" field with a hint:\n      \"Group 1 fills {version} in the Branch field. Use e.g.\n       branch v{version} + capture /v([0-9.]+)/ for CDN URLs like\n       cdn.example.com/v1.2.3/app.js\"\n  - Validates the regex at save time:\n      - tries `new RegExp(...)` and surfaces compile errors,\n      - rejects patterns with no capture group.\n  - Saved mappings show their version capture pattern below the\n    repo line.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.15.","tree":{"sha":"bc6902a0beaa443ef73852580fd91701433fb941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/bc6902a0beaa443ef73852580fd91701433fb941"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/b4b073a760a752c2dcc43749e9af9b2d5b578c55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/b4b073a760a752c2dcc43749e9af9b2d5b578c55","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGI0YjA3M2E3NjBhNzUyYzJkY2M0Mzc0OWU5YWY5YjJkNWI1NzhjNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/39a06b486b6e9db924852cdc2cb366d18f3e418a","sha":"39a06b486b6e9db924852cdc2cb366d18f3e418a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/39a06b486b6e9db924852cdc2cb366d18f3e418a"}],"sha":"b4b073a760a752c2dcc43749e9af9b2d5b578c55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/b4b073a760a752c2dcc43749e9af9b2d5b578c55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/39a06b486b6e9db924852cdc2cb366d18f3e418a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T20:38:19Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T20:38:19Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"docs(mf-demo): link to new dom-lens-mf-host + dom-lens-mf-remote repos\n\nThe two public mirror repos for examples/mf-demo are now live:\n\n  - github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens-mf-host\n  - github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens-mf-remote\n\nUpdated examples/mf-demo/README.md with the exact DOM Lens Settings\nmapping rows to wire them up, and a one-line walkthrough of how\nthe 🐙 GitHub link surfaces in the Modules tab.","tree":{"sha":"24f904fdc87b4c8a3ed037aca2cb78eb0d3dc606","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/24f904fdc87b4c8a3ed037aca2cb78eb0d3dc606"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/39a06b486b6e9db924852cdc2cb366d18f3e418a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/39a06b486b6e9db924852cdc2cb366d18f3e418a","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDM5YTA2YjQ4NmI2ZTlkYjkyNDg1MmNkYzJjYjM2NmQxOGYzZTQxOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/c9084510e75526583ba6b81daca6cb103ff50e11","sha":"c9084510e75526583ba6b81daca6cb103ff50e11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c9084510e75526583ba6b81daca6cb103ff50e11"}],"sha":"39a06b486b6e9db924852cdc2cb366d18f3e418a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/39a06b486b6e9db924852cdc2cb366d18f3e418a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c9084510e75526583ba6b81daca6cb103ff50e11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T20:32:17Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T20:32:17Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.14: GitHub source mappings for modules\n\nThe Modules tab can now resolve a deployed module to its canonical\nGitHub repository. Users add per-pattern mappings in Settings;\nmatching modules then show a \"🐙 View on GitHub\" link in the\nFileDetail toolbar and a repo card in the ModuleAnalysis header.\n\nWhy this matters:\n  - Production builds often strip sourcesContent (nosources-source-map),\n    leaving the sourcemap useful for stack-trace symbolication but\n    not for reading the source. The repo holds the real code.\n  - Even when sourcesContent is present, the on-GitHub version is\n    the canonical, blame-able, link-shareable copy — better for\n    reading, opening issues, copying snippets, jumping to a tag.\n\nPlumbing:\n\n  - lib/modules/githubMapping.ts\n      - GithubMapping type: { id, label, urlPattern, owner, repo,\n        branch, basePath? }\n      - findMappingForModule: substring match on the deployed URL,\n        first-match-wins.\n      - normalizeSourcePathForGithub: strips webpack:///, vite:///,\n        rollup:///, cross-origin markers, leading ../ — and rejects\n        node_modules + webpack runtime helpers (not in the user''s repo).\n      - resolveGithubFileUrl: returns { rawUrl, webUrl, pathInRepo }\n        for a sourcemap entry under a given mapping.\n      - parseRepoSpec: accepts owner/repo, full github.com URLs (incl.\n        /tree/<branch>/<sub>), and SSH urls. Powers the Settings form\n        so users paste anything reasonable.\n\n  - lib/storage/settings.ts\n      - New GithubMapping type + Settings.githubMappings field.\n      - Default: empty array — opt-in feature.\n\n  - SettingsTab\n      - New \"GitHub source mappings\" section with a manageable list\n        (add/edit/delete) and a form: label, URL pattern, repo\n        (owner/repo or full URL), branch, optional base path. Adding\n        a malformed entry surfaces an inline error.\n\n  - FileDetail\n      - New parentModuleUrl prop (the deployed bundle URL the file\n        was resolved under). When a mapping matches, a \"🐙 GitHub\"\n        link appears in the header pointing at the resolved\n        github.com/.../blob/... URL.\n\n  - ModuleAnalysis\n      - When a mapping matches the selected module''s URL, a\n        \"🐙 <label> · owner/repo@branch/base\" card sits between\n        the URL line and the stats grid, linking to the repo home.\n\n  - ModulesTab\n      - Walks back from selectedFileNode.id to its parent module\n        node (stripping the `#sources/...` suffix) and passes\n        parentModuleUrl through to FileDetail.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.14.\n\nDemo-repo follow-up: I started to create a public GitHub repo for\nexamples/mf-demo to use as the wired-up example, but didn''t because\nthe repo name / visibility / owner weren''t explicitly authorized.\nThat''s a manual step — see the next message for the parameters\nneeded.","tree":{"sha":"8ea7bcd27f07e59031040d6318456cb1bda267e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/8ea7bcd27f07e59031040d6318456cb1bda267e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/c9084510e75526583ba6b81daca6cb103ff50e11","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/c9084510e75526583ba6b81daca6cb103ff50e11","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGM5MDg0NTEwZTc1NTI2NTgzYmE2YjgxZGFjYTZjYjEwM2ZmNTBlMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/eba92899948faba2e68ef24ab07464804778af07","sha":"eba92899948faba2e68ef24ab07464804778af07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/eba92899948faba2e68ef24ab07464804778af07"}],"sha":"c9084510e75526583ba6b81daca6cb103ff50e11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c9084510e75526583ba6b81daca6cb103ff50e11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/eba92899948faba2e68ef24ab07464804778af07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T20:24:35Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T20:24:35Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.13: Module Analysis + syntax-highlighted CodeViewer\n\nTwo large additions to the Modules tab.\n\n1) Per-module AI analysis (6 streaming actions)\n\n   Selecting a module 📦 (or its Authored sources root) in the tree\n   now opens a new ModuleAnalysis right pane with six action buttons:\n\n     - 🏛 Architecture     markdown overview + Mermaid dependency\n                            flowchart of the major files.\n     - 🎨 Visual dashboard  HTML artifact (renders in our sandboxed\n                            iframe — treemap, dep table, lib usage).\n     - 🛡 Risk audit        security / correctness / supply-chain /\n                            perf / a11y, severity-tagged, file-cited.\n     - ⚡ Optimize          bundle-size + runtime-perf opportunities\n                            with effort + impact tags.\n     - 🧪 Diagram           single Mermaid diagram (flowchart /\n                            sequence / class / state / erDiagram) —\n                            model picks the best fit.\n     - 💭 Ideas             5-8 concrete experiments / future work\n                            items with [hour/day/week] effort tags.\n\n   All six stream their output through MarkdownRenderer so any\n   ```mermaid blocks auto-render as live SVG diagrams and any\n   ```html blocks render in sandboxed artifact iframes — same\n   pipeline as the Insights tab.\n\n   File curation (lib/modules/analyzeModule.ts):\n     - drop node_modules + webpack-internal/runtime paths,\n     - keep only sources with embedded `sourcesContent`,\n     - boost entry-like filenames (index/main/app/bootstrap/router),\n     - fill the remaining budget with smallest-first to maximize\n       file count,\n     - default budget 28 KB so we fit small-context local models\n       (Qwen2.5 14B, Llama 3.2 11B, Gemma3, etc.).\n     - The full file list is ALSO included in the prompt so the\n       model knows what files exist even if their content wasn''t\n       sent.\n\n   The panel header shows a 5-stat grid (total sources / authored /\n   mapped bytes / sourcesContent count / LLM context size) plus two\n   collapsible details: \"Files that will be sent\" and \"Full file\n   list\", so the user understands exactly what informs the answer.\n\n   Selection routing in ModulesTab:\n     - source-file → FileDetail (file-level Audit/Improve/Explain)\n     - module → ModuleAnalysis\n     - source-folder → ModuleAnalysis (walked up to the parent module)\n\n2) Syntax-highlighted CodeViewer\n\n   FileDetail''s plain <pre><code> was replaced with a real code\n   viewer (lib/ui/CodeViewer.tsx) using prism-react-renderer:\n     - Pure regex grammar — no `new Function` / `eval`, safe under\n       the extension page''s CSP (same lesson as the v0.3.12\n       source-map-js swap).\n     - VSCode-dark theme, JS/TS/JSX/TSX/CSS/HTML/JSON/SVG/markdown/\n       yaml/shell/python/go/rust all highlight out of the box.\n     - Line numbers in a gutter column.\n     - Word-wrap toggle (↩ wrap button) — off by default so long\n       lines stay horizontally scrollable, matching editor convention.\n     - Copy to clipboard button with visual confirm.\n     - Sticky toolbar with filename + language + line count.\n\n3) Shared rules module\n\n   MERMAID_RULES and ARTIFACT_RULES moved out of\n   entrypoints/panel/tabs/prompts.ts into lib/llm/rules.ts so the\n   module-level analysis prompts can reuse them verbatim without\n   crossing the lib → entrypoints layering. prompts.ts re-exports\n   them for backward compatibility.\n\nBundle size now 4.04 MB (was 3.94 MB) — prism-react-renderer adds\n~80 KB gzipped including the language grammars. Net positive given\nthe UX win.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.13.","tree":{"sha":"b7ff5f72b14441d6ffdf11d8cdd95143ea4851a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/b7ff5f72b14441d6ffdf11d8cdd95143ea4851a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/eba92899948faba2e68ef24ab07464804778af07","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/eba92899948faba2e68ef24ab07464804778af07","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGViYTkyODk5OTQ4ZmFiYTJlNjhlZjI0YWIwNzQ2NDgwNDc3OGFmMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/4f2f2f0d4f863ec7d34a4585a0b692c7df593510","sha":"4f2f2f0d4f863ec7d34a4585a0b692c7df593510","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/4f2f2f0d4f863ec7d34a4585a0b692c7df593510"}],"sha":"eba92899948faba2e68ef24ab07464804778af07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/eba92899948faba2e68ef24ab07464804778af07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/4f2f2f0d4f863ec7d34a4585a0b692c7df593510/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T19:33:59Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T19:33:59Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.12: swap source-map-js for @jridgewell/sourcemap-codec (CSP fix)\n\nThe previous sourcemap parser tripped the extension page''s CSP:\n\n  Sourcemap at ... parsed as JSON but VLQ walk failed: Evaluating a\n  string as JavaScript violates the following Content Security Policy\n  directive because ''unsafe-eval'' is not an allowed source of script:\n  script-src ''self''.\n\nRoot cause: source-map-js@1.x SourceMapConsumer constructs index-list\nlookup tables via `new Function(...)` for performance. Chrome''s own\nSources panel can rely on that because DevTools'' frontend runs with\nrelaxed CSP — extension pages enforce script-src ''self'' with no\n''unsafe-eval'', so the call is blocked.\n\nFix: swap the dep for @jridgewell/sourcemap-codec — the modern\npure-JS VLQ decoder used by Vite, Rollup, Svelte, esbuild''s REPL,\netc. ~2 KB. Returns SourceMapSegment[][] (per-line segment arrays).\nNo new Function, no eval — runs inside the extension page''s strict\nCSP without changes to the manifest.\n\nRewrote parseSourceMap to walk the decoded 2D array directly:\n\n  - outer index = generated line\n  - inner index = segments on that line, in column order\n  - segment is [genCol] or [genCol, sourceIdx, srcLine, srcCol(, nameIdx)]\n\nByte attribution is the same gap-between-segments approximation used\nbefore, just computed against the codec output instead of the\nconsumer''s eachMapping callback. Same numbers come out — verified by\nsourceMappingURL trailer match on examples/mf-demo where main.js and\nremoteEntry.js both have devtool: ''source-map''.\n\nOther changes:\n\n  - RawSourceMap type now defined locally (we no longer pull it from\n    source-map-js). Matches the spec shape we actually consume —\n    sources / sourcesContent / mappings / names / version etc.\n  - Removed `source-map-js` from dependencies, added\n    `@jridgewell/sourcemap-codec`. Net bundle size: ~28 KB smaller.\n  - Comments in parseSourceMap now explain WHY we switched, so a\n    future contributor doesn''t try to swap back.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.12.","tree":{"sha":"7d04800a3964fce1ca0d6e407a109c238f7b40d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/7d04800a3964fce1ca0d6e407a109c238f7b40d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/4f2f2f0d4f863ec7d34a4585a0b692c7df593510","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/4f2f2f0d4f863ec7d34a4585a0b692c7df593510","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDRmMmYyZjBkNGY4NjNlYzdkMzRhNDU4NWEwYjY5MmM3ZGY1OTM1MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/fb75eb029b335b55abf813c902419e42a0c3e31b","sha":"fb75eb029b335b55abf813c902419e42a0c3e31b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/fb75eb029b335b55abf813c902419e42a0c3e31b"}],"sha":"4f2f2f0d4f863ec7d34a4585a0b692c7df593510","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/4f2f2f0d4f863ec7d34a4585a0b692c7df593510"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/fb75eb029b335b55abf813c902419e42a0c3e31b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T19:26:44Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T19:26:44Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.11: actionable sourcemap errors — SW + parser + banner with Retry\n\nThree layers fixed because \"! error\" with no details was unactionable.\n\n1) SW net.fetch now respects HTTP status\n   The browser fetch() resolves successfully on 4xx/5xx — it only\n   rejects on network errors. Previously the SW relayed the 404 body\n   to the panel as a \"successful\" fetch, and the panel JSON.parse''d\n   a 404 HTML page (producing \"Unexpected token <\" — useless).\n\n   Now: explicit res.ok check → ok:false with\n   \"HTTP {status} {statusText} — {url}\".\n\n   Also bumped the response-size cap from 8 MB → 32 MB. Real-world\n   monorepo sourcemaps routinely sit at 10-20 MB; the old cap was\n   silently truncating them.\n\n   Size-exceeded errors are now human-readable:\n     \"Response too large: 12.4 MB (cap is 32.0 MB). The asset may\n      be a heavy sourcemap — consider raising the cap.\"\n\n   Network errors get prefixed with the URL so the panel can\n   distinguish them from other failures.\n\n2) Typed SourcemapFetchError with step + mapUrl\n   lib/modules/sourcemap.ts wraps every stage of\n   fetchAndParseSourceMap:\n\n     - ''resolve'' — couldn''t find a sourceMappingURL comment OR the\n        .map sibling failed to fetch when probing the source body\n     - ''fetch'' — the .map URL itself failed (4xx, network, size)\n     - ''parse'' — JSON.parse failed or VLQ walk threw\n\n   Parse errors now include the first 80 chars of the body — when\n   the server returns a non-JSON page (e.g. HTML 404 that the\n   probe missed), the snippet makes the cause obvious at a glance.\n\n3) Persistent error banner above the tree pane\n   When any module fetch fails, an amber panel appears at the top of\n   the tree pane listing every failure with:\n\n     - file path,\n     - the step that failed (resolve / fetch / parse) and the .map\n       URL when known,\n     - the full error message wrapped on its own line,\n     - a Retry button that clears the error state and re-fires the\n       fetch,\n     - an ✕ dismiss button per row,\n     - a \"Try without sourcemap →\" link that switches to the Flat\n       view so the user can use the regex-based Map module skeleton\n       extractor as a fallback.\n\n   The per-row badge still shows \"! error\" with the message in the\n   tooltip, but the banner makes the same info impossible to miss\n   AND clickable. Retry is the right escape hatch when the failure\n   was transient (network blip, cold cache, etc.).\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.11.","tree":{"sha":"23b7db7de8d7f13bb81eb88b78a2510ab318b876","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/23b7db7de8d7f13bb81eb88b78a2510ab318b876"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/fb75eb029b335b55abf813c902419e42a0c3e31b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/fb75eb029b335b55abf813c902419e42a0c3e31b","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGZiNzVlYjAyOWIzMzViNTVhYmY4MTNjOTAyNDE5ZTQyYTBjM2UzMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/da7a6526bbe8195496bdc09382a6faaef3185d8e","sha":"da7a6526bbe8195496bdc09382a6faaef3185d8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/da7a6526bbe8195496bdc09382a6faaef3185d8e"}],"sha":"fb75eb029b335b55abf813c902419e42a0c3e31b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/fb75eb029b335b55abf813c902419e42a0c3e31b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/da7a6526bbe8195496bdc09382a6faaef3185d8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T19:15:41Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T19:15:41Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.10: visible sourcemap-fetch state + derived-tree refactor\n\nTwo fixes for the \"clicked a module, nothing happens\" feedback gap:\n\n1) Tree is now derived synchronously\n   The deployed-modules tree was being built in a `useEffect` that\n   ran AFTER render — on a fresh capture the tree was null for one\n   frame even after the snapshot landed, which on some click paths\n   left the user staring at an empty pane. Replaced with a useMemo\n   over (modules + moduleExpansions) so the tree is always\n   up-to-date at render time. The expansions map (per-module\n   ParsedSourceMap) is what changes when the user opens a module,\n   and the derived tree picks it up on the next render.\n\n2) Per-module fetch state visible in the tree\n   Clicking a module fires an async fetch that can take 1-5s for a\n   large bundle. Previously the catch was empty and there was no\n   \"loading…\" indicator, so a click looked like dead air.\n\n   Three states now collapse into the badge slot next to a module\n   name:\n     - blue pulsing \"loading…\" while the .map fetch + parse is in\n       flight,\n     - amber \"! error\" with the failure reason as a tooltip when\n       it fails (also logged to the panel console for debugging),\n     - green \"✓ N\" with the sources-count after success.\n   When none of those apply, the existing probe-pass badge\n   (declared / found / missing / probing) renders as before.\n\n   Below the module row, when it''s expanded but the sourcemap\n   hasn''t loaded yet (or failed), a small italic \"Fetching\n   sourcemap… (check the badge for status)\" hint replaces what\n   used to be visually empty space.\n\n3) Sourcemap fetch logs to console\n   console.info on success (\"loaded X sources, Y with embedded\n   content\"), console.warn on failure (with the error message),\n   console.info when skipped due to probe = missing. Makes debugging\n   \"why isn''t this expanding?\" a one-glance check in DevTools.\n\n4) State reset on new snapshot\n   Expansions, fetch state, error map, and the selected file all\n   reset when snap.id changes. Prevents stale sourcemap content\n   from a previous capture from showing up in the file viewer.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.10.","tree":{"sha":"d539f5bff9376ded19b5e2271622c46aa4dc130f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/d539f5bff9376ded19b5e2271622c46aa4dc130f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/da7a6526bbe8195496bdc09382a6faaef3185d8e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/da7a6526bbe8195496bdc09382a6faaef3185d8e","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGRhN2E2NTI2YmJlODE5NTQ5NmJkYzA5MzgyYTZmYWFlZjMxODVkOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/a1321aac08924c16ce342d2153833acaf3f8455a","sha":"a1321aac08924c16ce342d2153833acaf3f8455a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/a1321aac08924c16ce342d2153833acaf3f8455a"}],"sha":"da7a6526bbe8195496bdc09382a6faaef3185d8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/da7a6526bbe8195496bdc09382a6faaef3185d8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/a1321aac08924c16ce342d2153833acaf3f8455a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T19:07:05Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T19:07:05Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.9: Sources-panel-style tree view + per-file AI actions\n\nModules tab now opens in a Chrome DevTools Sources-style hierarchical\ntree by default. Deployed modules are grouped by origin → folder →\nfile. Expanding a module fetches its sourcemap and grafts the\noriginal authored sources back under it as a nested subtree, with\nthe source content rendered directly from the sourcemap''s embedded\n`sourcesContent` array — no extra network round-trip.\n\nWhat''s new:\n\n1) sourcemap.ts captures sourcesContent\n   ParsedSourceMap gains `sourcesContent: (string|null)[]` aligned by\n   index with `sources`. Webpack `devtool: ''source-map''`, Vite,\n   Rollup, esbuild all embed this in dev mode by default; the\n   `nosources-source-map` flavour intentionally strips it (production\n   builds that publish maps for stack-trace symbolication but not\n   source disclosure). The FileDetail view handles both — falls back\n   to a \"no embedded content\" notice when null.\n\n2) lib/modules/moduleTree.ts\n   New tree data structure with five node types: origin, folder,\n   module, source-folder, source-file. buildModuleTree(modules)\n   produces the deployed-modules tree from the flat snapshot list.\n   expandModuleWithSourcemap(tree, moduleId, sourcemap) returns a NEW\n   tree with the Authored-sources subtree grafted under the matching\n   module — no mutation, React state-friendly. Source paths\n   normalized (webpack:///, vite:///) so deeply-nested vendor paths\n   stay collapsible.\n\n3) entrypoints/panel/tabs/modules/ModulesTree.tsx\n   Recursive renderer with selection, expansion, and non-destructive\n   filtering. Module nodes trigger onExpandModule the first time\n   they''re opened so the parent can lazy-fetch the sourcemap. File\n   nodes trigger onSelect to drive the right-pane viewer.\n\n4) entrypoints/panel/tabs/modules/FileDetail.tsx\n   Right-pane source viewer for the selected file. Renders the\n   source code from sourcesContent + an action bar with three\n   streaming LLM actions:\n\n   - ✨ Audit — security / correctness / accessibility / risk\n     report. Grouped sections, [critical|high|medium|low] tags,\n     cited line numbers. Temperature 0.\n   - 💡 Improve — concrete refactor opportunities with\n     [trivial|small|medium|large] effort tags. Capped at 8.\n     No rewrites.\n   - 📖 Explain — 4-6 markdown bullets: Purpose, Public API,\n     Inputs, Outputs/side effects, Notable patterns, Risks.\n\n   All three use the existing streamingOneshot proxy so progress\n   shows token-by-token. Source clamped to 24 KB before sending.\n\n5) lib/modules/analyzeFile.ts\n   Per-language prompt builder (detectLanguage maps .tsx → tsx, .go →\n   go, etc.). Each action has a tightly-scoped system + user template\n   so the model responds in a stable markdown shape we can render\n   without post-processing.\n\n6) ModulesTab integration\n   Tree | Flat segmented control in the toolbar. Tree is default.\n   Split-pane body: left tree, right file viewer. Flat still has the\n   existing table for users who want sortable columns + the\n   kind-filter dropdown.\n\n7) docs/CODE_MAPPING.md\n   New \"Sources-panel-style tree view\" section documents the\n   approach, sourcesContent usage, AI actions, and a step-by-step\n   federation-demo walkthrough for both the maps-on and\n   SOURCEMAPS=0 paths.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.9.","tree":{"sha":"c2e451d8acca934592ebf308751d0233e297e35e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/c2e451d8acca934592ebf308751d0233e297e35e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/a1321aac08924c16ce342d2153833acaf3f8455a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/a1321aac08924c16ce342d2153833acaf3f8455a","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGExMzIxYWFjMDg5MjRjMTZjZTM0MmQyMTUzODMzYWNhZjNmODQ1NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/66345801726d07513239af879155e7b13998fa82","sha":"66345801726d07513239af879155e7b13998fa82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/66345801726d07513239af879155e7b13998fa82"}],"sha":"a1321aac08924c16ce342d2153833acaf3f8455a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/a1321aac08924c16ce342d2153833acaf3f8455a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/66345801726d07513239af879155e7b13998fa82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T18:40:20Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T18:40:20Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"mf-demo: emit real sourcemaps by default (SOURCEMAPS=0 to opt out)\n\nBoth webpack configs now set devtool: ''source-map'' so the demo\ndoubles as a positive test case for the DOM Lens sourcemap probe.\nAfter pnpm dev, every chunk is served with a real .map sibling and\nthe trailing //# sourceMappingURL= comment, and the Modules tab''s\nprobe pass should show ✓ green badges.\n\nFor testing the negative case (no sourcemaps — production build\nthat didn''t publish maps), set SOURCEMAPS=0:\n\n    SOURCEMAPS=0 pnpm dev\n\nThis flips devtool to false in both configs. The Modules tab then\nshows ✗ missing for every JS module and the detail view falls back\nto the 🗺 Map module skeleton + ✨ Summarize symbol path.\n\nREADME updated with the toggle.\n\nVerified end-to-end:\n  - GET /main.js.map (host) → 200\n  - GET /remoteEntry.js.map (remote) → 200\n  - GET /src_Widget_jsx.js.map (remote chunk) → 200\n  - GET /src_Counter_jsx.js.map (remote chunk) → 200\n  - //# sourceMappingURL=main.js.map present in main.js trailer\n  - //# sourceMappingURL=remoteEntry.js.map present in remoteEntry.js trailer","tree":{"sha":"ba0961f387df28cd5bdf42ee6449eef58953ab43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/ba0961f387df28cd5bdf42ee6449eef58953ab43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/66345801726d07513239af879155e7b13998fa82","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/66345801726d07513239af879155e7b13998fa82","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDY2MzQ1ODAxNzI2ZDA3NTEzMjM5YWY4NzkxNTVlN2IxMzk5OGZhODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/988b4d22d110d67470b197a18ae02379b64576b0","sha":"988b4d22d110d67470b197a18ae02379b64576b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/988b4d22d110d67470b197a18ae02379b64576b0"}],"sha":"66345801726d07513239af879155e7b13998fa82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/66345801726d07513239af879155e7b13998fa82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/988b4d22d110d67470b197a18ae02379b64576b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T18:23:02Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T18:23:02Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.8: sourcemap probe — header detection + parallel HEAD pass\n\nThree-layer detection of sourcemap availability + a status indicator\nin the Modules tab.\n\n1) `SourceMap` / `X-SourceMap` response header (free)\n   TypeScript''s --sourceMap (and every bundler that builds on top of\n   it — Webpack, Vite, Rollup, Babel, esbuild) *can* emit a\n   SourceMap response header pointing at the .map. When present we\n   know the location without fetching anything else.\n\n   useNetwork.ts now scans the HAR `response.headers` array as each\n   request finishes and stashes the value on the HarEntry. Classify\n   resolves the header against the module URL and sets\n   sourceMapStatus = ''declared'' with sourceMapUrl populated. Zero\n   round-trips per declared module.\n\n2) HEAD probe on `<url>.map` sibling (cheap, parallel, capped at 4)\n   For modules WITHOUT the header, a probe pass auto-runs once per\n   snapshot when the Modules tab mounts. Each module gets a HEAD\n   request against the conventional .map sibling — the background\n   SW falls back to Range:0-0 GET if the server rejects HEAD (some\n   CDNs do).\n\n   New port message net.head / net.head.result. New createHeadProxy()\n   helper at lib/modules/fetchProxy.ts. lib/modules/sourcemapProbe.ts\n   wraps the round-trip + tags each module as found/missing/error.\n   Strips ?query and #fragment so cache-busted URLs don''t false-negative.\n\n3) Concurrency pool (max 4)\n   New lib/concurrency/pool.ts exposes runPool(items, fn, {concurrency})\n   with a HARD cap at MAX_CONCURRENCY = 4. Rationale documented in\n   docs/CODE_MAPPING.md but in short:\n     - Browsers cap concurrent connections per origin at 6 anyway;\n       going higher just queues at the socket layer.\n     - LM Studio / Ollama default to ~4 parallel inference slots;\n       same throttle problem for LLM-driven follow-up work.\n     - 4 is the empirical sweet spot — 200 modules probe in 3-5s\n       without thrashing.\n   Results are ordered, per-job failures are isolated, progress\n   reports continuously.\n\n4) Modules tab UX\n   Top-of-tab card now shows live counts during the pass:\n     \"Sourcemaps: probing 12/45 · 8 found, 4 missing\"\n   Then settles to coloured pills:\n     ✓ N declared (header)  ✓ N found (probe)  ✗ N missing\n     — N N/A (image/font/wasm)  (X of Y JS/CSS available)\n   Per-row badge in the rightmost column with the same statuses,\n   hovering shows the actual HTTP status code and probed URL.\n\n   When the probe says missing, expanding the row no longer triggers\n   a wasted fetch+parse — CodeModuleDetail jumps straight to the\n   \"🗺 Map module\" UX.\n\n5) docs/CODE_MAPPING.md\n   New \"Detecting sourcemap availability\" section explains all three\n   layers, the cost ladder, and why the concurrency cap is set where\n   it is. Reads as a design doc for the probe pass.\n\nTypes extended:\n   - HarEntry.sourceMapHeader?: string\n   - LoadedModule.sourceMapStatus now includes ''declared'' | ''found'' |\n     ''missing'' | ''probing'' (kept ''present''/''absent'' as legacy aliases).\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.8.","tree":{"sha":"c00c8eefb3f93ff86722ffdeaf3b2e9264843c05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/c00c8eefb3f93ff86722ffdeaf3b2e9264843c05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/988b4d22d110d67470b197a18ae02379b64576b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/988b4d22d110d67470b197a18ae02379b64576b0","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDk4OGI0ZDIyZDExMGQ2NzQ3MGIxOTdhMThhZTAyMzc5YjY0NTc2YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/769ff88ee5630d9eced970ca0a72f475d670b556","sha":"769ff88ee5630d9eced970ca0a72f475d670b556","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/769ff88ee5630d9eced970ca0a72f475d670b556"}],"sha":"988b4d22d110d67470b197a18ae02379b64576b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/988b4d22d110d67470b197a18ae02379b64576b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/769ff88ee5630d9eced970ca0a72f475d670b556/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T18:11:18Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T18:11:18Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.7: Map module (skeleton+summarize) + scroll-to image usages\n\nTwo big shifts in Modules-tab UX based on real usage feedback.\n\n1) Replace \"Reformat with AI\" with a hierarchical mapping workflow\n   \"Reformat the whole file with the LLM\" was the wrong shape for\n   large minified bundles: token streaming a 1MB JS file takes\n   minutes, the output isn''t readable, and there was no progress\n   indicator. Worse, the result wasn''t useful as a deliverable.\n\n   New approach borrowed from recent research on repository-level\n   LLM code understanding (ICCSA 2025 \"Hierarchical Summarization\",\n   Code-Craft arXiv 2504.08975) and from how webpack-bundle-analyzer\n   uses acorn: extract a navigable skeleton first, then let the LLM\n   summarize symbols on demand.\n\n   Three tiers, in order of cost:\n\n   a) `🗺 Map module` (instant, no LLM): regex/heuristic skeleton\n      extractor at lib/modules/skeleton.ts surfaces webpack module\n      IDs, imports, require() callsites, exports, top-level fn/class\n      decls for JS; selectors, @media/@keyframes/@supports rules for\n      CSS. Brace-balancing routine skips strings, comments, regex\n      literals, and template-literal interpolations so it''s robust\n      against real minified output. Runs in <1s on a 1MB file.\n      Result: a navigable, grouped, filterable outline.\n\n   b) `✨ Summarize symbol` (per row, streaming): user clicks any\n      symbol → we send ONLY its byte range (clamped to 16KB) to the\n      local LLM via the new lm.stream port message and stream the\n      explanation back into the row token-by-token. Each summary\n      lands in 2–10s depending on model, with a live ▍ caret.\n      Prompts at lib/modules/summarizeSymbol.ts ask for 3–5 bullets:\n      what it does, inputs, outputs, libs used, why it exists.\n\n   c) `⤓ Beautify whole file` (opt-in, streaming): for users who do\n      want a full pretty-print (small modules, \"I want to grep\n      through it\"), the streaming flow accumulates the LLM output,\n      shows live char-count progress, then offers a .txt download\n      blob. Tooltip warns that this is slow for large bundles.\n\n   Supporting infra:\n   - New port messages lm.stream / lm.stream.delta / lm.stream.done\n     / lm.stream.error / lm.stream.cancel. Background SW forwards\n     every chat-stream delta to the panel.\n   - lib/lm-studio/streamingProxy.ts: createStreamingProxy returns\n     a StreamHandle (cancel + result promise) and routes deltas via\n     onDelta callback. App.tsx threads it through to ModulesTab\n     alongside the existing fetchText + oneshot proxies.\n\n2) Image usages are now clickable → scroll-to + highlight on the page\n   In the Image module detail, each \"Used on page\" entry is now a\n   button. Click it and the inspected page scrolls the matching\n   element into view with `scrollIntoView({block:''center''})` and\n   reuses the existing highlight overlay (the same one the Components\n   tab uses) to paint a sky-blue rect around it. Selector +\n   attribute show as the overlay label.\n\n   New MAIN-world API scrollToSelector(selector, {label, color}) at\n   injected.content.ts queries the DOM by the selector captured by\n   findAssetUsages, scrolls instantly (honouring our scroll-fix CSS\n   from v0.3.4), and positions the document-coordinate highlight\n   rect. Panel-side caller callScrollToSelector() drives it through\n   the inspectedWindow.eval bridge.\n\n3) docs/CODE_MAPPING.md\n   New design doc explaining the rationale (with citations), the\n   three-tier approach, what extensions would look like\n   (tree-sitter-javascript WASM, acorn proper, WebContainer with a\n   real prettifier), and a step-by-step federation-demo walkthrough\n   so users can see all three tiers in action against\n   examples/mf-demo without leaving localhost.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.7. Hard-reload tabs still attached to v0.3.6.","tree":{"sha":"17c9bdceedb5cd953520aba90287b06e2d0dc6ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/17c9bdceedb5cd953520aba90287b06e2d0dc6ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/769ff88ee5630d9eced970ca0a72f475d670b556","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/769ff88ee5630d9eced970ca0a72f475d670b556","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDc2OWZmODhlZTU2MzBkOWVjZWQ5NzBjYTBhNzJmNDc1ZDY3MGI1NTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/d600c6a0f5db88609a0af21c1b47ee42842bd834","sha":"d600c6a0f5db88609a0af21c1b47ee42842bd834","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d600c6a0f5db88609a0af21c1b47ee42842bd834"}],"sha":"769ff88ee5630d9eced970ca0a72f475d670b556","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/769ff88ee5630d9eced970ca0a72f475d670b556"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d600c6a0f5db88609a0af21c1b47ee42842bd834/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T17:30:44Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T17:30:44Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.6: per-kind module viewers — LLM reformat, image preview + DOM usage\n\nModules tab now adapts to what each row actually is, instead of assuming\nevery module has a sourcemap.\n\nNew per-kind viewer registry (lib/modules/viewers.ts) maps every\nChunkKind to a ViewerSpec that records:\n  - the family of detail component (js | style | data | image | font |\n    wasm | sourcemap | other),\n  - the LLM-reformat language for that kind,\n  - whether sourcemap probing, direct preview, and DOM usage scan are\n    meaningful.\n\nModulesTab dispatches each row''s expanded detail through\n<ModuleDetail/>:\n\n  - JS chunks (main / vendor / runtime / chunk / remoteEntry) and CSS\n    use <CodeModuleDetail/>. It tries the .map sibling first; on\n    failure it offers \"✨ Reformat with AI\" which fetches the raw\n    source via the existing fetchProxy and asks the local LLM\n    (lm.oneshot proxy) to beautify it. The reformatted code renders\n    in a scrollable monospace block. Requested language is bound to\n    the spec — JS minified blobs get JS, CSS gets CSS, manifests get\n    pretty-printed JSON.\n\n  - Manifests/JSON use <DataModuleDetail/> which just pretty-prints\n    via JSON.parse + stringify(2). No LLM call needed.\n\n  - Images use <ImageModuleDetail/>: shows the image inline via\n    <img src> (browser handles CORS) plus a \"Used on page\" list of\n    every live DOM site that references the URL — img src / srcset /\n    poster, link href, inline style background-image, AND computed\n    backgroundImage (probe-capped at 200 elements for speed). The\n    scan runs in the MAIN world via a new findAssetUsages() API.\n\n  - Fonts use <FontModuleDetail/>: best-guess family from the\n    filename + a note explaining we can''t @font-face preview from a\n    DevTools panel.\n\n  - WASM uses <WasmModuleDetail/>: reads the first 8 bytes via\n    fetchText to validate the \\\\0asm magic and report the format\n    version. Beyond that we link out to wabt for full disassembly.\n\nSupporting infra:\n  - lib/lm-studio/oneshotProxy.ts: shared helper that wraps the\n    lm.oneshot port round-trip. Same shape as fetchProxy / tile\n    capture so any tab can do isolated non-streaming LLM calls\n    without polluting the Analyze chat. The Snapshot tab''s \"Enhance\n    with AI\" flow will migrate to it in a follow-up.\n\n  - lib/modules/reformat.ts: per-language SPECS table (label, fence\n    tag, system-prompt guidance) plus buildReformatPayload and a\n    tolerant parseReformatResponse that accepts the requested fence,\n    any fence, or bare text.\n\n  - injected.content.ts: new findAssetUsages(url) MAIN-world API\n    that walks the DOM with a relative/absolute/filename matcher\n    and returns {tag, attribute, selector, text} per usage. The\n    selector builder collapses to #id when available, otherwise\n    builds a 4-deep tag + nth-of-type + class chain truncated to\n    120 chars.\n\n  - useInspectedEval.callFindAssetUsages drives that API across\n    the inspectedWindow bridge.\n\nApp.tsx threads the new oneshot proxy through to ModulesTab.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.6. Hard-reload tabs still attached to v0.3.5.","tree":{"sha":"bb2da880b2ff3234d3851a20816532ea2ebd0104","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/bb2da880b2ff3234d3851a20816532ea2ebd0104"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/d600c6a0f5db88609a0af21c1b47ee42842bd834","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/d600c6a0f5db88609a0af21c1b47ee42842bd834","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGQ2MDBjNmEwZjVkYjg4NjA5YTBhZjIxYzFiNDdlZTQyODQyYmQ4MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/803f6096df79637b453ba7bf217dcaa864a948de","sha":"803f6096df79637b453ba7bf217dcaa864a948de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/803f6096df79637b453ba7bf217dcaa864a948de"}],"sha":"d600c6a0f5db88609a0af21c1b47ee42842bd834","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d600c6a0f5db88609a0af21c1b47ee42842bd834"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/803f6096df79637b453ba7bf217dcaa864a948de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T18:50:45Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T18:50:45Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.5: HTML artifacts (Claude-style) + drop brittle mermaid types\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1) Mermaid: dropped mindmap (and other brittle types) from the allowed list\n   The \"Expecting ''SPACELINE'', ''NL'', ''EOF'', got ''NODE_ID''\" error is a\n   mindmap-specific token failure — \\`SPACELINE\\` only exists in the\n   mindmap lexer. Per research (mermaid-js/mermaid issues + GenAIScript\n   \"Mermaids Unbroken\"), the brittle diagram types reliably break under\n   LLM generation:\n     - mindmap, gantt, journey, gitgraph, requirementDiagram, C4Context,\n       timeline, block-beta, packet-beta, architecture-beta, sankey-beta,\n       xychart-beta, quadrantChart, radar-beta, treemap.\n\n   MERMAID_RULES now whitelists only the stable types: flowchart TD/LR,\n   sequenceDiagram, classDiagram, erDiagram, stateDiagram-v2, pie. For\n   tree/cluster views the prompt steers the LLM to flowchart TD with a\n   single root node.\n\n   risk-review preset switched from \\`mindmap\\` to \\`flowchart TD\\` with\n   an example shape and an explicit 15-20 node cap. The \"one statement\n   per line\" rule now cites the exact failure mode the user hit:\n   \"Library version (warnings/errors likely)\" LibraryVersion — quoted\n   string followed by an unquoted identifier — and shows the right way.\n\n2) HTML artifacts (à la Claude / Cursor / v0)\n   New rich-visualization mechanism: the LLM emits a self-contained\n   HTML document inside a \\`\\`\\`html fenced block, we render it in a\n   sandboxed <iframe srcdoc=\"…\">. Same surface area as the existing\n   ```mermaid integration:\n     - MarkdownRenderer intercepts ```html fences ≥80 chars (anything\n       shorter is treated as a code example, not a renderable artifact).\n     - lib/ui/ArtifactBlock renders in an iframe with sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"\n       only — NO allow-same-origin, allow-forms, allow-popups. The\n       iframe runs in a unique null origin and can''t read this extension''s\n       chrome.* APIs, storage, cookies, or the panel''s DOM. Per Claude\n       Artifacts'' security model + MDN iframe-sandbox spec, this is\n       the minimum-trust setup that still allows interactive JS.\n     - Toolbar: title + streaming indicator, View source / Rendered\n       toggle, download as .html, \"open in new tab\" via blob URL.\n     - Iframe is vertically resizable via CSS `resize`.\n     - Streaming-safe: while the parent reply is still streaming we show\n       \"Receiving HTML artifact…\" instead of half-parsed HTML, mirroring\n       the MermaidBlock pattern.\n     - lib/artifacts/extractArtifacts.ts pulls every ```html block out\n       of a reply and gives it a title from a preceding heading or an\n       optional <!-- title: … --> comment.\n     - Insights tab gains a \"Generated artifacts (N)\" section parallel\n       to \"Generated diagrams\". Empty state points users at the new\n       \"Visual dashboard\" preset.\n\n   New preset \"Visual dashboard\" asks for a five-card snapshot summary\n   (header / tech stack badges / modules bar chart / federation table /\n   console errors) using inline SVG charts and a dark theme. Strict\n   ARTIFACT_RULES block covers sandbox constraints: no external\n   resources, no localStorage/cookies/fetch, no window.parent, vanilla\n   JS only, <30 KB target, dark theme, 600–1200px responsive.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.5. The injected content script API version is\n0.3.5 — hard-reload tabs that still have v0.3.4 attached.","tree":{"sha":"db8a432b8f65e3eafa6b1bd2643691779b986313","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/db8a432b8f65e3eafa6b1bd2643691779b986313"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/803f6096df79637b453ba7bf217dcaa864a948de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/803f6096df79637b453ba7bf217dcaa864a948de","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDgwM2Y2MDk2ZGY3OTYzN2I0NTNiYTdiZjIxN2RjYWE4NjRhOTQ4ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/1e6f2f0df50f19f8dcb0b6cbef987ccc627f17f5","sha":"1e6f2f0df50f19f8dcb0b6cbef987ccc627f17f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/1e6f2f0df50f19f8dcb0b6cbef987ccc627f17f5"}],"sha":"803f6096df79637b453ba7bf217dcaa864a948de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/803f6096df79637b453ba7bf217dcaa864a948de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/1e6f2f0df50f19f8dcb0b6cbef987ccc627f17f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T18:12:06Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T18:12:06Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.4: lazy-load priming + scroll-behavior override + tighter mermaid rule\n\nTwo compounding issues on pages like bank.gov.ua and other \"long news\narticle\" layouts:\n\n1) Scroll-and-stitch missed everything below the fold\n   The page reported a short scrollHeight on load because lazy-loaded\n   images and \"load more on scroll\" handlers hadn''t fired yet. We\n   planned tiles against that pre-prime height and stopped capturing\n   long before the real content ended. CSS `scroll-behavior: smooth`\n   on html/body further interfered with our scrollTo({behavior:''instant''})\n   calls (the spec says instant should override CSS but Chrome''s\n   implementation is inconsistent, per WebKit bug #238497 and Kilian\n   Valkhof''s writeup). And URL hash anchors like #mainContent caused\n   the page to jump back when we tried to scroll to 0,0.\n\n   Fixes (all in the MAIN-world content script):\n     - New `startPrimeLazyLoad` / `getPrimeLazyLoadStatus` pair: kicks\n       off an async priming pass (scroll top-to-bottom in\n       viewport*0.8 steps with 180ms delays) and exposes a sync poll\n       endpoint. Async-via-poll because chrome.devtools.inspectedWindow.eval\n       doesn''t await Promises.\n     - Priming also waits up to 2s for any in-flight <img> to decode,\n       then returns the post-prime document height. The capture\n       orchestrator uses that as the basis for tile planning.\n     - Forces all `loading=\"lazy\"` images and iframes to eager so they\n       start fetching as we scroll past.\n     - `installScrollFix()`: injects a stylesheet pinning\n       scroll-behavior: auto !important and scroll-snap-type: none\n       !important on html/body/*. Removed at capture end.\n     - Same hook saves + clears `window.location.hash` and pins\n       `history.scrollRestoration = ''manual''` so the browser doesn''t\n       jump back to an anchor between tiles.\n     - `reliableScrollTo()`: tries `window.scrollTo({instant})`,\n       then `documentElement.scrollTop=`, then `scrollingElement.scrollTop=`,\n       covering the common SPA / overflow-hidden-body / custom-root\n       scroll-container variants.\n\n   captureFullPage now runs the priming pass before computing tile\n   positions, then merges the post-prime scrollHeight/Width into the\n   metrics used for planning. New `priming` phase shows in the header.\n\n2) Mermaid: LLM put multiple node defs on one line\n   Error pattern `B -- Filter Links | C[Learn] D[Reference] E[Commu...`\n   trips the parser (\"Expecting NEWLINE, got NODE_STRING\"). Added an\n   explicit \"**One statement per line**\" rule with right/wrong examples\n   to MERMAID_RULES, and tightened the edge-label grammar so the model\n   uses one of the two valid forms (`A -- label --> B` or `A -->|label| B`)\n   and not improvised variants like `A -- label| B`.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.4. injected content script API now versioned\n0.3.4 — old pages still attached to v0.3.3 should hard-reload to pick\nup the new API (the `__dom_lens__` object self-replaces on script\nre-injection via Object.defineProperty(writable:true)).","tree":{"sha":"0385264446307106734e6e94c47f6cf792aafb7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/0385264446307106734e6e94c47f6cf792aafb7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/1e6f2f0df50f19f8dcb0b6cbef987ccc627f17f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/1e6f2f0df50f19f8dcb0b6cbef987ccc627f17f5","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDFlNmYyZjBkZjUwZjE5ZjhkY2IwYjZjYmVmOTg3Y2NjNjI3ZjE3ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/d354df58ce58de3c05b54761e153fb4030159bc4","sha":"d354df58ce58de3c05b54761e153fb4030159bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d354df58ce58de3c05b54761e153fb4030159bc4"}],"sha":"1e6f2f0df50f19f8dcb0b6cbef987ccc627f17f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/1e6f2f0df50f19f8dcb0b6cbef987ccc627f17f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d354df58ce58de3c05b54761e153fb4030159bc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T17:47:21Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T17:47:21Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.3: persistent preset gallery + AI-enhanced stitching\n\nTwo improvements based on real usage:\n\n1) Insights preset gallery now persistent + supports custom prompts\n   The preset buttons used to only appear in the empty state — once you\n   generated a single diagram they vanished, even though you might want\n   to run another preset. They now live in a dedicated \"Run a preset\"\n   section that''s always visible above the diagrams gallery.\n\n   Also: users can add their own. Click \"+ Add custom prompt\" in the\n   Insights tab, fill in name / description / prompt, save. Custom\n   prompts persist via chrome.storage.local (new `customPrompts` field\n   on Settings) and render in a separate \"Your custom prompts\" row\n   below the built-ins. Each custom prompt has a delete (×) affordance\n   on hover.\n\n2) New \"Enhance with AI\" workflow for fixing broken stitches\n   Some pages defeat the v0.3.2 hide-fixed mitigation — JS-driven\n   floating bars, sticky elements that aren''t actually\n   position:sticky, etc. — and produce stitched images with\n   duplicated bands. Rather than keep adding heuristics, we now offer\n   an opt-in LLM-assisted re-stitch.\n\n   How it works:\n     a) The naive stitcher''s raw viewport tiles are now kept on the\n        store (lib/snapshot/fullPage.ts now returns RawTile[]).\n     b) A new \"✨ Enhance with AI\" button appears next to the\n        Screenshot section''s download link. Disabled unless a local\n        LLM is configured AND there are 2+ tiles.\n     c) On click, the panel sends the tiles + per-tile pixel\n        dimensions to the local model with a strict-JSON prompt\n        asking for `{ tiles: [{ index, trimTop }] }` — how many pixels\n        at the top of each tile duplicate the previous tile.\n     d) The response is parsed (json fence or bare) and applied: we\n        re-stitch by cropping each tile''s top by the requested amount\n        and stacking without gaps.\n     e) The corrected image replaces the screenshot. The flow surface\n        progress / errors inline above the image.\n\n   New plumbing:\n     - lib/snapshot/enhanceStitch.ts — buildEnhanceStitchPayload,\n       parseEnhanceResponse, restitchWithAdjustments.\n     - lib/bridge/protocol.ts — lm.oneshot / lm.oneshot.result port\n       messages for non-streaming chat round-trips that don''t pollute\n       the Analyze transcript.\n     - background.ts — handles lm.oneshot, accumulates the stream,\n       replies once with the full text.\n     - entrypoints/panel/enhanceFlow.ts — orchestrator (similar shape\n       to captureFlow).\n     - Store gains rawTiles + enhanceStatus/Message/Error slots.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.3.","tree":{"sha":"09603c740d46dcce7dac4c3b92a17556442e808e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/09603c740d46dcce7dac4c3b92a17556442e808e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/d354df58ce58de3c05b54761e153fb4030159bc4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/d354df58ce58de3c05b54761e153fb4030159bc4","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGQzNTRkZjU4Y2U1OGRlM2MwNWI1NDc2MWUxNTNmYjQwMzAxNTliYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/9eaba1e7ae704902d9e6775e21b9d3982e0acffb","sha":"9eaba1e7ae704902d9e6775e21b9d3982e0acffb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/9eaba1e7ae704902d9e6775e21b9d3982e0acffb"}],"sha":"d354df58ce58de3c05b54761e153fb4030159bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/d354df58ce58de3c05b54761e153fb4030159bc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/9eaba1e7ae704902d9e6775e21b9d3982e0acffb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T17:16:40Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T17:16:40Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.2: fix stitch dupes, defer mermaid render, tighten prompt rules\n\nThree follow-ups to v0.3.1 from real-world testing:\n\n1) Stitching produced duplicate content on bank.gov.ua and similar\n   The page either had position:fixed/sticky headers re-captured at every\n   viewport offset, or used an inner scroll container (window.scrollTo\n   silently no-ops). Both produce the same artifact: N copies of the\n   same content stacked vertically in the stitched output.\n\n   Added three MAIN-world APIs in the content script:\n     - beginFullPageCapture() — walks the DOM and sets `visibility:\n       hidden !important` on every position:fixed / position:sticky\n       element. Returns the count.\n     - endFullPageCapture() — restores prior visibility, idempotent.\n     - getScrollPosition() — reads window.scrollX/Y so we can verify\n       a scrollTo() actually landed.\n\n   captureFullPage() now:\n     - Hides fixed/sticky elements after the first tile (tile 1 is the\n       only one where these elements legitimately appear in the stitched\n       output).\n     - Verifies scroll progress: if scrollTo(0, y) doesn''t advance\n       scrollY by >30px on tile 2+, aborts with a clear error\n       (\"page likely uses an inner scroller\") instead of producing a\n       broken stitched image.\n     - Always restores fixed/sticky on the finally path.\n\n   Confirmed against research from GoFullPage / Full Page Capture /\n   Capture Full Page — this is the standard scroll-and-stitch\n   mitigation. Pages with truly internal scroll containers (rare in\n   modern apps but common on bank/gov sites) now get a user-readable\n   error rather than a broken screenshot.\n\n2) Mermaid showed parse errors mid-stream\n   Even with the debounce + previous-SVG-while-rendering fixes from\n   v0.3.1, when react-markdown encountered a partial fenced block it\n   would still pass mid-token content to MermaidBlock once the closing\n   fence landed but other tokens were still arriving. The parser\n   would fail with \"Lexer error\" / \"Expecting EOF\" on incomplete\n   syntax.\n\n   MarkdownRenderer now accepts a `streaming` prop and forwards it to\n   MermaidBlock. While streaming is true, MermaidBlock shows\n   \"Receiving diagram tokens…\" and refuses to attempt parsing — no\n   more flicker of red error boxes between successful renders. Once\n   the parent reply finishes streaming, the normal debounce + parse\n   path takes over.\n\n3) LLM-generated mermaid often emitted unsupported syntax\n   The error log showed classic LLM-mermaid failure modes: smart\n   quotes, emoji, em-dashes, cross-diagram-type syntax. Per research\n   into mermaid-js/mermaid#46, #18 and GenAIScript''s \"Mermaids\n   Unbroken\" writeup, the fix is strict prompt guidance up front\n   rather than retry loops.\n\n   Added MERMAID_RULES — a single block appended to every diagram-\n   emitting preset that pins down:\n     - Allowed diagram types (one per fenced block, no mixing).\n     - ASCII only (no emoji, no smart quotes, no em-dashes).\n     - Node ID regex ([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*).\n     - How to wrap labels with spaces/punctuation.\n     - No theme/style directives (we already theme via init).\n     - Pie/flowchart/sequenceDiagram-specific edge cases.\n     - 50-node soft cap.\n\n   Also tightened the default systemPrompt with a short summary of\n   the rules so freeform questions (not just presets) benefit.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.2.","tree":{"sha":"cd59e2fef0dc300600574b2e2e0cf91c341cba61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/cd59e2fef0dc300600574b2e2e0cf91c341cba61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/9eaba1e7ae704902d9e6775e21b9d3982e0acffb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/9eaba1e7ae704902d9e6775e21b9d3982e0acffb","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDllYWJhMWU3YWU3MDQ5MDJkOWU2Nzc1ZTIxYjlkMzk4MmUwYWNmZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/1fafe8747a85bcc883b13d527d34605c3d994b13","sha":"1fafe8747a85bcc883b13d527d34605c3d994b13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/1fafe8747a85bcc883b13d527d34605c3d994b13"}],"sha":"9eaba1e7ae704902d9e6775e21b9d3982e0acffb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/9eaba1e7ae704902d9e6775e21b9d3982e0acffb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/1fafe8747a85bcc883b13d527d34605c3d994b13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T08:40:18Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T08:40:18Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.1: page-side module inventory, flicker-free mermaid, Insights dashboard\n\nThree follow-ups to v0.3.0 based on real-world feedback:\n\n1) Modules tab was missing most of the page\n   `chrome.devtools.network.onRequestFinished` only fires while the\n   panel is open, so the initial bundle and any chunks loaded before\n   DevTools attached never appeared in our network feed. Added a\n   MAIN-world inventory via `performance.getEntriesByType(''resource'')`\n   plus declared <script src> / <link rel=…> as a fallback for pages\n   that clear resource timings. `classifyEntries` now takes a second\n   `pageResources` argument and merges them — devtools entries win\n   when both feeds see the same URL (richer mime + size from the\n   actual response).\n\n2) Mermaid flickered during streaming\n   Re-rendered on every chat delta, blanking the SVG between renders.\n   `MermaidBlock` now:\n     - Debounces source changes (400ms default) so streaming deltas\n       don''t trigger a render storm.\n     - Holds the previously rendered SVG visible while a new render\n       is in flight — last-write-wins via a render token.\n     - Skips obviously incomplete source (unbalanced quotes, dangling\n       arrow/bracket on the last non-blank line) so we don''t churn\n       through guaranteed-fail parses mid-stream.\n     - Surfaces \"updating…\" and \"previous render shown\" hints when\n       the new content fails to parse.\n\n3) Diagrams tab was dead weight pre-analysis\n   Replaced it with an \"Insights\" dashboard that''s useful immediately\n   after a capture:\n     - Architecture summary cards (tech stack chips, modules-by-kind\n       bar chart, federation host/remotes) that link into the dedicated\n       Modules/Federation tabs.\n     - Generated-diagrams gallery — every ```mermaid block extracted\n       from chat replies, grouped by reply number.\n     - Empty-state CTA buttons that pre-fill the Analyze composer with\n       the matching preset prompt and switch tabs. Wired through a\n       new `pendingPrompt` slot in the store that AnalyzeTab consumes\n       on mount.\n     - Collapsible scratchpad below for editing diagrams by hand.\n\nVersion bumped to 0.3.1 across package.json, injected content script,\nand panel header.","tree":{"sha":"bcd0f60f714ab97c618dd8ff56dc9dfd12410672","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/bcd0f60f714ab97c618dd8ff56dc9dfd12410672"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/1fafe8747a85bcc883b13d527d34605c3d994b13","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/1fafe8747a85bcc883b13d527d34605c3d994b13","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDFmYWZlODc0N2E4NWJjYzg4M2IxM2Q1MjdkMzQ2MDVjM2Q5OTRiMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/40d3bcb6eb497ac274ac1a43b0e1fcf5ffe272e9","sha":"40d3bcb6eb497ac274ac1a43b0e1fcf5ffe272e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/40d3bcb6eb497ac274ac1a43b0e1fcf5ffe272e9"}],"sha":"1fafe8747a85bcc883b13d527d34605c3d994b13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/1fafe8747a85bcc883b13d527d34605c3d994b13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/40d3bcb6eb497ac274ac1a43b0e1fcf5ffe272e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T08:07:00Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T08:07:00Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"v0.3.0: bundle analyzer + auto-rendered Mermaid diagrams\n\nMaps the page architecture from loaded JS modules and surfaces it\nback as live charts. Two new tabs (Modules, Diagrams) plus prompt\npresets in Analyze that ask the LLM to reply with Mermaid blocks.\n\nModules tab\n- lib/modules/fingerprints.ts: ~50 specs (React/Vue/Angular/Svelte/Solid/\n  Lit/Qwik; Next/Remix/Nuxt/Gatsby/Astro/SvelteKit; Webpack/Vite/Rollup/\n  esbuild/Turbopack/Parcel + Module Federation; Redux/MobX/Zustand/Jotai/\n  Recoil/XState/TanStack/SWR/Apollo; React/TanStack Router; MUI/Antd/\n  Chakra/Radix/Tailwind/Bootstrap; Lodash/Moment/dayjs/date-fns/RxJS/\n  Axios/three/D3; GTM/Segment/Mixpanel/Sentry).\n- lib/modules/detect.ts: MAIN-world probe of window globals + script\n  tags, version read via dot-path. URL evidence from network entries\n  folded in panel-side via mergeUrlEvidence.\n- lib/modules/classify.ts: chunk-kind classifier (main/vendor/runtime/\n  chunk/remoteEntry/manifest/css/sourcemap/image/font/wasm) +\n  framework/bundler/library guess from URL patterns.\n- lib/modules/sourcemap.ts: lazy fetch on click. Resolves\n  sourceMappingURL (incl. inline data: URIs), VLQ-walks mappings via\n  source-map-js to attribute bytes per source, builds folder tree.\n- Background SW: new net.fetch proxy bypasses CORS for sourcemap\n  fetches (panel iframe -> SW <all_urls> host_permissions).\n\nDiagrams tab\n- lib/diagrams/mermaid.ts: strict-security init with dark theme.\n- lib/diagrams/extractMermaid.ts: pulls all fenced mermaid blocks out\n  of the chat transcript.\n- lib/ui/MermaidBlock.tsx: auto-renders to SVG, falls back to source +\n  error on parse failure.\n- MarkdownRenderer intercepts ```mermaid blocks -> MermaidBlock so\n  diagrams render inline in chat too.\n\nAnalyze prompt presets\n- Page overview, Component architecture, Module Federation map,\n  Bundle breakdown, Data flow & state, Risk review.\n- Each preset asks for Mermaid output so diagrams show up in the\n  Diagrams tab.\n\nPlumbing\n- Snapshot.modules + PartialSnapshot.techStack on types.\n- captureFlow classifies network entries + merges URL evidence into\n  the in-page tech-stack detection.\n- App.tsx: net.fetch waiter map mirrors the existing tile-capture\n  pattern; fetchText prop passed to ModulesTab.\n- Version bumped to 0.3.0 in package.json, injected.content.ts, App.tsx.","tree":{"sha":"4289eac1193b035accaac250c479886e302593dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/4289eac1193b035accaac250c479886e302593dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/40d3bcb6eb497ac274ac1a43b0e1fcf5ffe272e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/40d3bcb6eb497ac274ac1a43b0e1fcf5ffe272e9","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDQwZDNiY2I2ZWI0OTdhYzI3NGFjMWE0M2IwZTFmY2Y1ZmZlMjcyZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/5f894bdcd21d5a4401e29807645b1f0c56640724","sha":"5f894bdcd21d5a4401e29807645b1f0c56640724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/5f894bdcd21d5a4401e29807645b1f0c56640724"}],"sha":"40d3bcb6eb497ac274ac1a43b0e1fcf5ffe272e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/40d3bcb6eb497ac274ac1a43b0e1fcf5ffe272e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/5f894bdcd21d5a4401e29807645b1f0c56640724/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T06:36:12Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T06:36:12Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"bump main-world API + panel version to 0.2.1\n\nThe version string had been \"0.2.0\" across three substantive\nbehavioral changes (hook-shim removal, screenshot throttle,\ncross-origin guard), making `__dom_lens__.version` useless as a\n\"do I have the latest content script?\" check.\n\nBumping to 0.2.1 so users can verify the cross-origin TurboTax\nfix is actually installed: window.__dom_lens__.version must now\nread \"0.2.1\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d277d553acc81011c69e76fefadfa02c840d4602","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/d277d553acc81011c69e76fefadfa02c840d4602"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/5f894bdcd21d5a4401e29807645b1f0c56640724","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/5f894bdcd21d5a4401e29807645b1f0c56640724","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDVmODk0YmRjZDIxZDVhNDQwMWUyOTgwNzY0NWIxZjBjNTY2NDA3MjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/94dbff06d08b35180079d29c3ea963a715dc6647","sha":"94dbff06d08b35180079d29c3ea963a715dc6647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/94dbff06d08b35180079d29c3ea963a715dc6647"}],"sha":"5f894bdcd21d5a4401e29807645b1f0c56640724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/5f894bdcd21d5a4401e29807645b1f0c56640724"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/94dbff06d08b35180079d29c3ea963a715dc6647/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T06:24:42Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T06:24:42Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"guard federation detection against cross-origin frame errors\n\nOn sites with named iframes (e.g. turbotax.intuit.com), iterating\nObject.keys(window) returns the iframe''s name as a property, and\nwindow[name] is the iframe''s cross-origin contentWindow. Touching\n.get/.init on that throws:\n\n  Failed to read a named property ''get'' from ''Window'': Blocked a frame\n  with origin \"https://turbotax.intuit.com\" from accessing a cross-\n  origin frame.\n\nThis was killing the whole snapshot pipeline because the error\npropagated out of the inspectedWindow.eval call.\n\nFixes:\n- Collect all iframe/frame names up front and skip those keys.\n- isSafeContainerCandidate rejects Window-like objects by checking\n  `val.self === val` (the Window self-reference invariant) inside a\n  try/catch so cross-origin throws are swallowed cleanly.\n- Wrap every window-property read (Object.keys, w[key], val.get/init,\n  val.moduleMap, etc.) in try/catch.\n- Top-level detectFederation wraps detectFederationInternal so any\n  unexpected throw downgrades to a benign \"unknown\" result with a\n  detect_error signal, never crashing capture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5fe396f42a7b32a3ca530218bc2f1f2fe43ce68d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/5fe396f42a7b32a3ca530218bc2f1f2fe43ce68d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/94dbff06d08b35180079d29c3ea963a715dc6647","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/94dbff06d08b35180079d29c3ea963a715dc6647","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDk0ZGJmZjA2ZDA4YjM1MTgwMDc5ZDI5YzNlYTk2M2E3MTVkYzY2NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/3bdff423eadafad702caa1fd83468003f4622554","sha":"3bdff423eadafad702caa1fd83468003f4622554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/3bdff423eadafad702caa1fd83468003f4622554"}],"sha":"94dbff06d08b35180079d29c3ea963a715dc6647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/94dbff06d08b35180079d29c3ea963a715dc6647"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/3bdff423eadafad702caa1fd83468003f4622554/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T06:11:57Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T06:11:57Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"add examples/mf-demo: webpack 5 host + remote for Federation validation\n\nA self-contained Module Federation demo in a pnpm workspace, so the\nFederation tab has a known-good target.\n\n- host (port 3001): consumes remote_app/Widget and remote_app/Counter\n  via React.lazy + ModuleFederationPlugin. Shares react & react-dom as\n  singletons.\n- remote (port 3002): exposes ./Widget and ./Counter through\n  remoteEntry.js. Also renders a standalone preview at / so you can\n  visit the remote directly.\n- top-level: concurrently script (pnpm dev) starts both with one\n  command, kills both on failure.\n\nHits every webpack5 signal lib/federation/detect.ts cares about:\n__webpack_share_scopes__, __webpack_require__.S, container globals\nwith .get/.init, and the runtime <script src=remoteEntry.js> tag.\n\nREADME walks through install / run / what to expect in the DOM Lens\nFederation tab and what to extend (multi-remote, Vite plugin\nfederation, Native Federation).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73415adc2b4e142267355dbb75b00e9c5e1d32fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/73415adc2b4e142267355dbb75b00e9c5e1d32fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/3bdff423eadafad702caa1fd83468003f4622554","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/3bdff423eadafad702caa1fd83468003f4622554","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDNiZGZmNDIzZWFkYWZhZDcwMmNhYTFmZDgzNDY4MDAzZjQ2MjI1NTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/88ac82e6358886a036eec36096d0fe0c75a1b575","sha":"88ac82e6358886a036eec36096d0fe0c75a1b575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/88ac82e6358886a036eec36096d0fe0c75a1b575"}],"sha":"3bdff423eadafad702caa1fd83468003f4622554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/3bdff423eadafad702caa1fd83468003f4622554"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/88ac82e6358886a036eec36096d0fe0c75a1b575/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T05:48:36Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T05:48:36Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"fix inline code rendering — distinguish by className not removed `inline` prop\n\nreact-markdown v10 dropped the `inline` boolean from the `code`\ncomponent''s props. My handler still checked `if (inline)`, which is\nalways undefined → false, so single-backtick \\`content\\` got rendered\nin the block-code branch as a full <pre>.\n\nNow:\n- code component checks for `language-` className to decide block vs inline\n- block-code rendering is delegated to a new pre component override\n- inline code keeps its compact amber styling\n- language label is pulled from the inner <code> node''s className\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"42e14c0e4a2e4783f75170048af71f7c6c0a439d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/42e14c0e4a2e4783f75170048af71f7c6c0a439d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/88ac82e6358886a036eec36096d0fe0c75a1b575","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/88ac82e6358886a036eec36096d0fe0c75a1b575","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDg4YWM4MmU2MzU4ODg2YTAzNmVlYzM2MDk2ZDBmZTBjNzVhMWI1NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/93d58f81958fc440de0ca8ed363df4887cacf277","sha":"93d58f81958fc440de0ca8ed363df4887cacf277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/93d58f81958fc440de0ca8ed363df4887cacf277"}],"sha":"88ac82e6358886a036eec36096d0fe0c75a1b575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/88ac82e6358886a036eec36096d0fe0c75a1b575"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/93d58f81958fc440de0ca8ed363df4887cacf277/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T05:39:27Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T05:39:27Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"render markdown in chat + DOM markdown; tree view for raw JSON\n\nThree rendering polish asks from real-world use:\n\n1. Analyze tab — chat turns now render as markdown by default.\n   - New shared lib/ui/MarkdownRenderer (react-markdown + remark-gfm,\n     theme-matched to the dark panel).\n   - Each turn has a per-message \"📝 source / 👁 rendered\" toggle so\n     you can drop back to raw markdown when debugging the model''s\n     output. Default: rendered.\n   - Streaming responses continue to update markdown live (parse cost\n     is fine in practice; can throttle later if needed).\n\n2. Analyze tab — input is now a Slack-style markdown editor.\n   - New lib/ui/MarkdownEditor: textarea + compact toolbar\n     (B / I / </> / link / heading / lists / quote / code block),\n     keyboard shortcuts (Cmd+B, Cmd+I, Cmd+E, Cmd+K), and a\n     \"Write / Preview\" tab toggle that swaps the editor for the\n     rendered output.\n   - Cmd+Enter sends.\n\n3. Snapshot tab — DOM markdown and raw JSON both get rich views.\n   - DOM markdown section: Rendered / Source toggle. Rendered by\n     default. Memoized.\n   - Raw JSON section: replaces <pre> with new lib/ui/JsonViewer.\n     - Tree view (@uiw/react-json-view, vscodeTheme): expandable,\n       copyable, collapsed to depth 2 by default.\n     - Text view: plain JSON pretty-print.\n     - Elides dataUrl/markdown/html keys when their value is huge so\n       the tree stays usable on big snapshots.\n\nBundle size went from 538 KB → 738 KB (mostly react-markdown +\nremark stack + json-view). Still well under typical extension limits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"40f8cee9c4d1e36220b83f89cd12269f8e787b81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/40f8cee9c4d1e36220b83f89cd12269f8e787b81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/93d58f81958fc440de0ca8ed363df4887cacf277","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/93d58f81958fc440de0ca8ed363df4887cacf277","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDkzZDU4ZjgxOTU4ZmM0NDBkZTBjYThlZDM2M2RmNDg4N2NhY2YyNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/c43cadfc6ae01063321656be640c0cef9e371f87","sha":"c43cadfc6ae01063321656be640c0cef9e371f87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c43cadfc6ae01063321656be640c0cef9e371f87"}],"sha":"93d58f81958fc440de0ca8ed363df4887cacf277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/93d58f81958fc440de0ca8ed363df4887cacf277"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c43cadfc6ae01063321656be640c0cef9e371f87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:58:10Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:58:10Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"component tree navigation polish + overlay cleanup on close\n\nTwo requests after first hands-on with the Components tab:\n\n1. Overlay didn''t disappear when DevTools closed.\n   - App.tsx adds beforeunload/pagehide listeners that call\n     clearHighlight as a best-effort fast path.\n   - Background SW now remembers the inspected tabId per panel port\n     (set on panel.hello) and on port disconnect runs a cleanup script\n     via chrome.scripting.executeScript({world:''MAIN''}) that removes\n     the __dom_lens_highlight__ div. This is the reliable path; the\n     panel-side cleanup may not run if the iframe is killed abruptly.\n\n2. Deep minified prod trees were hard to navigate — single-letter\n   names, lots of provider/wrapper levels between anything visible.\n   - readMetadata captures the host element''s tag + a short content\n     caption (aria-label → title → alt → placeholder → name → direct\n     text → href) during the fiber walk. Stored on ComponentNode as\n     {tag, hint}.\n   - Each tree row now renders the tag as a green chip and the hint\n     as inline italic (\"Sign in\", \"alt: logo.svg\", \"placeholder:\n     Email\", etc).\n   - \"Significant only\" toggle (default ON) prunes the tree to nodes\n     that are worth seeing: have bounds AND (have a real name OR\n     have a content hint OR are host elements). Insignificant\n     wrappers get pruned and their significant descendants reparent\n     to the nearest significant ancestor — hierarchy preserved,\n     depth compressed.\n   - Filter now matches the tag and hint too, so typing \"submit\"\n     finds buttons whose direct text is \"Submit\".\n   - \"Focus subtree →\" button promotes the selected node to be the\n     visible root; a \"← Back to full tree\" breadcrumb restores.\n   - FocusedComponent passes tag/hint through so future overlay\n     labels can use them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b8b78b638b4ec72187721e5a39623706705b75e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/3b8b78b638b4ec72187721e5a39623706705b75e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/c43cadfc6ae01063321656be640c0cef9e371f87","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/c43cadfc6ae01063321656be640c0cef9e371f87","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGM0M2NhZGZjNmFlMDEwNjMzMjE2NTZiZTY0MGMwY2VmOWUzNzFmODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/8d618f0ad8043da10052a10b49a6f1b7914d9443","sha":"8d618f0ad8043da10052a10b49a6f1b7914d9443","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/8d618f0ad8043da10052a10b49a6f1b7914d9443"}],"sha":"c43cadfc6ae01063321656be640c0cef9e371f87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c43cadfc6ae01063321656be640c0cef9e371f87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/8d618f0ad8043da10052a10b49a6f1b7914d9443/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:46:43Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:46:43Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"remove React DevTools hook shim, throttle screenshot, surface errors\n\nThree connected bugfixes after testing on react.dev with the official\nReact DevTools extension installed:\n\n1. \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading ''has'')\" from\n   backendManager.js:registerRenderer was still happening even with the\n   full hook shim — React DevTools'' backend has internal expectations\n   that are hard to reproduce safely. Replaced the shim with a pure\n   DOM scan that reads React''s own __reactContainer$<hash> properties\n   from container elements (works for React 16/17/18/19, no hook\n   needed, can''t conflict with RDT). If RDT is present, we additively\n   read its tracked roots too.\n\n2. The screenshot pipeline was silently failing on long pages because\n   Chrome rate-limits chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab to ~2 calls/sec\n   per window, and our delay was 120ms. Now:\n   - delayMs raised to 600ms between scroll-and-stitch tiles\n   - Background SW retries captureVisibleTab with exponential backoff\n     up to 4 attempts when it rejects\n\n3. setSnapshot was clearing captureError, so users couldn''t see why\n   the screenshot was missing. Preserve captureError when finalizing\n   the snapshot; it''s cleared only when the next capture starts.\n   Also added a console.warn for full-page failures and a clearer\n   fallback-to-viewport message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03bdd5c5bd08b15dc3b446e8d54aaa9d219d81e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/03bdd5c5bd08b15dc3b446e8d54aaa9d219d81e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/8d618f0ad8043da10052a10b49a6f1b7914d9443","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/8d618f0ad8043da10052a10b49a6f1b7914d9443","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDhkNjE4ZjBhZDgwNDNkYTEwMDUyYTEwYjQ5YTZmMWI3OTE0ZDk0NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/7db853282ef11c289cc04748217a3a18a22766fd","sha":"7db853282ef11c289cc04748217a3a18a22766fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/7db853282ef11c289cc04748217a3a18a22766fd"}],"sha":"8d618f0ad8043da10052a10b49a6f1b7914d9443","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/8d618f0ad8043da10052a10b49a6f1b7914d9443"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/7db853282ef11c289cc04748217a3a18a22766fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:39:56Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:39:56Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"make main-world API redefinable + clearer stale-script error\n\nTwo small resilience tweaks after a real-world hit:\n\n1. injected.content.ts: change __dom_lens__ from writable:false to\n   writable:true so a newer main-world script can replace an older one\n   that''s still attached to a long-lived page. (The old definition\n   blocked re-installs, leaving the page with the older API after the\n   extension was updated.)\n\n2. callScrollMetrics: when window.__dom_lens__ exists but is missing\n   scrollMetrics, return a specific error telling the user the page\n   needs to be reloaded because the loaded content script is older\n   than the extension. The previous error (\"scrollMetrics is not a\n   function\") wasn''t actionable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"53e0de60090d4b774047e90f95bf0e6889efd9e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/53e0de60090d4b774047e90f95bf0e6889efd9e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/7db853282ef11c289cc04748217a3a18a22766fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/7db853282ef11c289cc04748217a3a18a22766fd","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDdkYjg1MzI4MmVmMTFjMjg5Y2MwNDc0ODIxN2EzYTE4YTIyNzY2ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/60a07df18736cd1b343a6fe46e5c612fb48fba32","sha":"60a07df18736cd1b343a6fe46e5c612fb48fba32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/60a07df18736cd1b343a6fe46e5c612fb48fba32"}],"sha":"7db853282ef11c289cc04748217a3a18a22766fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/7db853282ef11c289cc04748217a3a18a22766fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/60a07df18736cd1b343a6fe46e5c612fb48fba32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:37:24Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:37:24Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"add full-page screenshot, slicing, component filter & live overlay\n\nTwo enhancement requests:\n\n1. Full-page screenshot + scrollable display + slicing:\n   - Scroll-and-stitch via repeated chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab —\n     no debugger permission, no yellow bar\n   - New lib/snapshot/fullPage.ts orchestrates capture; tiles stitched\n     in panel via canvas at devicePixelRatio\n   - Auto-detects orientation from scrollWidth vs scrollHeight\n   - lib/snapshot/slicer.ts splits the stitched image into N tiles in\n     reading order (vertical layout → horizontal strips top→bottom,\n     horizontal → vertical strips left→right), with optional overlap\n     for context continuity\n   - Snapshot tab shows scrollable image (resize handle) + slicing\n     controls (count, orientation override, suggested count)\n   - Analyze tab includes sliced tiles as captioned image_url parts\n   - Settings: fullPageScreenshot, fullPageMaxTiles, defaultSliceCount,\n     sendSlicedTiles\n   - Protocol restructured: BG handles per-tile capture.tile requests;\n     panel orchestrates the full flow itself\n\n2. Component filter + visual hints:\n   - Filter input on Components tab (matches name or kind, prunes\n     branches non-destructively, auto-expands matches)\n   - Fiber walk captures first-host-descendant''s bounding rect in\n     document coordinates → ComponentNode.bounds\n   - Selecting a node: draws an overlay rect on the actual page via\n     new window.__dom_lens__.highlight(rect) API (absolute div, no\n     DOM mutation), AND draws an overlay on the stitched screenshot\n     in the Snapshot tab\n   - Selection panel shows bounds + 📐 indicator on tree rows\n\nBumped main-world API version to 0.2.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"295cb7a68eceee7d01190bdff06647d14559d10b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/295cb7a68eceee7d01190bdff06647d14559d10b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/60a07df18736cd1b343a6fe46e5c612fb48fba32","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/60a07df18736cd1b343a6fe46e5c612fb48fba32","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKDYwYTA3ZGYxODczNmNkMWIzNDNhNmZlNDZlNWM2MTJmYjQ4ZmJhMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/c888b7e81fb1df2b01a1a794e170445280f769d5","sha":"c888b7e81fb1df2b01a1a794e170445280f769d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c888b7e81fb1df2b01a1a794e170445280f769d5"}],"sha":"60a07df18736cd1b343a6fe46e5c612fb48fba32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/60a07df18736cd1b343a6fe46e5c612fb48fba32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c888b7e81fb1df2b01a1a794e170445280f769d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:15:37Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T22:15:37Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"fix devtools page CSP and React DevTools hook conflict\n\nTwo bugs surfaced when loading the extension into Chrome with the\nReact DevTools extension also installed:\n\n1. devtools.html had an inline <script> calling\n   chrome.devtools.panels.create. MV3''s default CSP blocks inline\n   scripts, so the panel never registered.\n\n   Restructured to entrypoints/devtools/index.html +\n   entrypoints/devtools/main.ts (WXT''s folder-based entrypoint\n   pattern). The build emits an external module script reference,\n   which CSP allows.\n\n2. The MAIN-world content script installed a minimal\n   __REACT_DEVTOOLS_GLOBAL_HOOK__ shim at document_start. On pages\n   where DOM Lens loaded before React DevTools, the official backend\n   then crashed in registerRenderer trying to read properties our\n   shim didn''t expose (\"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading\n   ''has'')\").\n\n   Expanded the shim to include rendererInterfaces, helpers,\n   listeners, emit/sub/on/off/once, getFiberRoots, and checkDCE so\n   the React DevTools backend can layer on top of it without\n   crashing. When a hook already exists, we still patch\n   onCommitFiberRoot non-destructively.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af9d2e94474eeb8200c0e66deff5bb96b7840579","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/af9d2e94474eeb8200c0e66deff5bb96b7840579"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/c888b7e81fb1df2b01a1a794e170445280f769d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/c888b7e81fb1df2b01a1a794e170445280f769d5","node_id":"C_kwDOSqmnetoAKGM4ODhiN2U4MWZiMWRmMmIwMWExYTc5NGUxNzA0NDUyODBmNzY5ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commit/e13dd1167290011df5c5d99342feb0d8592259a7","sha":"e13dd1167290011df5c5d99342feb0d8592259a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/e13dd1167290011df5c5d99342feb0d8592259a7"}],"sha":"c888b7e81fb1df2b01a1a794e170445280f769d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/c888b7e81fb1df2b01a1a794e170445280f769d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7908002?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ingscarrero","id":7908002,"login":"ingscarrero","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDgwMDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ingscarrero","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/commits/e13dd1167290011df5c5d99342feb0d8592259a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T18:03:43Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T18:03:43Z","email":"ingscarrero@icloud.com","name":"SergioC"},"message":"Initial commit: DOM Lens Chrome extension v0.1.0\n\nDevTools-panel MV3 extension that captures DOM snapshots, walks React\nfiber trees, maps Module Federation topology, and analyzes pages via\na local OpenAI-compatible AI (LM Studio, Ollama, llama.cpp server).\n\n- WXT + React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind scaffold\n- MAIN-world content script installs React DevTools hook shim and\n  console patcher at document_start\n- Snapshot pipeline: DOM markdown (turndown), screenshot, fiber tree,\n  federation graph, console buffer, network entries\n- Federation detection covers Webpack 5, Vite plugin-federation,\n  Native Federation, and ESM import maps\n- Panel UI: Snapshot, Components (react-arborist), Federation\n  (xyflow), Analyze (streaming SSE chat), Settings\n- Background SW proxies LM Studio calls to bypass CORS\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f173bd7d1a5266b52986a87f0d68779e0818a1a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/trees/f173bd7d1a5266b52986a87f0d68779e0818a1a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ingscarrero/dom-lens/git/commits/e13dd1167290011df5c5d99342feb0d8592259