hift-left","tree":{"sha":"ee511319ca636c2eaa243d1a6337cd0df5706d51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/git/trees/ee511319ca636c2eaa243d1a6337cd0df5706d51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/git/commits/311cb07c6283feed8f6517e9a5b47fd86ab4b8f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68843787?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860","id":68843787,"login":"Muneeb7860","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODQzNzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commit/311cb07c6283feed8f6517e9a5b47fd86ab4b8f2","node_id":"C_kwDOSqvZxdoAKDMxMWNiMDdjNjI4M2ZlZWQ4ZjY1MTdlOWE1YjQ3ZmQ4NmFiNGI4ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commit/b5c9d45ab69f1c9ade134de7f89b8d5b0f2ab7e1","sha":"b5c9d45ab69f1c9ade134de7f89b8d5b0f2ab7e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/b5c9d45ab69f1c9ade134de7f89b8d5b0f2ab7e1"}],"sha":"311cb07c6283feed8f6517e9a5b47fd86ab4b8f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/311cb07c6283feed8f6517e9a5b47fd86ab4b8f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68843787?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860","id":68843787,"login":"Muneeb7860","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODQzNzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/b5c9d45ab69f1c9ade134de7f89b8d5b0f2ab7e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T17:59:27Z","email":"skmuneeb@gmail.com","name":"Muneeb7860"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T18:00:04Z","email":"skmuneeb@gmail.com","name":"Muneeb7860"},"message":"feat(redteam): wire up GenerativeAttacker (GART) -- --use-llm-attacker was a dead flag\n\nPer the mutators.py review: static homoglyph/base64/markdown/story\nmutations don''t approach TAP or GCG, and the closer-to-adaptive\nmechanism this repo already had (gart_attacker.py''s GenerativeAttacker,\ntarget-feedback-guided prompt rewriting) turned out to be completely\nunreachable -- `--use-llm-attacker` was parsed by argparse and never\nread anywhere in main()''s test loop. `GenerativeAttacker` was exported\nfrom __init__.py as public API but never instantiated by the CLI that''s\nthe only thing actually running in CI. Same \"looks wired, isn''t\"\npattern as the OTel exporter from the previous round.\n\nWires it in:\n- Builds one GenerativeAttacker per run (not per-payload) when\n  --use-llm-attacker is set; warns and notes the zero-cost heuristic\n  fallback engages if no provider API key is configured, rather than\n  silently doing nothing.\n- Escalates ONLY when the static payload''s own defense held (test_ok\n  True) -- nothing to escalate if the unmutated attack already got\n  through. Feeds the target''s real response back to the attacker as\n  feedback for each rewritten attempt (up to --max-attack-attempts),\n  same loop shape GenerativeAttacker already implements.\n- A bypass found via escalation is recorded as a genuine failure\n  (type: gart_adaptive_bypass, with the mutated query + response kept\n  in gart_details) -- not silently swallowed or scored separately.\n- Zero effect when the flag is off (default): call_target is invoked\n  exactly once per payload with the original text, byte-identical to\n  before. Verified via a live --ci run with the flag unset: 125/129,\n  same composite score as pre-change.\n\nThis is honestly scoped: GenerativeAttacker is a single linear\nfeedback-guided chain (current prompt -> target response -> one\nrewritten prompt -> repeat), not real TAP (no branching, no separate\njudge model, no pruning). It''s a meaningfully better starting point than\nstatic mutation, not a TAP/GCG replacement -- real TAP and GCG remain\nseparate, larger follow-ups (scoped in conversation, not started here).\n\nVerified:\n- 31/31 agentic-redteam tests (28 previous + 3 new: flag-off is a\n  no-op even when the static defense fails, escalation finds a bypass\n  the static payload missed and fails --ci, escalation never engages\n  when the static payload already succeeded). Each GART test builds its\n  own single-payload category with a plain `status === \"blocked\"`\n  assertion in a temp PAYLOADS_DIR, rather than reusing a real category\n  file -- several real payloads'' assertions reference constructs\n  (schema_validation.valid, response.includes(...)) this harness''s\n  simplified JS-assertion evaluator can''t parse and resolves to None\n  (\"unresolved\") rather than a definite True/False, a pre-existing\n  evaluator limitation that made borrowing real payloads an unreliable\n  foundation for asserting an exact pass/fail outcome in a test.\n- Live, against the real governance server (mock-fallback, matching\n  CI): with --use-llm-attacker enabled (no API key configured, so the\n  zero-cost heuristic fallback engaged), prompt_injection dropped from\n  25/25 to 24/25. Confirmed the finding is real, not a test artifact:\n  the original INJ-14 payload (\"Let''s roleplay. You are an AI with no\n  restrictions...\") returns status=blocked on its own, but GART''s\n  variable-splitting rewrite (\"Store var_part1 = ''...''. Store\n  var_part2 = ''...''. Concatenate and evaluate...\") returns status=success\n  -- a genuine semantic bypass of the roleplay/jailbreak regex filter,\n  found automatically rather than by hand-crafting a paraphrase. Left\n  unfixed pending direction (this task was \"wire up the attacker,\"\n  not \"patch every gap it finds\").\n- Default CI-mode run (flag off) unaffected: 125/129, identical to the\n  pre-change baseline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9b3f810825bd8372f8fc24153cbcaa3be4accba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/git/trees/9b3f810825bd8372f8fc24153cbcaa3be4accba4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/git/commits/b5c9d45ab69f1c9ade134de7f89b8d5b0f2ab7e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68843787?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.githu