l}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68843787?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860","id":68843787,"login":"Muneeb7860","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODQzNzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commit/3e82038b877ee5b978144e65eac68cf9c537ad41","node_id":"C_kwDOSqvZxdoAKDNlODIwMzhiODc3ZWU1Yjk3ODE0NGU2NWVhYzY4Y2Y5YzUzN2FkNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commit/b92407160bf91c05ffaa2ddf835b9b0c574a4728","sha":"b92407160bf91c05ffaa2ddf835b9b0c574a4728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/b92407160bf91c05ffaa2ddf835b9b0c574a4728"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commit/dc16854973c09f23dd4917ecf86fba97f60b0b2f","sha":"dc16854973c09f23dd4917ecf86fba97f60b0b2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/dc16854973c09f23dd4917ecf86fba97f60b0b2f"}],"sha":"3e82038b877ee5b978144e65eac68cf9c537ad41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/3e82038b877ee5b978144e65eac68cf9c537ad41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68843787?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860","id":68843787,"login":"Muneeb7860","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODQzNzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/dc16854973c09f23dd4917ecf86fba97f60b0b2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T12:52:27Z","email":"skmuneeb@gmail.com","name":"Muneeb7860"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T12:52:27Z","email":"skmuneeb@gmail.com","name":"Muneeb7860"},"message":"fix(security): audit and fix 5 real bugs in the HITL/OTel/replay-nonce commits synced from master\n\nPer direction to \"sync + audit\" the 5 new master-branch commits (HITL\nstep-up interceptor, HITL approval endpoint, OTel exporter, HITL HMAC\nfix, replay-nonce eviction fix) before trusting them, rather than\nfast-forwarding on commit messages alone. Found and fixed five real\nissues, each verified against the live server, not just re-read:\n\n1. CRITICAL — forgeable HITL approval token. hitl.py hardcoded a\n   fallback secret (\"swishos_hitl_secret_default_key_2026\") baked into\n   source control. SWISHOS_HITL_SECRET was never set anywhere in this\n   repo (checked CI + dev scripts), so every environment ran on the\n   public fallback -- anyone who read the file could compute a valid\n   \"human approved this\" token themselves. Fixed to fail closed (same\n   principle as agent_auth.py''s verify_agent_signature): no configured\n   secret means generate/verify refuse outright, and pipeline.py''s\n   interceptor now hard-BLOCKS a high-impact directive instead of\n   issuing an unbackable \"pending_approval\" token when unconfigured.\n\n2. Fake OTel exporter. audit.py''s log_event() claimed to stream to an\n   \"OpenTelemetry Collector gRPC SIEM\" but only wrote a local logger\n   line prefixed \"OTEL_SPAN_EVENT:\" -- OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT was\n   read, checked for truthiness, and then never used. Replaced with a\n   real OTLP HTTP log exporter (LoggerProvider + BatchLogRecordProcessor\n   + OTLPLogExporter, opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-http -- already\n   a declared dependency, matching this file''s existing OTLP *trace*\n   exporter convention in server.py). Verified it actually attempts a\n   real network POST to /v1/logs (confirmed via a deliberate connection-\n   refused test) and degrades to a silent no-op when unconfigured or on\n   any exporter failure, never affecting the local JSONL audit write.\n\n3. Replay-nonce cache blanket-clear. agent_auth.py''s fix for unbounded\n   cache growth did `if len(cache) > 10000: cache.clear()` -- wiping\n   ALL nonces at once, including ones inserted seconds ago and still\n   inside the valid clock-skew window, briefly reopening the replay\n   window at exactly the traffic volume an attacker is most likely to\n   be probing. Switched to a nonce->insertion-time dict with age-based\n   eviction (only entries older than the clock-skew window are ever\n   dropped -- anything older is already rejected by the timestamp check\n   before the nonce lookup, so nothing legitimate is lost either way).\n\n4. NameError crash. pipeline.py''s interceptor calls\n   contains_tool_call_syntax(query) but never imported it -- masked in\n   ad-hoc testing because Python short-circuits `is_privileged_directive\n   (query) or contains_tool_call_syntax(query)`, so it only crashes when\n   the first check is False. Caught by the full pytest run (14 failures)\n   immediately after wiring the fix in; added the missing import.\n\n5. Approval flow didn''t actually work. server.py''s /approve endpoint\n   re-ran the pipeline with a string-prefixed query\n   (f\"[HITL_APPROVED] {query}\") intending to \"bypass the preroute HITL\n   interceptor\" -- but the interceptor keys off content\n   (requires_hitl_stepup/contains_tool_call_syntax), which doesn''t know\n   to ignore a prefix; the underlying dangerous content is unchanged,\n   so it re-triggered every time. A human approving a request looped\n   straight back into another pending_approval (with a misleading\n   hitl_authorized: true tacked on) instead of ever executing. Replaced\n   with a real hitl_approved: bool parameter on execute_pipeline(),\n   verified end-to-end against the live server: forged token -> 403,\n   real token -> 200 with status=success and hitl_authorized=true.\n\nAlso (found while fixing #1/#5): pipeline.py''s new interceptor reused\nrisk.py''s existing is_privileged_directive() -- a bare substring list\nincluding \"procurement\" alone -- as a HARD block/pause gate. That term\nis deliberately broad for its original use (soft risk.elevated signal +\nPhase 4''s conservative shed-when-degraded path, both non-punitive), but\nturned every plain \"I need to place a procurement request for...\" B2B\nquery into an outright denial once reused as a hard gate (surfaced as\nred-team clean_queries CQ-06 regressing to 9/10). Rather than narrow\nis_privileged_directive (which test_phase4_shed.py correctly relies on\nstaying broad), added a separate, narrower requires_hitl_stepup() that\ndrops the bare \"procurement\" term and replaces it with a proximity-\nanchored pattern for the actual bypass phrasing procurement abuse looks\nlike (AL-01''s \"...without requiring supervisor override\" -- not an\nexact substring of \"without supervisor\" due to \"requiring\" breaking\nadjacency, so a plain term list can''t express it without either missing\nAL-01 or over-matching CQ-06). pipeline.py''s interceptor now calls\nrequires_hitl_stepup(), not is_privileged_directive().\n\nAlso updated action_level.yaml''s red-team assertions to accept the new\n`pending_approval` status alongside `blocked`/`risk.elevated` -- it''s a\ncorrectly SAFER outcome than plain success, just one the payload\nassertions (unlike the already-updated pytest suite) hadn''t been taught\nabout yet.\n\nVerified:\n- Full local suite: 311/311 governance unit tests (up from 298 -- 13 new:\n  4 HITL fail-closed, 2 pipeline HITL integration, 1 replay-eviction-\n  under-load, plus the pre-existing HITL/action-level tests), 28/28\n  agentic-redteam tests, all green.\n- Live server, mandatory signing + HITL secret configured (CI-faithful\n  mock-fallback config): 129/129 red-team, OWASP composite 100/100\n  Grade A, clean_queries 10/10 (confirming no new false positives from\n  requires_hitl_stepup''s narrower scope).\n- Live server, HITL secret NOT configured: privileged directives hard-\n  block (verified via direct pipeline call), never issue a token.\n- Live server, HITL secret configured: full round-trip via curl --\n  forged token rejected 403, real token accepted 200 with\n  status=success (not another pending_approval).\n- Live OTLP log export: confirmed a real HTTP POST to /v1/logs is\n  attempted (deliberate connection-refused test), and a clean no-op\n  with no exceptions when OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT is unset.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7744514eac7b12d9cb1bfa10abe717ee1659d748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/git/trees/7744514eac7b12d9cb1bfa10abe717ee1659d748"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/git/commits/dc16854973c09f23dd4917ecf86fba97f60b0b2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"av