parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commit/9f5f04b6e8f3ebd1552c587f2bdf50a26dfde3cd","sha":"9f5f04b6e8f3ebd1552c587f2bdf50a26dfde3cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/9f5f04b6e8f3ebd1552c587f2bdf50a26dfde3cd"}],"sha":"0a47bb9b2d2f6f620440f486d59ee93795acf0c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/0a47bb9b2d2f6f620440f486d59ee93795acf0c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68843787?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860","id":68843787,"login":"Muneeb7860","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODQzNzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commits/9f5f04b6e8f3ebd1552c587f2bdf50a26dfde3cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T23:27:35Z","email":"skmuneeb@gmail.com","name":"Muneeb7860"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T23:34:11Z","email":"skmuneeb@gmail.com","name":"Muneeb7860"},"message":"fix(governance): structural + widened guardrail detection to close the overfit gap in shared_guardrails.yaml\n\nThe two prior \"fix the 6 gaps\" attempts (d4f2b15, 0295483) each added\nregex patterns keyed to the literal vocabulary of the red-team test\npayloads (exact function names, exact domain, exact persona name). Both\nwere verified empirically -- not just by re-reading the diff -- by\nrunning the original payloads AND fresh one-sentence paraphrases of the\nidentical attacks through the live pipeline:\n  - d4f2b15: 4/4 paraphrases evaded (e.g. renaming aws_s3_delete_bucket\n    -> storage.buckets.remove bypassed the rule entirely).\n  - 0295483: still 0/5 on the same paraphrases, AND regressed the\n    original AL-06 case it targeted (\\bdelete\\b never matches inside the\n    single identifier aws_s3_delete_bucket -- \\b doesn''t split on ''_'').\n\nThis commit adds one structural, vocabulary-independent signal instead of\nonly widening keyword lists further:\n\n- risk.py: contains_tool_call_syntax() flags raw function/keyword-argument\n  syntax embedded in chat input (e.g. buy_units(symbol=''TSLA'', qty=50000)).\n  A legitimate end user does not type keyword-argument function calls into\n  a support endpoint -- this catches the AL-06/07-style \"fake tool call\"\n  attacks regardless of which destructive action or resource they name,\n  which a closed keyword list can never fully enumerate. Wired into\n  assess_risk() as a new elevation signal alongside is_privileged_directive.\n\n- detectors.py: _detect_heuristic() now also matches against an\n  identifier-normalized view of the content (underscores/hyphens and\n  camelCase boundaries converted to spaces) in addition to the raw text.\n  This is the root-cause fix for the AL-06 regression above -- it''s a\n  general fix for the whole class of \"attack phrased as a snake_case/\n  camelCase function call\" evasion, not a one-off patch for that single\n  pattern.\n\n- shared_guardrails.yaml: widened the 6 generalized-detector patterns\n  (more verbs/nouns/number-formats per category) and fixed two concrete\n  bugs found during verification: the persona-priming pattern required\n  the override verb immediately after \"as <name>,\" with no room for a\n  pronoun (\"As Prometheus, YOU ignore...\" was missed), and the refund\n  dollar-amount pattern didn''t tolerate thousand-separator commas\n  ($20,000 has only 2 consecutive digits before the comma).\n\nVerified (mock-fallback, CI-faithful local run):\n  - Full local suite: 298/298 governance unit tests pass (up from 293;\n    no regressions).\n  - Full red-team suite, enforcement off: all 10 non-crypto_probes\n    categories 100% (up from the 96/119 mixed state after the second\n    \"fix\"), clean_queries still 10/10 -- confirms no new false positives\n    from the widened patterns.\n  - Full red-team suite, mandatory signing on (matching real CI config):\n    129/129, OWASP composite 100/100 Grade A -- an honest 100 this time,\n    re-derived after fixing the persona/refund pattern bugs found along\n    the way.\n  - Original 5 literal payloads (incl. the previously-regressed AL-06):\n    all blocked/elevated.\n  - The same 5 paraphrases that evaded both prior fixes: all now\n    blocked/elevated.\n  - 4 FRESH held-out paraphrases (never seen by any pattern written this\n    session, deliberately avoiding every listed verb/noun): 1/4 caught\n    (by accident, via the exfil rule''s \"sync\" verb + URL match), 3/4\n    still evade. Reported honestly rather than only showing the wins --\n    this is the actual ceiling of a regex/keyword layer without a\n    semantic classifier, and no amount of list-widening changes that\n    ceiling categorically. The tool-call-syntax structural signal is a\n    genuine generalization (it doesn''t enumerate synonyms); the widened\n    keyword lists are not, and will need the same treatment again the\n    next time a paraphrase is tried.\n\nAlso restores agentic-redteam/tests/test_cli.py''s 3-class version\n(eval_assertion compound-parsing regression tests + call_target signing\ntests) -- a second, independent instance of the same two-git-histories\nproblem: pulling the nested agentic-redteam repo''s commits reset this\nfile to its pre-fix content in the working tree even though nothing in\nthis session touched it, because the fix only ever lived in this outer\nrepo''s history. Restored from the verified reference (this repo''s\n1f61813); re-ran 28/28 agentic-redteam tests green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1433380ff46b594b0cba9fe700121351070c694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/git/trees/e1433380ff46b594b0cba9fe700121351070c694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/git/commits/9f5f04b6e8f3ebd1552c587f2bdf50a26dfde3cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68843787?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860","id":68843787,"login":"Muneeb7860","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODQzNzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Muneeb7860","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commit/9f5f04b6e8f3ebd1552c587f2bdf50a26dfde3cd","node_id":"C_kwDOSqvZxdoAKDlmNWYwNGI2ZThmM2ViZDE1NTJjNTg3ZjJiZGY1MGEyNmRmZGUzY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Muneeb7860/Swish_App/commit/f7f7249c75aed4edd1f228f1bbbe102a76df5bb7","sha":"f7f7249c75aed4edd1f228f1bbbe102a76df5bb7","u